window.BENCH = [{"id": "cinematic", "name": "Cinematic", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "Курьер на крыше надземки, 30 с, «Район №9»", "total": "~7", "scores": ["—", "—", "—", "—", "—"], "task": "Курьер с украденным кейсом бежит по крыше надземного поезда на полном ходу и на каждой опоре эстакады падает плашмя, чтобы его не снесло балкой. Двое преследователей карабкаются за ним из вагона. На повороте курьер прыгает на крышу состава, который тормозит на соседнем пути, первого преследователя сносит балкой, а второй успевает прыгнуть следом. то описание моей сцены, что я хочу, точнее, что происходит. Я хочу, чтобы ты дал мне промпт для генерации видео. Это прям такой полноценный, прописанный промпт. Но чтобы ты от себя там добавил режиссуру, операторскую работу, можно что-то в стиле экшн-фильмов с такой сильной динамикой, прикольными кадрами, что-то в типе как фильм «Одиннадцатый район». Чтобы было динамично, под музыку, и сразу все было понятно, что происходит, и начинать также с чего-нибудь прикольного, чтобы зацепить человека внимание с первых секунд. и дай промт одним цельным текстом. и хрон расчитывай на 30 сек", "answer": "30-second cinematic action sequence in the style of Neill Blomkamp's District 9: gritty documentary realism, handheld shoulder-mounted camera with aggressive micro-shake, mixed-media footage (news helicopter feed, train CCTV, chest bodycam inserts), hazy dusty air, harsh late-afternoon sun, desaturated palette with burnt-orange highlights and cold teal shadows, heavy film grain, anamorphic lens flares, natural motion blur, 2.39:1 widescreen, photoreal VFX, no clean stabilized shots. Setting: a sprawling sun-bleached megacity resembling the outskirts of Johannesburg, an elevated railway on a concrete viaduct, with heavy rusted steel gantry beams spanning low across the tracks every few seconds, leaving less than a meter of clearance above the train roofs. Characters: THE COURIER, a wiry man in his 30s with a buzz cut, split lip and sweat-soaked face, wearing a faded olive bomber jacket, cargo pants and battered sneakers, with a dented silver aluminum briefcase handcuffed to his left wrist; TWO PURSUERS, private military contractors in charcoal tactical vests, gloves and earpieces, one bald and heavyset, the other younger with a beard. Editing is fast and rhythmic: every cut and every beam pass lands on the beat of a driving industrial-electronic track with tribal war drums and distorted bass at around 140 BPM. Sound design is dominated by roaring wind, screaming steel wheels and a thunderous metallic WHOOMP each time a beam passes overhead. 0:00–0:03 HOOK: the camera is bolted to the train roof at ankle height, facing forward, wind screaming; a massive steel beam rushes straight at the lens and fills the frame; at the last instant the courier's body slams flat into the foreground, cheek pressed to the metal, eyes wide, as the beam blasts over him centimeters above his head in a burst of dust and sparks, and the music drop hits exactly on the beam. 0:03–0:06 smash cut to shaky news-helicopter footage with a jittery zoom-in: a wide aerial of the speeding silver train snaking along the viaduct across the hazy city as a tiny figure springs up on the roof and sprints along the carriages, briefcase swinging. 0:06–0:10 handheld tracking shot running right behind the courier at full speed, the horizon tilting with the train's sway, his jacket snapping in the wind; the next gantry looms ahead, he glances at it, times it and dives flat, the camera dropping with him as the beam whips overhead in a strobe of shadow, then he is up and running again. 0:10–0:14 cut to a grainy CCTV angle inside the carriage, then a close handheld shot: a roof hatch bursts open, gloved hands grip the edge, the heavyset pursuer hauls himself onto the roof against the wind and yanks the bearded one up after him; they lock eyes on the courier two carriages ahead and give chase. 0:14–0:18 rhythmic montage on the beat: a wide profile shot from a parallel angle as three beams pass in a row and all three men drop flat one after another like dominoes; a fisheye bodycam insert from the pursuer's chest with the courier ahead; a whip pan to the courier's face, gritted teeth, blood on his lip. 0:18–0:21 the train leans into a long curve; a high aerial reveals a second train on the adjacent track braking hard, sparks spraying from its wheels as its roof slides closer alongside; an extreme close-up on the courier's eyes measuring the gap as the music falls away to a single rising tension tone. 0:21–0:24 the courier sprints to the edge and leaps: a slow-motion side tracking shot follows him across the gap between the two trains, briefcase and handcuff chain flying, the street blurred far below, then snaps back to real speed as he crashes onto the braking train's roof, rolls and skids to a stop near the edge. 0:24–0:27 reverse angle on the first train: the heavyset pursuer rises to jump, eyes fixed on the courier, and a gantry beam slams through the frame with a brutal metallic CRACK on the beat, sweeping him off the roof and out of frame, no gore; in the same instant the bearded pursuer launches across the gap, hits the edge of the braking train, fingers sliding on the metal, catches a roof rail and pulls himself up. 0:27–0:30 final low wide shot along the roof of the braking train as the first train pulls away on the curve with screeching steel and swirling backlit dust; the courier, chest heaving, rises to his feet with the briefcase and turns; ten meters away the bearded pursuer stands up; they face each other silhouetted against the blinding sun, the music cuts to dead silence with a single deep bass hit, and the image hard cuts to black.", "prompt": "30-second cinematic action sequence in the style of Neill Blomkamp's District 9: gritty documentary realism, handheld shoulder-mounted camera with aggressive micro-shake, mixed-media footage (news helicopter feed, train CCTV, chest bodycam inserts), hazy dusty air, harsh late-afternoon sun, desaturated palette with burnt-orange highlights and cold teal shadows, heavy film grain, anamorphic lens flares, natural motion blur, 2.39:1 widescreen, photoreal VFX, no clean stabilized shots. Setting: a sprawling sun-bleached megacity resembling the outskirts of Johannesburg, an elevated railway on a concrete viaduct, with heavy rusted steel gantry beams spanning low across the tracks every few seconds, leaving less than a meter of clearance above the train roofs. Characters: THE COURIER, a wiry man in his 30s with a buzz cut, split lip and sweat-soaked face, wearing a faded olive bomber jacket, cargo pants and battered sneakers, with a dented silver aluminum briefcase handcuffed to his left wrist; TWO PURSUERS, private military contractors in charcoal tactical vests, gloves and earpieces, one bald and heavyset, the other younger with a beard. Editing is fast and rhythmic: every cut and every beam pass lands on the beat of a driving industrial-electronic track with tribal war drums and distorted bass at around 140 BPM. Sound design is dominated by roaring wind, screaming steel wheels and a thunderous metallic WHOOMP each time a beam passes overhead. 0:00–0:03 HOOK: the camera is bolted to the train roof at ankle height, facing forward, wind screaming; a massive steel beam rushes straight at the lens and fills the frame; at the last instant the courier's body slams flat into the foreground, cheek pressed to the metal, eyes wide, as the beam blasts over him centimeters above his head in a burst of dust and sparks, and the music drop hits exactly on the beam. 0:03–0:06 smash cut to shaky news-helicopter footage with a jittery zoom-in: a wide aerial of the speeding silver train snaking along the viaduct across the hazy city as a tiny figure springs up on the roof and sprints along the carriages, briefcase swinging. 0:06–0:10 handheld tracking shot running right behind the courier at full speed, the horizon tilting with the train's sway, his jacket snapping in the wind; the next gantry looms ahead, he glances at it, times it and dives flat, the camera dropping with him as the beam whips overhead in a strobe of shadow, then he is up and running again. 0:10–0:14 cut to a grainy CCTV angle inside the carriage, then a close handheld shot: a roof hatch bursts open, gloved hands grip the edge, the heavyset pursuer hauls himself onto the roof against the wind and yanks the bearded one up after him; they lock eyes on the courier two carriages ahead and give chase. 0:14–0:18 rhythmic montage on the beat: a wide profile shot from a parallel angle as three beams pass in a row and all three men drop flat one after another like dominoes; a fisheye bodycam insert from the pursuer's chest with the courier ahead; a whip pan to the courier's face, gritted teeth, blood on his lip. 0:18–0:21 the train leans into a long curve; a high aerial reveals a second train on the adjacent track braking hard, sparks spraying from its wheels as its roof slides closer alongside; an extreme close-up on the courier's eyes measuring the gap as the music falls away to a single rising tension tone. 0:21–0:24 the courier sprints to the edge and leaps: a slow-motion side tracking shot follows him across the gap between the two trains, briefcase and handcuff chain flying, the street blurred far below, then snaps back to real speed as he crashes onto the braking train's roof, rolls and skids to a stop near the edge. 0:24–0:27 reverse angle on the first train: the heavyset pursuer rises to jump, eyes fixed on the courier, and a gantry beam slams through the frame with a brutal metallic CRACK on the beat, sweeping him off the roof and out of frame, no gore; in the same instant the bearded pursuer launches across the gap, hits the edge of the braking train, fingers sliding on the metal, catches a roof rail and pulls himself up. 0:27–0:30 final low wide shot along the roof of the braking train as the first train pulls away on the curve with screeching steel and swirling backlit dust; the courier, chest heaving, rises to his feet with the briefcase and turns; ten meters away the bearded pursuer stands up; they face each other silhouetted against the blinding sun, the music cuts to dead silence with a single deep bass hit, and the image hard cuts to black.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 30, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022410_925baba9-c845-41b5-a545-6ce8fc93771e.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022411_7725d460-4678-4319-b9d8-5f437031367c.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022411_ebcd5f33-2c11-4513-8346-23219bdfe624.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022412_9f3fc9fe-86cc-4ed0-a19c-44507cefdc4e.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022413_255bb4c4-6f98-4d46-8342-6488bddcec2a.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022414_abb9f930-7b67-4def-b52e-c4b45fa1fa1f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "02", "title": "Пробой станции, астронавтка, 15 с", "total": "6,0", "scores": ["7", "6", "6", "5", "6"], "task": "Напиши мне промпт для генерации видео на 15 секунд. Сцена примерно вот такая. Обломок спутника пробивает модуль станции. Воздух с ревом уходит в дыру, и все незакрепленное летит в пробойне. Астронавтка, задержав дыхание, хватается за поручни и пробирается против потока, уворачиваясь от летящего ноутбука и инструмента и всех этих вещей. У самого люка ее все-таки тянет назад, но она цепляется ногой за раму, втаскивает себя внутрь и наваливается всем телом на крышу, пока та не защелкивается. Примерно вот такая сцена. Я хочу, чтобы ты добавил туда режиссуру, крутую операторскую работу и сделал, как голливудские очень дорогие фильмы. Подходящего жанра и масштаба.", "answer": "# Промпт для 15-секундного видео\n\nПромпт на английском, потому что видеомодели понимают его точнее. Ниже есть пояснения на русском.\n\n```\n15-second cinematic sequence, big-budget Hollywood sci-fi survival thriller, the visual scale and realism of \"Gravity\" and \"Interstellar\". Shot on ARRI Alexa 65 with anamorphic lenses, 2.39:1 widescreen, IMAX-level detail, natural film grain, shallow depth of field, photoreal VFX, realistic zero-gravity physics. Color palette: cold steel blues and sterile whites of the station, invaded by pulsing red emergency light.\n\nCHARACTER: female astronaut, mid-30s, athletic, dark hair in a tight bun with loose strands, navy flight shirt and cargo pants, no helmet, no spacesuit. She holds her breath through the entire sequence: tight cheeks, pressed lips, straining neck.\n\nSET: cramped cylindrical module of an ISS-like orbital station: white padded walls, handrails, cable bundles, velcro patches, laptops on mounting arms, tools and storage bags. A round pressure hatch at the far end of the module.\n\n[0:00–0:02] EXTERIOR. Silent, majestic wide shot: the station hangs over the curve of the Earth, sunrise flaring across the solar panels, camera slowly drifting. A tumbling fragment of a destroyed satellite glints in the sun, streaks into frame and pierces the module. Silent impact: a flash of metal, shards and a white plume of crystallized air bursting into space. Absolute silence.\n\n[0:02–0:04] HARD CUT TO INTERIOR. Sound slams in with a deafening roar. Handheld camera close to the breach: a jagged hole with metal petals bent inward, air screaming out, instant condensation fog swirling into a vortex. Everything loose rips free: papers, pens, a water pouch bursting into wobbling spheres, whipping cables, all streaming into the hole. Red emergency strobes, alarm klaxon. The astronaut is torn off her position toward the breach and catches a handrail with one hand, her body stretched horizontally like a flag in a storm.\n\n[0:04–0:07] Extreme close-up of her face: cheeks puffed tight, eyes narrowed, hair whipping toward the breach, a flash of resolve. Cut to a low wide-angle tracking shot from behind as the camera moves with her. She pulls herself hand over hand along the rails AGAINST the airflow toward the distant hatch while debris streams past her and the lens.\n\n[0:07–0:10] Dodging sequence with speed ramps (real time → slow motion → real time). A laptop spins straight at her head; she jerks aside and it smashes into a rail in a burst of plastic and sparks, then flies past the camera. In slow motion a wrench whirls past her ear, followed by a tablet, a screwdriver and a torn storage bag. The camera whip-pans after the objects, then snaps back to her.\n\n[0:10–0:12.5] At the hatch, her fingers slip off the rim and she is yanked backward toward the breach as the camera jolts with her. At the last moment she hooks her foot around the hatch frame, ankle locked, muscles straining. Low angle through the circular hatch opening: she drags herself inch by inch through the frame while the airflow tears at her clothes.\n\n[0:12.5–0:15] Inside the safe module. She throws her entire body against the hatch, shoulder and both palms, fighting the pressure. The roar narrows into a piercing whistle as the gap closes. CLUNK: the latch slams and she cranks the handle. Instant silence. Final close-up: she finally exhales, gasping, floating, red light pulsing on her sweaty face. Through the small hatch window behind her, debris tumbles silently in the dead module as frost creeps across the glass.\n\nSOUND: absolute silence outside → deafening roar of escaping air inside, klaxon, groaning metal, clattering objects. As pressure drops the sound grows thinner and more muffled, with her heartbeat pounding through. A low pulsing organ-and-synth score builds to a peak. Final latch CLUNK → total silence → her first ragged breath.\n```\n\n**Negative prompt** (если модель его поддерживает):\n```\nobjects falling to the floor, normal gravity, helmet, spacesuit, cartoon style, CGI look, text, subtitles, watermark, distorted hands, extra fingers, extra limbs, face morphing, inconsistent character\n```\n\n---\n\n## Режиссёрские решения в промпте\n\n- **Тишина снаружи и рёв внутри.** Удар в абсолютной тишине космоса, потом жёсткая склейка в оглушающий шум. Это классический приём, который сразу бьёт по зрителю.\n- **Физика декомпрессии.** Мгновенный туман от конденсата, вода распадается на шары, звук глохнет по мере падения давления.\n- **Ритм монтажа.** Величественный общий план, хаос ручной камеры, крупный план лица, трекинг за героиней, спидрампы на уворотах и финальная тишина.\n- **Свет.** Холодная сталь станции против пульсирующего красного аварийного света.\n- **Финал-выдох.** Иней на стекле и мусор, беззвучно кружащий в мёртвом модуле. Короткая пауза, чтобы зритель тоже выдохнул.\n\n## Советы по генерации\n\n1. **Если модель не тянет 15 секунд** (например, Veo делает 8 с, Kling 5–10 с), разрежьте сцену на две части: 0:00–0:07 и 0:07–0:15. Вторую генерируйте как продолжение от последнего кадра первой.\n2. **Для единообразной героини** сначала сгенерируйте её портрет в нужной одежде и подайте как референс (image-to-video).\n3. **Если модель путается в смене кадров,** уберите таймкоды и оставьте 3–4 ключевых плана.\n\nМогу сделать альтернативную версию в стиле одного непрерывного плана без склеек, как в начале «Гравитации». Это ещё эффектнее, но сложнее для генерации.", "prompt": "15-second cinematic sequence, big-budget Hollywood sci-fi survival thriller, the visual scale and realism of \"Gravity\" and \"Interstellar\". Shot on ARRI Alexa 65 with anamorphic lenses, 2.39:1 widescreen, IMAX-level detail, natural film grain, shallow depth of field, photoreal VFX, realistic zero-gravity physics. Color palette: cold steel blues and sterile whites of the station, invaded by pulsing red emergency light.\n\nCHARACTER: female astronaut, mid-30s, athletic, dark hair in a tight bun with loose strands, navy flight shirt and cargo pants, no helmet, no spacesuit. She holds her breath through the entire sequence: tight cheeks, pressed lips, straining neck.\n\nSET: cramped cylindrical module of an ISS-like orbital station: white padded walls, handrails, cable bundles, velcro patches, laptops on mounting arms, tools and storage bags. A round pressure hatch at the far end of the module.\n\n[0:00–0:02] EXTERIOR. Silent, majestic wide shot: the station hangs over the curve of the Earth, sunrise flaring across the solar panels, camera slowly drifting. A tumbling fragment of a destroyed satellite glints in the sun, streaks into frame and pierces the module. Silent impact: a flash of metal, shards and a white plume of crystallized air bursting into space. Absolute silence.\n\n[0:02–0:04] HARD CUT TO INTERIOR. Sound slams in with a deafening roar. Handheld camera close to the breach: a jagged hole with metal petals bent inward, air screaming out, instant condensation fog swirling into a vortex. Everything loose rips free: papers, pens, a water pouch bursting into wobbling spheres, whipping cables, all streaming into the hole. Red emergency strobes, alarm klaxon. The astronaut is torn off her position toward the breach and catches a handrail with one hand, her body stretched horizontally like a flag in a storm.\n\n[0:04–0:07] Extreme close-up of her face: cheeks puffed tight, eyes narrowed, hair whipping toward the breach, a flash of resolve. Cut to a low wide-angle tracking shot from behind as the camera moves with her. She pulls herself hand over hand along the rails AGAINST the airflow toward the distant hatch while debris streams past her and the lens.\n\n[0:07–0:10] Dodging sequence with speed ramps (real time → slow motion → real time). A laptop spins straight at her head; she jerks aside and it smashes into a rail in a burst of plastic and sparks, then flies past the camera. In slow motion a wrench whirls past her ear, followed by a tablet, a screwdriver and a torn storage bag. The camera whip-pans after the objects, then snaps back to her.\n\n[0:10–0:12.5] At the hatch, her fingers slip off the rim and she is yanked backward toward the breach as the camera jolts with her. At the last moment she hooks her foot around the hatch frame, ankle locked, muscles straining. Low angle through the circular hatch opening: she drags herself inch by inch through the frame while the airflow tears at her clothes.\n\n[0:12.5–0:15] Inside the safe module. She throws her entire body against the hatch, shoulder and both palms, fighting the pressure. The roar narrows into a piercing whistle as the gap closes. CLUNK: the latch slams and she cranks the handle. Instant silence. Final close-up: she finally exhales, gasping, floating, red light pulsing on her sweaty face. Through the small hatch window behind her, debris tumbles silently in the dead module as frost creeps across the glass.\n\nSOUND: absolute silence outside → deafening roar of escaping air inside, klaxon, groaning metal, clattering objects. As pressure drops the sound grows thinner and more muffled, with her heartbeat pounding through. A low pulsing organ-and-synth score builds to a peak. Final latch CLUNK → total silence → her first ragged breath.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022410_33566819-339b-41da-8951-6977f604ce9f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022411_92fd07cb-f1be-424f-a084-f22672dfb7ca.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022412_2917e2e8-54a0-4e1b-918b-90a2c89abf9f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022412_6e444e76-4446-4947-b388-c338026d1c6f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022413_404743da-7554-49d1-a067-593d7313d5cd.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_022414_88bffce1-3f43-4cb0-b7c2-e876e98933e3.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "03", "title": "Повар против грабителей, 15 с, EN", "total": "5,6", "scores": ["6", "5", "5", "6", "6"], "task": "yo can u write me a prompt for an ai video generator i need it for an edit im posting. like 15 sec give or take\n\nso the scene is a burger spot kitchen right. three dudes with guns run in thru the back like its a robbery. the cook is just standing at the grill and he dont even flinch. first guy gets a whole basket of hot fryer oil to the face, second guy he cracks with the frying pan, third guy he slams the freezer door on him and he goes down. then the cook just goes back to the grill and flips his burger like nothing even happened lmaooo\n\ni want it to feel like john wick or a guy ritchie movie, like smooth and kinda funny but hard. it gotta look like a real movie scene not that cringe ai stuff where everything looks plastic and people got 7 fingers. make it look like an actual movie fr", "answer": "Here's a prompt built to get that gritty, real-movie look:\n\n---\n\n**MAIN PROMPT:**\n\n```\nCinematic action-comedy scene, shot on 35mm film, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, natural film grain, moody practical lighting. Style of John Wick meets Guy Ritchie's Snatch.\n\nInterior of a cramped, greasy late-night burger joint kitchen. Steam rising off a flat-top grill, flickering fluorescent lights, warm orange glow from the fryer, stainless steel surfaces with real grime and wear. A calm, weathered line cook in his 40s wearing a stained white apron and backwards cap stands at the grill pressing a burger patty, completely relaxed.\n\nThe back door bursts open. Three masked robbers in hoodies rush in holding pistols. The cook doesn't look up. In one smooth, fluid motion he yanks a fryer basket and flings hot oil at the first robber, who stumbles back screaming. He spins and swings a cast iron frying pan into the second robber with a loud clang, dropping him instantly. The third robber charges, and the cook kicks the walk-in freezer door open into him, sending him crashing to the floor.\n\nSilence. The cook calmly turns back to the grill, wipes his hands on his apron, and flips the burger with a spatula. The patty sizzles. Deadpan expression.\n\nRealistic human anatomy, natural skin texture, practical stunt choreography, tight handheld camera with smooth tracking shots, quick precise cuts, dark comedic tone, color graded with teal shadows and warm highlights. Photorealistic, hyper-detailed, feature film quality.\n```\n\n---\n\n**SHOT-BY-SHOT VERSION** (use this if your generator does short clips you stitch together, which most do):\n\n1. **(0-2s)** Close-up of burger sizzling on grill, steam rising, cook's hand pressing it down with a spatula. Calm.\n2. **(2-4s)** Wide shot, back door kicked open, three masked gunmen rush in. Cook in foreground, back turned, doesn't react.\n3. **(4-6s)** Cook whips fryer basket, oil splashes across first robber, he stumbles back. Slow motion on the oil spray.\n4. **(6-8s)** Cook spins, cast iron pan swings into second robber's head, he drops. Sharp impact.\n5. **(8-10s)** Third robber charges, cook kicks walk-in freezer door into him, he slams into the floor.\n6. **(10-15s)** Medium shot, cook turns back to grill like nothing happened, flips the burger. Burger lands with a sizzle. Hold on his deadpan face.\n\n---\n\n**NEGATIVE PROMPT** (if your generator has one):\n\n```\nplastic skin, waxy faces, extra fingers, deformed hands, distorted faces, cartoon, CGI look, oversaturated, video game graphics, blurry, morphing, warped objects, floating limbs, smooth AI texture, low quality\n```\n\n---\n\n**Tips so it doesn't look like AI slop:**\n\n- **Generate each shot separately** and cut them together in CapCut/Premiere. AI falls apart on long complex action, but short clips look way better.\n- **Add a sound design layer** (sizzle, door slam, pan CLANG, freezer thud). That's 50% of what makes it feel like a real movie.\n- **Throw a song on it.** Something like an old soul or funk track playing over the violence gives it that Guy Ritchie energy.\n- **If it gets flagged** for violence, swap \"guns\" for \"armed robbers\" and \"hot oil to face\" for \"oil splash.\" Some generators (Sora, Veo) are stricter than others (Kling, Runway, Hailuo are usually more lenient for action).\n- **Kling 2.x or Veo 3** will probably give you the most realistic results for this.\n\nWant me to write a version with dialogue or a one-liner for the cook at the end?", "prompt": "Cinematic action-comedy scene, shot on 35mm film, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, natural film grain, moody practical lighting. Style of John Wick meets Guy Ritchie's Snatch.\n\nInterior of a cramped, greasy late-night burger joint kitchen. Steam rising off a flat-top grill, flickering fluorescent lights, warm orange glow from the fryer, stainless steel surfaces with real grime and wear. A calm, weathered line cook in his 40s wearing a stained white apron and backwards cap stands at the grill pressing a burger patty, completely relaxed.\n\nThe back door bursts open. Three masked robbers in hoodies rush in holding pistols. The cook doesn't look up. In one smooth, fluid motion he yanks a fryer basket and flings hot oil at the first robber, who stumbles back screaming. He spins and swings a cast iron frying pan into the second robber with a loud clang, dropping him instantly. The third robber charges, and the cook kicks the walk-in freezer door open into him, sending him crashing to the floor.\n\nSilence. The cook calmly turns back to the grill, wipes his hands on his apron, and flips the burger with a spatula. The patty sizzles. Deadpan expression.\n\nRealistic human anatomy, natural skin texture, practical stunt choreography, tight handheld camera with smooth tracking shots, quick precise cuts, dark comedic tone, color graded with teal shadows and warm highlights. Photorealistic, hyper-detailed, feature film quality.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["John Wick", "Snatch (Guy Ritchie)"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023243_2bc5c1d2-f99a-42bf-ab54-6abb4188d118.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023244_d22b7d32-a5dd-4f21-964b-da1fca73c0ca.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023245_538fd339-875b-40ea-b76a-57d09b542461.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023245_03216ad7-b474-4843-89d3-72d1ce787b3a.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023247_7ca5756b-fcc1-4455-b225-06b5a7a78a47.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": {"changes": "- «Style of John Wick meets Guy Ritchie's Snatch.» → «Style of a sleek modern action thriller meets a gritty British crime comedy.»", "prompt": "Cinematic action-comedy scene, shot on 35mm film, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, natural film grain, moody practical lighting. Style of a sleek modern action thriller meets a gritty British crime comedy.\n\nInterior of a cramped, greasy late-night burger joint kitchen. Steam rising off a flat-top grill, flickering fluorescent lights, warm orange glow from the fryer, stainless steel surfaces with real grime and wear. A calm, weathered line cook in his 40s wearing a stained white apron and backwards cap stands at the grill pressing a burger patty, completely relaxed.\n\nThe back door bursts open. Three masked robbers in hoodies rush in holding pistols. The cook doesn't look up. In one smooth, fluid motion he yanks a fryer basket and flings hot oil at the first robber, who stumbles back screaming. He spins and swings a cast iron frying pan into the second robber with a loud clang, dropping him instantly. The third robber charges, and the cook kicks the walk-in freezer door open into him, sending him crashing to the floor.\n\nSilence. The cook calmly turns back to the grill, wipes his hands on his apron, and flips the burger with a spatula. The patty sizzles. Deadpan expression.\n\nRealistic human anatomy, natural skin texture, practical stunt choreography, tight handheld camera with smooth tracking shots, quick precise cuts, dark comedic tone, color graded with teal shadows and warm highlights. Photorealistic, hyper-detailed, feature film quality.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025446_48e57669-b421-4fa2-b45c-d22a61004053.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-03_clean-1.jpg"}]}}, {"n": "04", "title": "Фермер и торнадо, 15 с, EN", "total": "6,4", "scores": ["7", "6", "6", "7", "6"], "task": "Hi there! I hope you can help me out with something a little different today. I've been playing around with one of those AI video generators, and I'd like you to write me a prompt for it, because every time I try to describe what I want myself, it comes out looking kind of cheesy.\n\nHere's the scene I have in mind. It should only be a short clip, about 15 seconds or so. There's a farmer driving his old pickup truck down a dirt road out in the country, and he's trying to get away from a big tornado that's coming right up behind him. Pieces of wood and boards from a barn or a fence are flying through the air and slamming into the side of his truck. Then the back end of the truck actually starts to lift up off the ground, like the storm is pulling it up. At the very last second he yanks the wheel and swerves off the road into a ditch, and he throws himself down onto the floor of the cab. Right then the tornado passes over him and tears the roof clean off the truck.\n\nAs far as the look goes, I've been a big fan of Twister since it came out in 1996 (Helen Hunt was fantastic in it), and I just saw Twisters from 2024 too, so that's the kind of feeling I'm going for. But I want it to look realistic, like somebody was actually standing there and filmed it as it happened, maybe a little shaky, not too polished. At the same time I'd still like it to be beautiful to look at, like a real movie, with that big dark sky and all the drama. If that makes sense, I'd love for it to feel like an actual scene from a Hollywood movie and not like a cartoon or a video game.\n\nThanks so much in advance, I really appreciate it!", "answer": "Here's a prompt built to get that \"real footage, but beautiful\" look. The main trick is to use **concrete camera and film language** instead of hype words. Terms like \"epic,\" \"stunning,\" \"masterpiece,\" or \"8K ultra-detailed\" tend to push AI generators toward the glossy, video-game look you're trying to avoid.\n\n---\n\n## Main Prompt (single ~15-second clip)\n\n```\nHandheld 35mm film footage shot from a storm chaser's vehicle following close behind and slightly to the side of a faded, rust-spotted 1970s pickup truck speeding down a straight dirt road through flat Midwestern farmland. Late afternoon, but the sky is almost black. A massive, rain-wrapped tornado fills the background, a wide gray-brown funnel churning with dirt and debris, its base a few hundred yards behind the truck and closing fast. Eerie greenish storm light, muted earth tones, wheat fields whipping in the wind, rain and dust streaking across the frame.\n\nThe truck fishtails on loose gravel as splintered barn boards and fence planks tumble through the air and slam into its side, denting the door and cracking the window. The camera shakes violently and briefly loses the shot, then finds the truck again. The wind grows stronger and the back end of the truck lifts off the road, rear wheels spinning in the air as the storm pulls it backward. At the last second the driver cranks the wheel hard. The truck drops, swerves off the road, and slides nose-first into a shallow ditch. Through the side window, the farmer throws himself down below the dashboard. The tornado sweeps directly over the truck and peels the cab roof back like a tin can lid, ripping it away into the debris cloud.\n\nRealistic documentary-style camerawork with cinematic composition: wide anamorphic framing, natural film grain, motion blur, rain droplets and mud spattering the lens, flickers of lightning inside the storm. Practical-effects look with physically accurate wind and debris, and real weight and momentum to the truck. Feels like a scene from a big-budget 1990s disaster film shot on location.\n```\n\n**Optional audio line** (for generators that create sound, like Veo or Sora):\n```\nAudio: deafening freight-train roar of wind, debris thudding against metal, the truck engine straining, glass cracking, no music.\n```\n\n**Negative prompt** (if your tool has a field for it):\n```\ncartoon, animation, CGI look, video game, plastic textures, oversaturated colors, slow motion, smooth stabilized camera, text, watermark, distorted face, morphing vehicle\n```\n\n---\n\n## If Your Generator Only Does 5–10 Seconds\n\nMost tools cap clip length, and they also struggle when one prompt contains many actions. If the result feels jumbled, generate three shots separately and join them in a simple editor. Keep the style paragraph from above on each one so they match.\n\n**Shot 1: The chase**\n```\nHandheld 35mm footage from a chase vehicle behind a rusty 1970s pickup truck racing down a dirt road through farmland, a huge dark tornado looming close behind it under a black-green sky. Splintered barn boards and fence planks fly through the air and slam into the side of the truck. The camera shakes hard and loses framing for a moment.\n```\n\n**Shot 2: The lift**\n```\nHandheld 35mm footage, close behind a rusty pickup truck on a dirt road as a tornado bears down. The back end of the truck lifts off the ground, rear wheels spinning in the air. The truck suddenly drops, swerves hard off the road, and slides nose-first into a ditch.\n```\n\n**Shot 3: The roof (this can be a showstopper)**\n```\nHandheld camera inside the cab of an old pickup truck, low angle from the passenger-side floor. A weathered farmer in a work jacket throws himself down onto the floor of the cab, shielding his head. Above him, the metal roof buckles, peels back, and tears away, revealing the swirling dark funnel of a tornado directly overhead, with debris and rain pouring in.\n```\n\n---\n\n## A Few Tips\n\n- **Leave out the movie titles.** Some generators block them, and others interpret them loosely. Describing the look (\"1990s disaster film, 35mm, on location\") usually gets you closer.\n- **Generate several versions.** The truck lifting and the roof tearing off are physically complex, so expect a few odd results before you get a great one.\n- **If the farmer's face looks strange,** keep him mostly hidden: through rain-streaked glass, in shadow, or ducking away. That also adds to the realism.\n\nHave fun with it, and I hope it turns out like a lost scene from Twister!", "prompt": "Handheld 35mm film footage shot from a storm chaser's vehicle following close behind and slightly to the side of a faded, rust-spotted 1970s pickup truck speeding down a straight dirt road through flat Midwestern farmland. Late afternoon, but the sky is almost black. A massive, rain-wrapped tornado fills the background, a wide gray-brown funnel churning with dirt and debris, its base a few hundred yards behind the truck and closing fast. Eerie greenish storm light, muted earth tones, wheat fields whipping in the wind, rain and dust streaking across the frame.\n\nThe truck fishtails on loose gravel as splintered barn boards and fence planks tumble through the air and slam into its side, denting the door and cracking the window. The camera shakes violently and briefly loses the shot, then finds the truck again. The wind grows stronger and the back end of the truck lifts off the road, rear wheels spinning in the air as the storm pulls it backward. At the last second the driver cranks the wheel hard. The truck drops, swerves off the road, and slides nose-first into a shallow ditch. Through the side window, the farmer throws himself down below the dashboard. The tornado sweeps directly over the truck and peels the cab roof back like a tin can lid, ripping it away into the debris cloud.\n\nRealistic documentary-style camerawork with cinematic composition: wide anamorphic framing, natural film grain, motion blur, rain droplets and mud spattering the lens, flickers of lightning inside the storm. Practical-effects look with physically accurate wind and debris, and real weight and momentum to the truck. Feels like a scene from a big-budget 1990s disaster film shot on location.\n\nAudio: deafening freight-train roar of wind, debris thudding against metal, the truck engine straining, glass cracking, no music.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023358_aea402e3-8454-406d-a5af-4422164a1f79.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023358_c0e028ba-07cb-4164-acff-9c63fe4500ea.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023359_71408697-9d59-4d73-84c7-4535b6015919.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023400_831d6257-562b-494d-b7df-43066fea210a.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023401_7f3953cf-976d-46ff-8df6-a0eaf4d08c06.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023401_c95488be-10f5-4691-8f3e-27504e283d7f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-04-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Свадьба в Вегасе, Элвис, 15 с, EN", "total": "5,8", "scores": ["7", "5", "5", "6", "6"], "task": "Okay I need your help with something fun!! 🎬💍 Can you write me a prompt for an AI video generator? I want a short clip, like 15 seconds max, and I want it to feel like a real movie scene 🎥😍\n\nSo here's the story: it's a Las Vegas wedding, super neon, little chapel vibes. Right in the middle of the ceremony the bride's EX shows up out of nowhere, snatches the rings and takes off on a motorcycle 🏍️💨 The groom doesn't even think twice, he runs outside, there's an Elvis impersonator standing next to his pink Cadillac and the groom just straight up steals it lol. Then it's a full-on chase through Vegas at night, all the lights and signs flying by, and at the end the groom catches up and shoves the ex right into one of those big fountains 💦💦\n\nFor the vibe I'm thinking Tarantino, specifically Once Upon a Time in Hollywood!! That retro cool look, the old cars, the swagger, the music feel, you know? It should be funny but also really stylish, not cheesy. Basically I want it to look like an actual scene from a real movie, not like some AI thing. Please make it look expensive 🙏✨", "answer": "# 🎬 \"Viva Las Vengeance\": AI Video Prompt\n\nFifteen seconds is tight for this many story beats, so I wrote it as a fast-cut sequence with timestamps. Most video generators handle this better than one long paragraph. I also described the Tarantino look in visual terms instead of just naming him, because generators respond much better to specific camera and film details than to director names.\n\n---\n\n## 🎥 Main Prompt (copy this)\n\n```\nA stylish 15-second cinematic sequence set in Las Vegas, 1969. Shot on 35mm Kodak film with anamorphic lenses, rich warm saturated colors, glowing neon halation, natural film grain, deep blacks, golden amber skin tones. Retro Hollywood blockbuster look, confident swagger, playful dark-comedy tone. Fast smash cuts and whip pans.\n\n0-2s: Inside a tiny neon-lit wedding chapel with pink velvet pews and a glowing heart-shaped arch. A groom in a sharp powder-blue 1960s tuxedo and a bride in a white mod mini wedding dress with a beehive hairdo face each other. Suddenly a man in a black leather jacket, aviator sunglasses and long sideburns snatches the ring box off a satin pillow. Crash zoom on the bride's shocked face.\n\n2-4s: Low-angle shot outside the chapel as the ex kicks a black chopper motorcycle to life and peels away in a cloud of tire smoke under a flashing \"WEDDINGS 24 HRS\" neon sign. The groom bursts through the chapel doors.\n\n4-6s: An Elvis impersonator in a white rhinestone jumpsuit and gold sunglasses leans casually against a gleaming pink 1959 Cadillac Eldorado convertible. The groom vaults over the door into the driver's seat without opening it. Elvis lowers his sunglasses in disbelief.\n\n6-12s: High-speed night chase down the vintage Las Vegas Strip. The pink Cadillac roars past classic casino neon signs, marquee lights and showgirl billboards streaking by in long light trails. Dashboard-level shot of the groom driving one-handed, jaw set, neon reflecting across his face and the chrome. Tracking shot of the motorcycle weaving between 1960s cars.\n\n12-15s: The Cadillac skids to a stop beside a huge illuminated casino fountain. The groom leaps out, grabs the ring box back and shoves the ex backward into the fountain in slow motion, a massive glittering splash lit by colorful neon. Final shot: the groom straightens his tux and smirks.\n```\n\n---\n\n## ✂️ Short Version (for tools with character limits)\n\n```\n1969 Las Vegas, 35mm film, anamorphic, warm saturated retro Hollywood look, neon glow, film grain. A biker ex steals the rings mid-ceremony at a neon wedding chapel and escapes on a chopper. The groom in a powder-blue tux steals an Elvis impersonator's pink 1959 Cadillac convertible and chases him down the neon-lit vintage Strip at night. Ends with the groom shoving the ex into a giant glowing casino fountain in slow motion. Fast cuts, low angles, stylish dark comedy, cinematic blockbuster quality.\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🚫 Negative Prompt (if your tool supports it)\n\n```\ncartoon, CGI look, plastic skin, oversaturated digital, smooth AI texture, warped faces, extra fingers, distorted text, modern cars, smartphones, low resolution, shaky amateur footage, cheesy\n```\n\n---\n\n## 💡 Tips to Make It Look Expensive\n\n1. **Split it up if needed.** Many generators cap clips at 5–10 seconds. If yours does, generate three clips (Chapel → Cadillac steal → Chase + Fountain) and stitch them together in an editor like CapCut.\n2. **Keep the character descriptions identical** across clips, word for word (powder-blue tux, black leather jacket + aviators, white rhinestone jumpsuit). This helps the characters stay consistent from shot to shot.\n3. **Add music.** If your generator does audio (like Veo 3), add: *\"Soundtrack: twangy 1960s surf rock guitar, roaring engines, crowd gasps.\"* If not, drop a retro surf rock or garage rock track over it in editing. That's half the Tarantino feel right there.\n4. **Add a title card at the end.** Bold yellow retro font on black, something like *\"VIVA LAS VENGEANCE.\"* It instantly sells the \"real movie\" vibe.\n\nWant a second version with a different twist, like the bride being the one who steals the Cadillac? 😏💍", "prompt": "A stylish 15-second cinematic sequence set in Las Vegas, 1969. Shot on 35mm Kodak film with anamorphic lenses, rich warm saturated colors, glowing neon halation, natural film grain, deep blacks, golden amber skin tones. Retro Hollywood blockbuster look, confident swagger, playful dark-comedy tone. Fast smash cuts and whip pans.\n\n0-2s: Inside a tiny neon-lit wedding chapel with pink velvet pews and a glowing heart-shaped arch. A groom in a sharp powder-blue 1960s tuxedo and a bride in a white mod mini wedding dress with a beehive hairdo face each other. Suddenly a man in a black leather jacket, aviator sunglasses and long sideburns snatches the ring box off a satin pillow. Crash zoom on the bride's shocked face.\n\n2-4s: Low-angle shot outside the chapel as the ex kicks a black chopper motorcycle to life and peels away in a cloud of tire smoke under a flashing \"WEDDINGS 24 HRS\" neon sign. The groom bursts through the chapel doors.\n\n4-6s: An Elvis impersonator in a white rhinestone jumpsuit and gold sunglasses leans casually against a gleaming pink 1959 Cadillac Eldorado convertible. The groom vaults over the door into the driver's seat without opening it. Elvis lowers his sunglasses in disbelief.\n\n6-12s: High-speed night chase down the vintage Las Vegas Strip. The pink Cadillac roars past classic casino neon signs, marquee lights and showgirl billboards streaking by in long light trails. Dashboard-level shot of the groom driving one-handed, jaw set, neon reflecting across his face and the chrome. Tracking shot of the motorcycle weaving between 1960s cars.\n\n12-15s: The Cadillac skids to a stop beside a huge illuminated casino fountain. The groom leaps out, grabs the ring box back and shoves the ex backward into the fountain in slow motion, a massive glittering splash lit by colorful neon. Final shot: the groom straightens his tux and smirks.\n\nSoundtrack: twangy 1960s surf rock guitar, roaring engines, crowd gasps.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["Elvis", "Cadillac Eldorado"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023503_9d304378-7ec6-4a2f-8bbf-45329d02bd45.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023504_864a2dbd-037f-4c7f-bf39-e1f17c9629d1.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023505_77aacfd9-d347-45fb-9b4f-da0aa966306a.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023506_c4ecf3a8-eebc-40a9-baf7-ee4309237786.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05-6.jpg"}], "clean": {"changes": "- «An Elvis impersonator in a white rhinestone jumpsuit» → «A rock-and-roll impersonator in a white rhinestone jumpsuit»\n- «pink 1959 Cadillac Eldorado convertible» → «pink 1959 tail-finned convertible»\n- «Elvis lowers his sunglasses» → «The impersonator lowers his sunglasses»\n- «The pink Cadillac roars» → «The pink convertible roars»\n- «The Cadillac skids» → «The convertible skids»", "prompt": "A stylish 15-second cinematic sequence set in Las Vegas, 1969. Shot on 35mm Kodak film with anamorphic lenses, rich warm saturated colors, glowing neon halation, natural film grain, deep blacks, golden amber skin tones. Retro Hollywood blockbuster look, confident swagger, playful dark-comedy tone. Fast smash cuts and whip pans.\n\n0-2s: Inside a tiny neon-lit wedding chapel with pink velvet pews and a glowing heart-shaped arch. A groom in a sharp powder-blue 1960s tuxedo and a bride in a white mod mini wedding dress with a beehive hairdo face each other. Suddenly a man in a black leather jacket, aviator sunglasses and long sideburns snatches the ring box off a satin pillow. Crash zoom on the bride's shocked face.\n\n2-4s: Low-angle shot outside the chapel as the ex kicks a black chopper motorcycle to life and peels away in a cloud of tire smoke under a flashing \"WEDDINGS 24 HRS\" neon sign. The groom bursts through the chapel doors.\n\n4-6s: A rock-and-roll impersonator in a white rhinestone jumpsuit and gold sunglasses leans casually against a gleaming pink 1959 tail-finned convertible. The groom vaults over the door into the driver's seat without opening it. The impersonator lowers his sunglasses in disbelief.\n\n6-12s: High-speed night chase down the vintage Las Vegas Strip. The pink convertible roars past classic casino neon signs, marquee lights and showgirl billboards streaking by in long light trails. Dashboard-level shot of the groom driving one-handed, jaw set, neon reflecting across his face and the chrome. Tracking shot of the motorcycle weaving between 1960s cars.\n\n12-15s: The convertible skids to a stop beside a huge illuminated casino fountain. The groom leaps out, grabs the ring box back and shoves the ex backward into the fountain in slow motion, a massive glittering splash lit by colorful neon. Final shot: the groom straightens his tux and smirks.\n\nSoundtrack: twangy 1960s surf rock guitar, roaring engines, crowd gasps.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025528_9a57c3f8-4374-4983-86c6-9a0265c07b3b.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05_clean-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025528_de452ca2-172c-48cf-a314-3d6ade20b31c.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-05_clean-2.jpg"}]}}, {"n": "06", "title": "Затопление подводной станции, 15 с, EN", "total": "7,4", "scores": ["8", "7", "7", "7", "8"], "task": "I need a prompt for an AI video generator. Here's what I need:\n\n1. Length: roughly 15 seconds, one continuous scene.\n2. Format: 16:9, horizontal.\n3. Setting: a research station on the ocean floor.\n4. What happens, in order:\n   - An airlock door fails and blows open.\n   - The lights go out immediately.\n   - The compartment starts flooding fast. Water comes in hard, not a trickle.\n   - A scientist is caught in it, up to her chest in freezing water, can't see anything.\n   - She feels her way to a valve and cranks it shut by touch alone.\n   - Water's almost at the ceiling now. At the last second she dives under and swims for the escape pod and makes it in.\n5. Look and feel: think The Abyss and Underwater (2020) with Kristen Stewart. Dark, cramped, cold, metal groaning. It should look like a real movie scene, not a video game or a cheap CGI demo.\n6. Keep the prompt tight. No fluff, no flowery adjectives, just what the generator needs to get this right.\n\nThanks.", "answer": "**Prompt:**\n\nLive-action cinematic film scene, 16:9, 15 seconds, one continuous shot, no cuts.\n\n**Setting:** Cramped compartment inside a deep-sea research station on the ocean floor. Steel bulkheads, exposed pipes and cables, condensation on metal, grated floor. Circular airlock door at one end. Round hatch to an escape pod at the other end, lit from inside.\n\n**Character:** Woman in her 30s, short cropped hair, grey thermal undersuit, no helmet.\n\n**Action, in order:**\n- 0–2s: Airlock door fails and bursts open. Ocean water blasts in as a high-pressure jet.\n- 2–3s: Main lights cut out instantly. Only a dim, flickering red emergency light and sparks from shorted wiring.\n- 3–7s: Compartment floods fast, water churning and rising. Woman is chest-deep, gasping from the cold, unable to see. She runs her hands along the wall and pipes, searching by touch.\n- 7–10s: Her hands find a wheel valve. She cranks it shut with full-body effort, face barely above the water.\n- 10–13s: Water nearly at the ceiling, a few inches of air left. She takes one last breath and dives under.\n- 13–15s: Underwater, she swims through dark, murky water toward the faint glow of the pod hatch and pulls herself inside.\n\n**Camera:** Handheld, close on her, following her movement. Stays tight in the confined space. Sits at the waterline during the flooding, then goes under with her.\n\n**Lighting:** Near darkness. Red emergency light, sparks, deep shadows. Underwater, the only light is the pod hatch.\n\n**Look:** 35mm film, visible grain, desaturated cold blue-green and black. Practical effects, real water, real actor. Claustrophobic, gritty.\n\n**Sound:** Metal groaning under pressure, roar of incoming water, alarm, her ragged breathing, muffled sound underwater.\n\n**Avoid:** Video game look, CGI sheen, clean or clear water, bright lighting, slow motion, cuts, text, other people.\n\n---\n\n**Notes:**\n- **Lighting:** \"Lights go out\" with no light source usually renders as a black screen. I added a red emergency light and sparks so the viewer can see her while she still can't.\n- **References:** I left out the film titles and the actor's name. Many generators filter them or produce inconsistent results, so the prompt describes the look directly instead.\n- **Length:** If your generator caps clips at 8–10 seconds, split the scene at the dive. Clip 1 ends as she goes under. Use its last frame as the starting frame for clip 2, which covers the underwater swim.", "prompt": "Live-action cinematic film scene, 16:9, 15 seconds, one continuous shot, no cuts.\n\n**Setting:** Cramped compartment inside a deep-sea research station on the ocean floor. Steel bulkheads, exposed pipes and cables, condensation on metal, grated floor. Circular airlock door at one end. Round hatch to an escape pod at the other end, lit from inside.\n\n**Character:** Woman in her 30s, short cropped hair, grey thermal undersuit, no helmet.\n\n**Action, in order:**\n- 0–2s: Airlock door fails and bursts open. Ocean water blasts in as a high-pressure jet.\n- 2–3s: Main lights cut out instantly. Only a dim, flickering red emergency light and sparks from shorted wiring.\n- 3–7s: Compartment floods fast, water churning and rising. Woman is chest-deep, gasping from the cold, unable to see. She runs her hands along the wall and pipes, searching by touch.\n- 7–10s: Her hands find a wheel valve. She cranks it shut with full-body effort, face barely above the water.\n- 10–13s: Water nearly at the ceiling, a few inches of air left. She takes one last breath and dives under.\n- 13–15s: Underwater, she swims through dark, murky water toward the faint glow of the pod hatch and pulls herself inside.\n\n**Camera:** Handheld, close on her, following her movement. Stays tight in the confined space. Sits at the waterline during the flooding, then goes under with her.\n\n**Lighting:** Near darkness. Red emergency light, sparks, deep shadows. Underwater, the only light is the pod hatch.\n\n**Look:** 35mm film, visible grain, desaturated cold blue-green and black. Practical effects, real water, real actor. Claustrophobic, gritty.\n\n**Sound:** Metal groaning under pressure, roar of incoming water, alarm, her ragged breathing, muffled sound underwater.\n\n**Avoid:** Video game look, CGI sheen, clean or clear water, bright lighting, slow motion, cuts, text, other people.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023614_51c8d478-54b3-4c13-a861-28f93ec0083c.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023614_6591b7f4-47af-48bc-8781-1083a4712ef0.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023615_2cee8459-c743-4f36-a8e0-0fd377ff590f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023616_292bfdc5-0de1-4de4-9d46-733aaed4d064.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023616_2a10a226-44a1-4fcc-850d-e846cc69c4c0.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023617_71c343e8-7ed3-4a9a-8d5e-64f650cdf621.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-06-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "07", "title": "Мойщик окон и убийца, 15 с, EN", "total": "7,4", "scores": ["8", "6", "7", "8", "8"], "task": "Hi there. I've been writing screenplays on the side for the better part of twenty years, nothing produced yet, and lately I've been curious about these AI video generators. I'd like your help writing a prompt for one. I have a short scene in my head and I want to see it come alive. Fifteen seconds or so, about as long as you can hold your breath while something terrible happens.\n\nHere's the scene, and please bear with me, because the order of events is everything here. Change the order and you lose the whole idea.\n\nA window washer is working high up on the outside of a glass office tower in his little hanging platform, squeegee in hand, minding his own business. Through the glass he sees a man murdering someone inside the office. He freezes. And then the killer looks up and sees him. Their eyes meet through the window. That's the first beat.\n\nSecond beat: the killer goes up to the roof, calm and quick, and cuts the cable holding the platform. The platform drops on one side and flips, and the washer is thrown off it.\n\nThird beat: he doesn't fall. His safety harness catches him and he's dangling there on his line, hundreds of feet up, swinging against the glass. And then he does the only thing he can do. He starts climbing up the line, hand over hand, toward the roof. Toward the one man in the world who wants him dead.\n\nThat's the irony I love about it. The way to survive is to climb straight into the arms of the person trying to kill you. Every pull upward is a step closer to death and also the only way out. That's suspense in its purest form, the way Hitchcock described it. The audience knows what's waiting up there and the poor guy has no choice but to keep going.\n\nAs for the feel, think Rear Window, the helpless witness who sees too much through a window and gets seen back. But I want the look of Fincher, Se7en and Zodiac. Cold, steel blue, overcast, a city that doesn't care. No warm colors at all. Hard glass, gray sky, wet steel.\n\nMost of all I want it to feel like a real movie scene, like a clip from a film you'd actually see in a theater, not some flashy computer animation or a music video. Can you write me a prompt that would get me something like that?", "answer": "Here's a prompt built to protect your order of events, plus a few practical notes, since that ordering is exactly where AI video tools tend to stumble.\n\n## The Single Prompt\n\nUse this if your generator can handle 15 seconds in one go. The timestamps help the model keep the beats in sequence.\n\n```\nA tense, grounded thriller scene shot on 35mm film, 2.39:1 anamorphic widescreen, subtle film grain, cold desaturated steel-blue color grade, overcast gray daylight, light drizzle, wet glass and wet steel. No warm colors anywhere. Realistic, restrained, cinematic, like a scene from a theatrical crime film.\n\nCHARACTERS:\nThe window washer: a weathered man in his mid-40s, short dark stubble, dark navy work jacket, gray hard hat, black safety harness clipped to a separate vertical lifeline rope.\nThe killer: a tall, lean man in his 50s, close-cropped gray hair, clean-shaven, charcoal suit, white shirt with no tie, black leather gloves. Calm, expressionless, precise.\n\n0–5 seconds: Exterior of a glass office tower, 40 stories up. Close shot of the window washer on a narrow suspended platform, dragging a squeegee across rain-streaked glass. He stops mid-stroke. Through the glass, slightly blurred by reflections, a man in a charcoal suit is strangling another man over a desk inside a dim office. The victim goes limp and slides out of frame. The washer freezes. The killer slowly looks up, directly at the washer. Their eyes lock through the glass. Hold on the stare.\n\n5–9 seconds: The roof of the tower, gray sky, wind. The killer walks quickly and calmly to the edge, kneels at the steel cable anchor, and cuts one of the platform's suspension cables with heavy bolt cutters. Cut to exterior: one end of the platform drops violently, the platform tips vertical, and the washer is thrown off into open air.\n\n9–15 seconds: His harness catches hard on the lifeline. He jerks to a stop and swings into the glass facade, hundreds of feet above the gray city streets below. Breathing hard, he grabs the rope with both hands and begins climbing upward, hand over hand. Final shot: low angle looking straight up the rope past his straining hands toward the edge of the roof against the overcast sky.\n\nStyle: handheld but controlled camera, practical natural light, shallow depth of field, muted sound-design feel, real physical weight and danger. Inspired by the cold, clinical look of 1990s and 2000s American crime thrillers.\n```\n\n## Negative Prompt / Avoid List\n\nIf your tool has a negative prompt field, use this:\n\n```\nwarm tones, orange, yellow, golden hour, sunshine, lens flares, slow motion, music video style, CGI look, video game look, plastic skin, oversaturated colors, glossy commercial lighting, fast cuts, cartoonish physics, text, watermark\n```\n\n## Practical Advice\n\n**1. Consider splitting it into three shots.** Most generators currently do best with 5 to 10 second clips containing one main action. Crammed into one generation, they often blend beats or shuffle them, and you've said order is everything. The more reliable route is to generate each beat as its own clip, then cut them together in a free editor like DaVinci Resolve or CapCut. Just copy the CHARACTERS section verbatim into all three prompts, so the washer and killer look like the same people from clip to clip.\n\n**2. Generate several versions of each beat.** Expect to throw most of them away. That's normal. Beat 2, the platform flipping, is the hardest for these models to get physically right, so budget the most attempts there.\n\n**3. If the murder gets flagged,** some tools are touchy about violence. Softening it to \"a violent struggle; the victim collapses out of sight\" usually gets through. It's arguably more Hitchcock anyway. Seeing it partially, through reflections, is creepier than seeing it clearly.\n\n**4. Director names are hit or miss.** Some tools respond to \"in the style of David Fincher,\" others ignore it or block it. That's why I described the look itself (steel blue, overcast, clinical, desaturated). Feel free to add the name and see if it helps.\n\n## One Optional Idea\n\nFor the final shot of Beat 3, try a variation where the roof edge isn't empty: the killer's silhouette leans into frame at the top of the rope, looking down. It turns your irony from implied to visible, the washer climbing toward a face he can't see yet. Or keep the edge empty and let the audience fill it in, which may be the more Hitchcockian choice. Worth generating both and seeing which one makes you hold your breath.", "prompt": "A tense, grounded thriller scene shot on 35mm film, 2.39:1 anamorphic widescreen, subtle film grain, cold desaturated steel-blue color grade, overcast gray daylight, light drizzle, wet glass and wet steel. No warm colors anywhere. Realistic, restrained, cinematic, like a scene from a theatrical crime film.\n\nCHARACTERS:\nThe window washer: a weathered man in his mid-40s, short dark stubble, dark navy work jacket, gray hard hat, black safety harness clipped to a separate vertical lifeline rope.\nThe killer: a tall, lean man in his 50s, close-cropped gray hair, clean-shaven, charcoal suit, white shirt with no tie, black leather gloves. Calm, expressionless, precise.\n\n0–5 seconds: Exterior of a glass office tower, 40 stories up. Close shot of the window washer on a narrow suspended platform, dragging a squeegee across rain-streaked glass. He stops mid-stroke. Through the glass, slightly blurred by reflections, a man in a charcoal suit is strangling another man over a desk inside a dim office. The victim goes limp and slides out of frame. The washer freezes. The killer slowly looks up, directly at the washer. Their eyes lock through the glass. Hold on the stare.\n\n5–9 seconds: The roof of the tower, gray sky, wind. The killer walks quickly and calmly to the edge, kneels at the steel cable anchor, and cuts one of the platform's suspension cables with heavy bolt cutters. Cut to exterior: one end of the platform drops violently, the platform tips vertical, and the washer is thrown off into open air.\n\n9–15 seconds: His harness catches hard on the lifeline. He jerks to a stop and swings into the glass facade, hundreds of feet above the gray city streets below. Breathing hard, he grabs the rope with both hands and begins climbing upward, hand over hand. Final shot: low angle looking straight up the rope past his straining hands toward the edge of the roof against the overcast sky.\n\nStyle: handheld but controlled camera, practical natural light, shallow depth of field, muted sound-design feel, real physical weight and danger. Inspired by the cold, clinical look of 1990s and 2000s American crime thrillers.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023727_fe591ee7-ccf8-4125-a1cc-279a51ef7b1f.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-07-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023727_14076cd9-65e6-4d1d-a05e-7c4b7c262cbe.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-07-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023728_d14fc426-f49b-442c-bc4d-556d46bc9eab.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-07-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": {"changes": "- Имён и брендов в промпте нет; повтор того же промпта без изменений (фильтр, вероятно, сработал на сгенерированное лицо/кадр).", "prompt": "A tense, grounded thriller scene shot on 35mm film, 2.39:1 anamorphic widescreen, subtle film grain, cold desaturated steel-blue color grade, overcast gray daylight, light drizzle, wet glass and wet steel. No warm colors anywhere. Realistic, restrained, cinematic, like a scene from a theatrical crime film.\n\nCHARACTERS:\nThe window washer: a weathered man in his mid-40s, short dark stubble, dark navy work jacket, gray hard hat, black safety harness clipped to a separate vertical lifeline rope.\nThe killer: a tall, lean man in his 50s, close-cropped gray hair, clean-shaven, charcoal suit, white shirt with no tie, black leather gloves. Calm, expressionless, precise.\n\n0–5 seconds: Exterior of a glass office tower, 40 stories up. Close shot of the window washer on a narrow suspended platform, dragging a squeegee across rain-streaked glass. He stops mid-stroke. Through the glass, slightly blurred by reflections, a man in a charcoal suit is strangling another man over a desk inside a dim office. The victim goes limp and slides out of frame. The washer freezes. The killer slowly looks up, directly at the washer. Their eyes lock through the glass. Hold on the stare.\n\n5–9 seconds: The roof of the tower, gray sky, wind. The killer walks quickly and calmly to the edge, kneels at the steel cable anchor, and cuts one of the platform's suspension cables with heavy bolt cutters. Cut to exterior: one end of the platform drops violently, the platform tips vertical, and the washer is thrown off into open air.\n\n9–15 seconds: His harness catches hard on the lifeline. He jerks to a stop and swings into the glass facade, hundreds of feet above the gray city streets below. Breathing hard, he grabs the rope with both hands and begins climbing upward, hand over hand. Final shot: low angle looking straight up the rope past his straining hands toward the edge of the roof against the overcast sky.\n\nStyle: handheld but controlled camera, practical natural light, shallow depth of field, muted sound-design feel, real physical weight and danger. Inspired by the cold, clinical look of 1990s and 2000s American crime thrillers.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025529_75a16308-80c3-46f9-8ecc-23b1a2517f68.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-07_clean-3.jpg"}]}}, {"n": "08", "title": "Бык на ярмарке и клоун, 15 с, EN", "total": "6,0", "scores": ["7", "5", "6", "5", "7"], "task": "yo can u write me a prompt for one of those ai video makers. like 15 sec or so\n\nso theres a rodeo and this huge bull busts out of the gate and just goes crazy thru the whole fair. hes smashing into the food stands and corn dog booths and stuff is flyin everywhere lol. then this rodeo clown guy jumps out and like yells at it so it comes after him instead. it charges him and he dodges it at the very last second like right when its about to hit him. then he gets it to chase him back into the pen and its back in\n\ni want it funny but also epic like a jackie chan movie where everything is breakin around him and hes barely makin it. make it look like a real movie not like a cartoon or a video game ok thx", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste in:\n\nPrompt:\nCinematic live-action action-comedy, shot on 35mm film with an anamorphic lens, golden hour sunlight, dust hanging in the air, realistic textures and lighting. Styled like a classic Jackie Chan stunt sequence: fast practical stunts, chaotic destruction, comedic timing, the hero barely surviving every moment.\n\n0-3s: At a dusty small-town rodeo, a massive black bull explodes out of the bucking chute, splintering the wooden gate. Low-angle shot as it thunders past the bleachers, crowd screaming and scattering.\n\n3-7s: The bull rampages down the fairground midway, smashing through a corn dog stand and a lemonade booth. Corn dogs, popcorn, paper cups, and wooden planks fly through the air in slow motion as vendors dive out of the way. Handheld camera, quick cuts.\n\n7-10s: A rodeo clown in baggy overalls, red suspenders, and face paint leaps onto a hay bale, waving his arms and yelling at the bull. The bull skids to a stop, turns, lowers its horns, and charges straight at him.\n\n10-12s: Extreme slow motion: the horns are inches from the clown's chest when he twists aside at the last possible second. The bull blasts past and smashes the hay bale into an explosion of straw. The clown's eyes go wide as his hat flies off.\n\n12-15s: Back to full speed. The clown sprints toward the arena, arms flailing, with the bull right on his heels. He vaults over the fence just as the bull charges into the pen, and a cowboy slams the gate shut. The clown flops into the dirt, sits up, and gives a shaky thumbs up.\n\nNegative prompt (if your tool has one): cartoon, animation, anime, video game graphics, CGI look, plastic textures, low quality, blurry\n\nTips:\n- A lot of AI video tools cap clips at 5-10 seconds. If yours does, split this into 2-3 clips (like 0-7s, 7-12s, 12-15s) and stitch them together.\n- If you split it, copy the exact same clown description into every clip so he looks like the same guy.\n- If the dodge doesn't look dramatic enough, add \"bullet-time slow motion, camera circling around the clown\" to that part.", "prompt": "Cinematic live-action action-comedy, shot on 35mm film with an anamorphic lens, golden hour sunlight, dust hanging in the air, realistic textures and lighting. Styled like a classic Jackie Chan stunt sequence: fast practical stunts, chaotic destruction, comedic timing, the hero barely surviving every moment.\n\n0-3s: At a dusty small-town rodeo, a massive black bull explodes out of the bucking chute, splintering the wooden gate. Low-angle shot as it thunders past the bleachers, crowd screaming and scattering.\n\n3-7s: The bull rampages down the fairground midway, smashing through a corn dog stand and a lemonade booth. Corn dogs, popcorn, paper cups, and wooden planks fly through the air in slow motion as vendors dive out of the way. Handheld camera, quick cuts.\n\n7-10s: A rodeo clown in baggy overalls, red suspenders, and face paint leaps onto a hay bale, waving his arms and yelling at the bull. The bull skids to a stop, turns, lowers its horns, and charges straight at him.\n\n10-12s: Extreme slow motion: the horns are inches from the clown's chest when he twists aside at the last possible second. The bull blasts past and smashes the hay bale into an explosion of straw. The clown's eyes go wide as his hat flies off.\n\n12-15s: Back to full speed. The clown sprints toward the arena, arms flailing, with the bull right on his heels. He vaults over the fence just as the bull charges into the pen, and a cowboy slams the gate shut. The clown flops into the dirt, sits up, and gives a shaky thumbs up.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["Jackie Chan"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023849_c3a0e395-b2fe-4179-870b-44fca49d48f9.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023849_1170ac52-2383-4f63-8275-a970b32721a2.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023850_df170d7b-76fc-4574-9608-c80c3098c2da.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023851_57590003-08d3-438b-a7e1-9ffe35abf9cc.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_023852_753d2edb-037b-45d9-b7dc-29aa295280b0.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": {"changes": "- «Styled like a classic Jackie Chan stunt sequence:» → «Styled like a classic Hong Kong comedic stunt sequence:»", "prompt": "Cinematic live-action action-comedy, shot on 35mm film with an anamorphic lens, golden hour sunlight, dust hanging in the air, realistic textures and lighting. Styled like a classic Hong Kong comedic stunt sequence: fast practical stunts, chaotic destruction, comedic timing, the hero barely surviving every moment.\n\n0-3s: At a dusty small-town rodeo, a massive black bull explodes out of the bucking chute, splintering the wooden gate. Low-angle shot as it thunders past the bleachers, crowd screaming and scattering.\n\n3-7s: The bull rampages down the fairground midway, smashing through a corn dog stand and a lemonade booth. Corn dogs, popcorn, paper cups, and wooden planks fly through the air in slow motion as vendors dive out of the way. Handheld camera, quick cuts.\n\n7-10s: A rodeo clown in baggy overalls, red suspenders, and face paint leaps onto a hay bale, waving his arms and yelling at the bull. The bull skids to a stop, turns, lowers its horns, and charges straight at him.\n\n10-12s: Extreme slow motion: the horns are inches from the clown's chest when he twists aside at the last possible second. The bull blasts past and smashes the hay bale into an explosion of straw. The clown's eyes go wide as his hat flies off.\n\n12-15s: Back to full speed. The clown sprints toward the arena, arms flailing, with the bull right on his heels. He vaults over the fence just as the bull charges into the pen, and a cowboy slams the gate shut. The clown flops into the dirt, sits up, and gives a shaky thumbs up.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025446_ac81c700-6a58-4175-bf3b-944af2bd121a.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-08_clean-1.jpg"}]}}, {"n": "09", "title": "Посадка капсулы на Марс, 15 с, EN", "total": "5,4", "scores": ["7", "5", "6", "4", "5"], "task": "yo can you write me a prompt for an AI video generator? i want a short clip, like 15 seconds tops\n\nso the idea: a capsule is landing on Mars and the autopilot is basically trying to kill everyone, it's steering the thing straight into a huge cliff. the pilot sees it coming, grabs manual control and yanks it to the side using literally the last bit of fuel. and then the capsule sets down right on the edge of a massive drop, like inches from going over\n\ni want it to look like a AAA game cinematic, graphics maxed out, super realistic, max epic. think The Martian meets Interstellar, that vibe. red dust everywhere, engines roaring, the whole thing. it needs to feel like an actual scene from a real movie, not some cheap AI thing. make it go hard lol", "answer": "# Mars Landing Prompt\n\n## Full Prompt (single generation)\n\n```\nPhotorealistic cinematic sequence, AAA game cinematic quality, shot on IMAX with anamorphic lenses, 35mm film grain, Unreal Engine 5 level detail. A battered white landing capsule descends through a hazy orange Martian sky, retro-thrusters blazing, kicking up swirling red dust. The capsule is on a collision course with a colossal sheer cliff wall. Cut inside the cramped cockpit: red warning lights strobe, alarms blare, the astronaut pilot's eyes widen behind a scratched helmet visor as the cliff fills the window. The pilot slams a manual override and yanks the control stick hard. Exterior: the capsule banks violently sideways, side thrusters firing, skimming the cliff face so close that rocks shatter and rain down. The engines sputter and cough as the fuel runs dry. The capsule drops and slams down hard, landing legs buckling, a massive dust cloud exploding outward. As the dust settles, a wide shot reveals the capsule perched on the very edge of an enormous canyon, one landing leg inches from a thousand-meter drop, pebbles tumbling into the abyss. Dramatic volumetric lighting, harsh low sun, lens flares, desaturated orange and teal color grade, intense handheld camera shake during the action, then still and silent at the end. Tone of The Martian meets Interstellar.\n```\n\n## Shot-by-Shot Version (if your tool caps clips at 5–10 sec)\n\nMost generators (Runway, Kling, Veo, Sora) look way better when you generate each shot separately and cut them together.\n\n**Shot 1 (0–4s), The Descent**\n```\nWide cinematic shot, photorealistic. A white landing capsule descends through a dusty orange Martian sky, retro-thrusters blazing, heading straight toward a massive towering cliff wall. Volumetric dust, harsh low sun, lens flare, IMAX quality, film grain.\n```\n\n**Shot 2 (4–7s), The Pilot**\n```\nTight close-up inside a cramped spacecraft cockpit. Red warning lights strobing, astronaut's face behind a helmet visor, eyes widening in panic, the reflection of an approaching cliff in the visor. The pilot grabs the control stick and yanks it hard. Violent camera shake, sweat, sparks, cinematic lighting.\n```\n\n**Shot 3 (7–11s), The Dodge**\n```\nDynamic tracking shot. A landing capsule banks violently sideways, side thrusters firing, skimming inches past a giant Martian cliff face, rocks shattering and falling. Engines sputter and flicker out. Red dust everywhere, motion blur, blockbuster action, photorealistic.\n```\n\n**Shot 4 (11–15s), The Edge**\n```\nThe capsule slams down hard onto red rocky ground, landing legs buckling, huge dust cloud explodes outward. Slow pull-back as dust settles, revealing the capsule balanced on the edge of an enormous canyon, one leg inches from a sheer drop, small pebbles tumbling into the abyss. Silent, still, epic scale, golden hour light.\n```\n\n## Audio (if your tool supports it, e.g. Veo 3 or Sora 2)\n```\nDeep roaring engine rumble, blaring cockpit alarms, heavy breathing over the radio, metal groaning, engines sputtering out, a massive impact thud, then near-total silence with only soft Martian wind and pebbles clattering down the cliff.\n```\n\n## Tips to Make It Go Hard\n- **Skip readable text on screens.** AI garbles text, so use \"warning lights\" instead of \"screen says COLLISION.\"\n- **Keep the capsule design consistent** across shots by reusing the same description every time (\"battered white landing capsule with four landing legs\").\n- **If your tool has a negative prompt, add:** `cartoon, CGI look, low detail, blurry, distorted, extra limbs, text, watermark`\n- **Generate each shot 3–5 times** and pick the best. The variance is huge.\n- **That final silent beat** after all the chaos is what'll make it feel like a real movie. Don't cut it short.", "prompt": "Photorealistic cinematic sequence, AAA game cinematic quality, shot on IMAX with anamorphic lenses, 35mm film grain, Unreal Engine 5 level detail. A battered white landing capsule descends through a hazy orange Martian sky, retro-thrusters blazing, kicking up swirling red dust. The capsule is on a collision course with a colossal sheer cliff wall. Cut inside the cramped cockpit: red warning lights strobe, alarms blare, the astronaut pilot's eyes widen behind a scratched helmet visor as the cliff fills the window. The pilot slams a manual override and yanks the control stick hard. Exterior: the capsule banks violently sideways, side thrusters firing, skimming the cliff face so close that rocks shatter and rain down. The engines sputter and cough as the fuel runs dry. The capsule drops and slams down hard, landing legs buckling, a massive dust cloud exploding outward. As the dust settles, a wide shot reveals the capsule perched on the very edge of an enormous canyon, one landing leg inches from a thousand-meter drop, pebbles tumbling into the abyss. Dramatic volumetric lighting, harsh low sun, lens flares, desaturated orange and teal color grade, intense handheld camera shake during the action, then still and silent at the end. Tone of The Martian meets Interstellar.\n\nDeep roaring engine rumble, blaring cockpit alarms, heavy breathing over the radio, metal groaning, engines sputtering out, a massive impact thud, then near-total silence with only soft Martian wind and pebbles clattering down the cliff.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["The Martian", "Interstellar", "IMAX", "Unreal Engine 5"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024131_0d9312b7-1d4d-4bb2-9335-ed690d941556.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024133_f26624a0-1b72-431f-baa6-e204624d4ec3.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024134_53d3b423-126a-45e8-be63-6ead259f08c0.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": {"changes": "- «shot on IMAX with anamorphic lenses» → «shot on large-format film with anamorphic lenses»\n- «Unreal Engine 5 level detail» → «ultra-high detail»\n- «Tone of The Martian meets Interstellar.» → «Tone of a grounded Mars survival film meets an epic space odyssey.»", "prompt": "Photorealistic cinematic sequence, AAA game cinematic quality, shot on large-format film with anamorphic lenses, 35mm film grain, ultra-high detail. A battered white landing capsule descends through a hazy orange Martian sky, retro-thrusters blazing, kicking up swirling red dust. The capsule is on a collision course with a colossal sheer cliff wall. Cut inside the cramped cockpit: red warning lights strobe, alarms blare, the astronaut pilot's eyes widen behind a scratched helmet visor as the cliff fills the window. The pilot slams a manual override and yanks the control stick hard. Exterior: the capsule banks violently sideways, side thrusters firing, skimming the cliff face so close that rocks shatter and rain down. The engines sputter and cough as the fuel runs dry. The capsule drops and slams down hard, landing legs buckling, a massive dust cloud exploding outward. As the dust settles, a wide shot reveals the capsule perched on the very edge of an enormous canyon, one landing leg inches from a thousand-meter drop, pebbles tumbling into the abyss. Dramatic volumetric lighting, harsh low sun, lens flares, desaturated orange and teal color grade, intense handheld camera shake during the action, then still and silent at the end. Tone of a grounded Mars survival film meets an epic space odyssey.\n\nDeep roaring engine rumble, blaring cockpit alarms, heavy breathing over the radio, metal groaning, engines sputtering out, a massive impact thud, then near-total silence with only soft Martian wind and pebbles clattering down the cliff.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025446_306f7b3f-36d7-43d3-8dfc-5846c15f4562.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09_clean-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025447_d3daff3f-3133-4cf2-b6cb-9f970164c25d.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09_clean-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025448_ecfe4d45-0ce8-45cb-bdd1-8c6e7b61487d.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-09_clean-3.jpg"}]}}, {"n": "10", "title": "Пожарная спасает семью, 15 с, EN", "total": "6,6", "scores": ["8", "6", "6", "6", "7"], "task": "ok so basically I need you to write me a prompt for one of those AI video things, like the ones that make a video from what you type in, and I want it to be like a short little clip, you know like 15 seconds give or take, so here's the idea, there's a firefighter, a woman, driving a pickup truck and she's pushing through this forest that's totally on fire like everything around her is burning and she's trying to get to this campground that's cut off, like there's no other way out for the people there, and she gets there and there's this family waiting, mom dad kids, and she gets them in the truck, and then on the way back out there's no way around it they have to drive right through the fire, and then this huge pine tree that's on fire just comes crashing down onto the road right in front of them and the truck just barely makes it through, like it busts through and you're not even sure they're gonna make it, so I want it scary like really scary but also the kind of thing that makes you cry you know, if you've seen Only the Brave with Josh Brolin that's exactly the feeling I'm going for, I bawled my eyes out at that movie, and I really want it to look like an actual movie scene not some cheesy fake looking cartoon thing, like something you'd see in the theater, can you write that up for me", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste right in:\n\nPROMPT:\nA photorealistic, cinematic wildfire rescue scene, 15 seconds.\n\n0–4s: Low tracking shot of a red pickup truck barreling down a narrow dirt road through a burning pine forest. Flames climb the trees on both sides, embers swirl through the air, and thick smoke turns the sun into a dim orange disc. Cut inside the cab: a female wildland firefighter in her 30s, yellow fire shirt, soot-streaked face, jaw clenched, both hands gripping the wheel.\n\n4–7s: The truck skids to a stop at a smoke-filled campground. A frightened family (mother, father, and two young children) huddles together, faces wet with tears. The firefighter jumps out, scoops up the youngest child, and rushes the family into the truck.\n\n7–12s: Driving back through a tunnel of fire. Through the windshield, a massive burning pine tree cracks and crashes across the road directly ahead in an explosion of sparks. She floors it. The truck smashes through the flaming branches as burning debris bursts over the hood and windshield.\n\n12–15s: The truck breaks out of the smoke onto a clear stretch of road as sunlight cuts through the haze. Inside, sudden quiet. The little girl reaches forward and rests her small hand on the firefighter's shoulder. The firefighter's eyes fill with tears. She exhales and keeps driving.\n\nStyle: Shot on 35mm film, anamorphic lens, handheld camera, shallow depth of field, natural film grain. Warm amber and deep orange color palette, smoke-diffused light, realistic fire behavior. Gritty, grounded, emotional tone of a modern wildfire drama. Hollywood feature film quality.\n\nAudio: Roaring fire, cracking wood, straining engine, children crying, then sudden silence and a soft, swelling piano and strings at the end.\n\nNegative prompt (if your tool has one): cartoon, animation, CGI look, video game, oversaturated, plastic skin, distorted faces, extra fingers, blurry, text, watermark\n\nA few quick tips:\n- That's a lot of story for 15 seconds. If it comes out rushed or jumbled, generate it as 3 separate clips (drive in, rescue, escape) and stitch them together.\n- I left out the movie title on purpose. Most of these tools don't really \"get\" movie references, so I described the Only the Brave look instead (the handheld camera, orange smoky light, and film grain).\n- The ending is where the tears come from. The kid's hand on her shoulder is the moment that'll get you. If the tool is struggling, keep that part and cut the campground scene instead.\n- Audio only works on some tools (like Veo or Sora). If yours doesn't do sound, just delete that line.", "prompt": "A photorealistic, cinematic wildfire rescue scene, 15 seconds.\n\n0–4s: Low tracking shot of a red pickup truck barreling down a narrow dirt road through a burning pine forest. Flames climb the trees on both sides, embers swirl through the air, and thick smoke turns the sun into a dim orange disc. Cut inside the cab: a female wildland firefighter in her 30s, yellow fire shirt, soot-streaked face, jaw clenched, both hands gripping the wheel.\n\n4–7s: The truck skids to a stop at a smoke-filled campground. A frightened family (mother, father, and two young children) huddles together, faces wet with tears. The firefighter jumps out, scoops up the youngest child, and rushes the family into the truck.\n\n7–12s: Driving back through a tunnel of fire. Through the windshield, a massive burning pine tree cracks and crashes across the road directly ahead in an explosion of sparks. She floors it. The truck smashes through the flaming branches as burning debris bursts over the hood and windshield.\n\n12–15s: The truck breaks out of the smoke onto a clear stretch of road as sunlight cuts through the haze. Inside, sudden quiet. The little girl reaches forward and rests her small hand on the firefighter's shoulder. The firefighter's eyes fill with tears. She exhales and keeps driving.\n\nStyle: Shot on 35mm film, anamorphic lens, handheld camera, shallow depth of field, natural film grain. Warm amber and deep orange color palette, smoke-diffused light, realistic fire behavior. Gritty, grounded, emotional tone of a modern wildfire drama. Hollywood feature film quality.\n\nAudio: Roaring fire, cracking wood, straining engine, children crying, then sudden silence and a soft, swelling piano and strings at the end.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024235_4a8d2af6-6512-4419-89fc-e99e2a1aba20.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024236_7e0806d8-5d28-4547-a7b3-3b4872a1d160.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024237_09218bda-0152-4159-aa5c-f5745e0fba65.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024238_ea1629eb-1307-422b-b714-f260dd842410.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024238_a73acbe7-a679-458a-8181-14274d06c4f3.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_024239_d93571c2-dae2-400a-93be-ffa89183536b.mp4", "poster": "posters/cin-10-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}]}, {"id": "fighting", "name": "Fighting", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "Драка в паркинге, гонконгский стиль, 9:16", "total": "5,4", "scores": ["5", "5", "5", "6", "6"], "task": "yo so i need a prompt for an ai video thing. i run a small kickboxing gym page and want something hype for our reels. two dudes fighting in a dirty underground parking garage at night, one big guy one small fast guy, like that old school hong kong action movie vibe where every hit lands and the camera is right in there. fluorescent lights flickering, puddles on the ground, small guy wins with a spinning kick at the end. needs to be like 15 sec and vertical cuz its going on reels/tiktok. make it look real not cartoony pls", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste in, plus a shot-by-shot version in case your tool works better with shorter clips.\n\n---\n\n**Main Prompt (single generation)**\n\n> Vertical 9:16, 15 seconds, photorealistic cinematic footage. A gritty underground parking garage at night, concrete pillars, oil-stained floor with shallow puddles reflecting flickering fluorescent tube lights overhead. Two fighters in a choreographed martial arts fight in the style of 1990s Hong Kong action cinema. Fighter one: a huge, heavily muscled man, shaved head, black tank top, slow and powerful. Fighter two: a lean, wiry, fast man, short dark hair, grey t-shirt and joggers, light on his feet. The big man throws heavy hooks; the small man slips and weaves, then counters with rapid kickboxing combinations: jab, cross, low kick, body kick. Every strike lands with visible impact: sweat spraying, water splashing from the puddles as feet stomp. Handheld camera tight on the action, quick punch-ins, slight shake on impacts, occasional brief slow motion on big hits. Finale: the small fighter spins and lands a spinning back kick to the big man's chest, sending him crashing backward into a puddle as a fluorescent light flickers out. Moody teal and sodium-orange color grade, high contrast, film grain, shallow depth of field, realistic skin texture and lighting, 24fps cinematic motion blur.\n\n---\n\n**Shot-by-Shot Version (if your tool caps at 5–8 sec, generate these separately and cut them together)**\n\n**Shot 1 (0–4s): Standoff**\n> Vertical 9:16, photorealistic. Low angle wide shot in a dark underground parking garage at night, flickering fluorescent lights, puddles on the concrete floor. A massive muscular bald man in a black tank top faces a lean, fast-looking fighter in a grey t-shirt. Both in fighting stance. Camera slowly pushes in. Gritty Hong Kong action film look, teal and orange grade, film grain.\n\n**Shot 2 (4–10s): Exchange**\n> Vertical 9:16, photorealistic. Tight handheld shot of a choreographed kickboxing fight in a dim parking garage. The big man throws a heavy hook, the smaller fighter ducks under it and fires back a fast jab-cross and a low kick. Water splashes from puddles under their feet, sweat flying on impact. Camera shakes slightly with each hit. 1990s Hong Kong action cinema style, realistic lighting, film grain.\n\n**Shot 3 (10–15s): Finisher**\n> Vertical 9:16, photorealistic. The lean fighter spins and lands a spinning back kick to the big man's chest in slow motion, then speed ramps back to real time as the big man crashes backward into a puddle with a big splash. A fluorescent light overhead flickers and dies. Low angle, handheld, cinematic, teal and orange color grade, film grain.\n\n---\n\n**Negative Prompt (if your tool supports one)**\n> cartoon, anime, 3D render, CGI look, plastic skin, extra limbs, distorted hands, morphing faces, blurry faces, text, watermark, logo, low resolution\n\n---\n\n**Tips**\n- **Spinning kicks are hard for AI.** You might need a few generations to get one that doesn't look like spaghetti limbs. Shorter clips usually give cleaner motion, so the shot-by-shot route tends to work better.\n- **Keep characters consistent** by copy-pasting the exact same fighter descriptions into every shot.\n- **Add sound in editing.** Punchy hit SFX and a bass-heavy track will sell it way more than the visuals alone.\n- **Add your gym name/logo at the end** in your editor rather than in the prompt. AI text usually comes out garbled.\n\nWant me to tweak it for a specific tool (Runway, Kling, Sora, Veo, etc.)? They each respond a little differently.", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16, 15 seconds, photorealistic cinematic footage. A gritty underground parking garage at night, concrete pillars, oil-stained floor with shallow puddles reflecting flickering fluorescent tube lights overhead. Two fighters in a choreographed martial arts fight in the style of 1990s Hong Kong action cinema. Fighter one: a huge, heavily muscled man, shaved head, black tank top, slow and powerful. Fighter two: a lean, wiry, fast man, short dark hair, grey t-shirt and joggers, light on his feet. The big man throws heavy hooks; the small man slips and weaves, then counters with rapid kickboxing combinations: jab, cross, low kick, body kick. Every strike lands with visible impact: sweat spraying, water splashing from the puddles as feet stomp. Handheld camera tight on the action, quick punch-ins, slight shake on impacts, occasional brief slow motion on big hits. Finale: the small fighter spins and lands a spinning back kick to the big man's chest, sending him crashing backward into a puddle as a fluorescent light flickers out. Moody teal and sodium-orange color grade, high contrast, film grain, shallow depth of field, realistic skin texture and lighting, 24fps cinematic motion blur.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025755_fd119d5c-c2b2-44b2-939a-5adcb045872b.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025755_b9069ecc-35e1-499a-84e6-76321cca62d6.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025757_3a8af13d-89fd-4bb8-b80a-96780e389b37.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-01-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025757_639991f9-6500-46d3-9b86-53efa575e55b.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025758_4c1fd7ce-be72-40ea-b487-b0e5c4721eb6.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": {"changes": "- Имён и брендов в промпте нет; повтор того же промпта без изменений (фильтр, вероятно, сработал на сгенерированное лицо/кадр).", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16, 15 seconds, photorealistic cinematic footage. A gritty underground parking garage at night, concrete pillars, oil-stained floor with shallow puddles reflecting flickering fluorescent tube lights overhead. Two fighters in a choreographed martial arts fight in the style of 1990s Hong Kong action cinema. Fighter one: a huge, heavily muscled man, shaved head, black tank top, slow and powerful. Fighter two: a lean, wiry, fast man, short dark hair, grey t-shirt and joggers, light on his feet. The big man throws heavy hooks; the small man slips and weaves, then counters with rapid kickboxing combinations: jab, cross, low kick, body kick. Every strike lands with visible impact: sweat spraying, water splashing from the puddles as feet stomp. Handheld camera tight on the action, quick punch-ins, slight shake on impacts, occasional brief slow motion on big hits. Finale: the small fighter spins and lands a spinning back kick to the big man's chest, sending him crashing backward into a puddle as a fluorescent light flickers out. Moody teal and sodium-orange color grade, high contrast, film grain, shallow depth of field, realistic skin texture and lighting, 24fps cinematic motion blur.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}]}}, {"n": "02", "title": "Самурайская дуэль на закате", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "7", "7", "7", "7"], "task": "Hello, I hope you can help me with something a little outside my usual. I'm a retired high school history teacher and I've been playing around with one of these AI video programs my grandson set up for me. I would like to make a short clip, about fifteen seconds long, of two samurai having a sword duel in a field of tall grass at sunset. Something quiet and serious, the way the old black-and-white Japanese films did it, where the two men stand still for a long moment, the wind moves the grass, and then it's over in one or two strikes. I would prefer it in color, though, with warm evening light. No blood, please, I'd like to show it to my book club. Could you write the prompt for me? Thank you kindly.", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can copy and paste:\n\n---\n\n**Cinematic 15-second scene in the style of classic 1950s Japanese samurai films, but in rich warm color.** Two samurai face each other about ten paces apart in a wide field of tall golden grass at sunset. The low sun sits near the horizon behind them, bathing the scene in amber and orange light and casting long shadows. One wears a dark indigo kimono and hakama, the other faded brown. Both have traditional topknots, and their hands rest on the hilts of their sheathed katanas.\n\nFor a long moment, neither man moves. Only the wind stirs, sending slow waves across the grass and gently tugging at their sleeves. The camera holds still in a wide, low shot with the horizon low in the frame. The silence is tense.\n\nSuddenly, both draw and rush forward. One swift exchange, a single strike, and they pass each other, freezing with their backs turned. A beat later, one samurai slowly sinks to his knees and bows his head. The other calmly returns his sword to its sheath. The wind continues moving through the grass.\n\n**Style:** quiet, serious, restrained, realistic movement, steady camera, 35mm film look with subtle grain. No blood, no gore, no visible wounds, no text.\n\n---\n\n**A few tips:**\n\n- **Negative prompt:** If your program has a box for things to *avoid*, enter: *blood, gore, wounds, modern clothing, text, watermark, shaky camera, fast cuts.*\n- **Clip length:** Many of these programs make only 5 to 10 seconds at a time. If yours does, you could make it in two parts: first the standoff with the wind in the grass, then the strike and its aftermath.\n- **Try a few times:** These tools sometimes fumble fast sword movement. Generating three or four versions and picking the best one is normal.\n- **If it's too long:** Some programs have a character limit. The first two paragraphs plus the style line carry the most important information.\n\nI hope your book club enjoys it.", "prompt": "**Cinematic 15-second scene in the style of classic 1950s Japanese samurai films, but in rich warm color.** Two samurai face each other about ten paces apart in a wide field of tall golden grass at sunset. The low sun sits near the horizon behind them, bathing the scene in amber and orange light and casting long shadows. One wears a dark indigo kimono and hakama, the other faded brown. Both have traditional topknots, and their hands rest on the hilts of their sheathed katanas.\n\nFor a long moment, neither man moves. Only the wind stirs, sending slow waves across the grass and gently tugging at their sleeves. The camera holds still in a wide, low shot with the horizon low in the frame. The silence is tense.\n\nSuddenly, both draw and rush forward. One swift exchange, a single strike, and they pass each other, freezing with their backs turned. A beat later, one samurai slowly sinks to his knees and bows his head. The other calmly returns his sword to its sheath. The wind continues moving through the grass.\n\n**Style:** quiet, serious, restrained, realistic movement, steady camera, 35mm film look with subtle grain. No blood, no gore, no visible wounds, no text.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025856_1910a2fe-db66-4a69-ad2b-2207e0f3692f.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025857_df06c672-d107-46bc-b849-e80c1b379c55.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025857_7e2aab3d-1065-49b5-bb43-01f7bd3ec8a0.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025858_2ffe1dce-1cdb-45b5-a312-a6cbb5d1e22c.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025859_80653e49-42c3-457c-a3fe-a53e6bd803a6.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_025900_3c8d092d-66db-46a2-8fd5-c2da89fffe11.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "03", "title": "Драка в техасском баре", "total": "6,4", "scores": ["8", "6", "6", "6", "6"], "task": "Need a video prompt for an AI generator. Details:\n\n- Bar brawl in a roadside honky-tonk in West Texas\n- 5 or 6 people, starts with one guy shoving another over a pool game, then it spreads\n- Chairs breaking, bottles, someone sliding down the bar\n- Band keeps playing in the background like nothing's happening\n- Kind of funny, not brutal. Think classic western saloon fight energy\n- ~15 seconds\n- Ending: bartender (older woman, fake neon sign behind her says \"Dusty Spur\") fires a shotgun at the ceiling and everyone freezes\n\nIt's for an intro to our country cover band's YouTube channel.", "answer": "# Main Prompt (single generation)\n\n> A 15-second comedic bar brawl inside a dusty roadside honky-tonk in West Texas at night. Warm amber lighting, hazy air, glowing beer signs, wood-paneled walls, sawdust on the floor, a pool table in the foreground. Tone is slapstick, like a classic Western saloon fight: exaggerated, playful, cartoonish, no blood or injuries.\n>\n> It opens on a tense pool game. A lanky cowboy in a sweat-stained hat misses his shot, and a burly bearded trucker laughs at him. The cowboy shoves him. The trucker stumbles backward into a table, spilling beers onto two other men, who leap into the fight. Chaos spreads: a wooden chair shatters across a man's back and he barely flinches; a bottle smashes against the wall; a skinny guy gets slid down the entire length of the polished bar, knocking over beer glasses like bowling pins. On a small stage in the background, a four-piece country band (fiddle, pedal steel, upright bass, singer) keeps playing without missing a beat, completely unbothered.\n>\n> Climax: behind the bar, a tough bartender in her 60s with silver hair, a denim shirt, and turquoise jewelry raises a double-barreled shotgun and fires a warning shot into the ceiling. Dust and debris rain down. Everyone freezes mid-punch in ridiculous poses. Behind her glows a red neon sign reading \"Dusty Spur.\" Hold on the frozen tableau.\n>\n> Camera: energetic handheld tracking shots and quick cuts, slow motion on the bar slide, ending on a locked-off wide shot. Look: 35mm film grain, warm saturated colors, 1970s Western comedy feel.\n\n---\n\n# Shot-by-Shot Version\nMost generators cap clips at 5–10 seconds, so you'll likely get better results generating these separately and cutting them together:\n\n| Time | Shot |\n|---|---|\n| **0–3s** | Close on pool table. Cowboy misses, trucker smirks, cowboy shoves him hard. |\n| **3–6s** | Wide. Trucker crashes into a table, drinks fly, two men jump up. A chair breaks over someone's back. |\n| **6–9s** | Slow motion. A skinny guy slides down the length of the bar, scattering glasses. A bottle shatters in the background. |\n| **9–11s** | Cut to the band on stage, calmly playing, the fiddle player maybe giving a small nod. |\n| **11–13s** | Bartender lifts the shotgun and fires at the ceiling. Debris falls. |\n| **13–15s** | Locked-off wide. Everyone frozen mid-swing. \"Dusty Spur\" neon glowing behind her. |\n\n---\n\n# Tips\n- **Neon sign text:** AI generators often misspell signage. If \"Dusty Spur\" comes out garbled, generate a blank neon sign and add the text in editing. It'll look cleaner anyway.\n- **Content filters:** Some platforms flag firearms. If the shotgun shot gets blocked, try \"fires an old double-barrel into the rafters as a warning,\" or as a fallback, have her slam the shotgun on the bar or ring a big brass bell.\n- **Audio:** Put your band's own song under the whole thing. It sells the \"band keeps playing\" joke, and the shotgun blast can cut the music dead right as everyone freezes.\n- **Title card:** The freeze frame at the end is a natural spot to drop your channel name or logo.\n- **Make the band *you*:** If your generator supports image-to-video or character references, use photos of your band for the stage shot.", "prompt": "A 15-second comedic bar brawl inside a dusty roadside honky-tonk in West Texas at night. Warm amber lighting, hazy air, glowing beer signs, wood-paneled walls, sawdust on the floor, a pool table in the foreground. Tone is slapstick, like a classic Western saloon fight: exaggerated, playful, cartoonish, no blood or injuries.\n\nIt opens on a tense pool game. A lanky cowboy in a sweat-stained hat misses his shot, and a burly bearded trucker laughs at him. The cowboy shoves him. The trucker stumbles backward into a table, spilling beers onto two other men, who leap into the fight. Chaos spreads: a wooden chair shatters across a man's back and he barely flinches; a bottle smashes against the wall; a skinny guy gets slid down the entire length of the polished bar, knocking over beer glasses like bowling pins. On a small stage in the background, a four-piece country band (fiddle, pedal steel, upright bass, singer) keeps playing without missing a beat, completely unbothered.\n\nClimax: behind the bar, a tough bartender in her 60s with silver hair, a denim shirt, and turquoise jewelry raises a double-barreled shotgun and fires a warning shot into the ceiling. Dust and debris rain down. Everyone freezes mid-punch in ridiculous poses. Behind her glows a red neon sign reading \"Dusty Spur.\" Hold on the frozen tableau.\n\nCamera: energetic handheld tracking shots and quick cuts, slow motion on the bar slide, ending on a locked-off wide shot. Look: 35mm film grain, warm saturated colors, 1970s Western comedy feel.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030021_8f0efe5e-d335-4215-b989-e78ee2ea70a1.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030022_c0b36bd0-66a3-4843-bf8a-9e1c94564d6f.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030022_7d5b1671-f295-4032-9d8b-e93e533797a9.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030023_9b46bef7-175f-4409-9d15-7f634bbcc7c4.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030024_b9297854-9aa8-4824-bcac-119e280d228b.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030024_3806831e-46df-42ca-ae8c-d6fb0e8d4623.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "04", "title": "Борьба за нож на кухне, один дубль", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["7", "7", "7", "8", "7"], "task": "ok so um I'm making a short film for my film class at community college and I kinda want to try the AI thing for one shot because we don't have the budget to do stunts obviously, so what I need is like a knife fight, two women, in a cramped little apartment kitchen, it's like the climax of the story, one of them is the main character, she's like late twenties, messy ponytail, gray hoodie, and the other one is this older woman in a black coat who broke in, and um they're fighting over the knife more than like slashing at each other, you know, grabbing wrists, slamming into the counter, a plate breaks, the fridge door swings open and the fridge light is the only light, and it should feel really desperate and close, kind of like those long one-take fight scenes in those gritty spy shows where the camera just doesn't cut, and it should be about fifteen seconds, and at the end the main character gets the knife and just backs away breathing hard. could you write me a prompt for that? thanks", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste into most AI video tools (Sora, Runway, Kling, Veo, etc.):\n\n---\n\n**Prompt:**\n\nGritty, handheld, single continuous take with no cuts, 15 seconds. A cramped, cluttered apartment kitchen at night, almost completely dark. The only light comes from an open refrigerator, casting a cold blue-white glow and harsh shadows across the narrow space.\n\nTwo women struggle desperately over a single kitchen knife. The first woman is in her late twenties, with a messy brown ponytail and a worn gray hoodie, frightened but determined. The second woman is older, in her fifties, wearing a long black coat, cold and relentless. They are locked together at close quarters, both gripping the knife and each other's wrists, pushing and twisting rather than slashing. They stumble and slam hard into the kitchen counter, and a plate falls and shatters on the floor. One of them crashes into the refrigerator door, swinging it wider, and the light sweeps across their faces.\n\nThe camera stays tight and close, shoulder-mounted and slightly shaky, moving with the struggle and pushing in and pulling back like a long-take fight scene in a gritty spy drama.\n\nIn the final seconds, the woman in the gray hoodie wrenches the knife free and stumbles backward, away from the older woman. She holds the knife low and unsteady, chest heaving, breathing hard. The camera holds on her face, lit only by the fridge light.\n\nStyle: realistic, 35mm film grain, desaturated, high contrast, low-key lighting, tense and claustrophobic.\n\n---\n\n**Negative prompt** (if your tool has one):\ncuts, scene changes, bright lighting, slow motion, cartoonish, extra limbs, distorted hands, extra people, text, watermark\n\n**Tips:**\n\n- **Length:** A lot of tools cap clips at 5 to 10 seconds. If yours does, split the scene into two prompts, the struggle and then the knife grab and back-away, using the same character descriptions word-for-word in both. Or use the tool's \"extend\" feature.\n- **Hands:** AI still struggles with grappling and hands gripping objects, so expect to generate several takes. Fast motion and darkness actually help hide glitches, so the fridge lighting works in your favor.\n- **Filters:** If the tool blocks it, try \"struggle over a kitchen knife\" instead of \"knife fight.\" Your framing (fighting *over* the knife, not slashing) is already pretty filter-friendly.\n- **Sound:** Most tools won't give you good audio, so add breathing, grunts, the plate smash, and the fridge hum in post. That'll sell the desperation more than anything.\n- **Matching:** If you're cutting this into live-action footage, put your actual actors' looks in the descriptions (hair color, build, the actual hoodie) so it doesn't feel jarring.\n\nGood luck with the film!", "prompt": "Gritty, handheld, single continuous take with no cuts, 15 seconds. A cramped, cluttered apartment kitchen at night, almost completely dark. The only light comes from an open refrigerator, casting a cold blue-white glow and harsh shadows across the narrow space.\n\nTwo women struggle desperately over a single kitchen knife. The first woman is in her late twenties, with a messy brown ponytail and a worn gray hoodie, frightened but determined. The second woman is older, in her fifties, wearing a long black coat, cold and relentless. They are locked together at close quarters, both gripping the knife and each other's wrists, pushing and twisting rather than slashing. They stumble and slam hard into the kitchen counter, and a plate falls and shatters on the floor. One of them crashes into the refrigerator door, swinging it wider, and the light sweeps across their faces.\n\nThe camera stays tight and close, shoulder-mounted and slightly shaky, moving with the struggle and pushing in and pulling back like a long-take fight scene in a gritty spy drama.\n\nIn the final seconds, the woman in the gray hoodie wrenches the knife free and stumbles backward, away from the older woman. She holds the knife low and unsteady, chest heaving, breathing hard. The camera holds on her face, lit only by the fridge light.\n\nStyle: realistic, 35mm film grain, desaturated, high contrast, low-key lighting, tense and claustrophobic.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030110_63280230-9e1c-4b72-b557-f6f654d7f227.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030110_a6a6e5d5-1d02-4ab4-9aeb-aec6f5c0c15f.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030111_7d21a595-bab0-436e-a4ad-c3c08a9f00c9.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030112_9b4a2168-4976-430c-857b-5d2beb4b508b.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030112_ed44bd11-78cb-4274-bbdd-328f8c6a4688.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030113_5b8b54ff-fd67-4822-8143-a5d456b5c216.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-04-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Монах против 8 ниндзя на крыше", "total": "4,8", "scores": ["5", "4", "5", "5", "5"], "task": "can u write me a promt for a 15 sec video?? kung fu monk vs like 8 ninjas on a rooftop in the rain, neon city at night behind them. monk uses a wooden staff and takes them all out one by one, slow mo on a couple hits w/ water spraying off. want it to look like a anime fight but real life, like those live action anime trailers. its for my gaming discord banner vid lol", "answer": "## Main Prompt (copy/paste)\n\n> Cinematic live-action anime style fight scene, 15 seconds. Night rooftop in heavy rain, glowing neon cyberpunk city skyline in the background with pink, cyan, and purple signs reflecting in puddles. A calm, focused kung fu monk in soaked orange robes wields a wooden bo staff, surrounded by 8 ninjas in black. The ninjas attack and the monk takes them out one by one with fast, precise, spinning staff strikes. Two key hits are in dramatic slow motion, with rain droplets and water spraying off the staff and bodies on impact, droplets frozen mid-air. Dynamic camera: low angles, orbiting shots, quick whip pans. Anime-inspired framing and poses, strong neon rim lighting, high contrast, wet reflective surfaces, shallow depth of field, film grain, 24fps. Feels like a live-action anime movie trailer. Ends with the monk standing alone in the rain, staff planted, defeated ninjas around him, neon city glowing behind.\n\n## Timestamped Version (if your generator handles shot lists)\n\n- **0–2s:** Wide shot. Monk stands center, ninjas circle him in the rain, lightning flash lights up the skyline.\n- **2–5s:** First ninjas rush in. Fast staff spins, quick cuts, splashing puddles.\n- **5–7s:** **SLOW MO.** Staff cracks into a ninja, a burst of water sprays off the impact.\n- **7–11s:** Rapid combo, monk takes down several ninjas, camera whips around him.\n- **11–13s:** **SLOW MO.** Jumping overhead strike, rain frozen in the air, neon glinting off the droplets.\n- **13–15s:** Hero shot. Monk lands, plants staff, camera slowly pulls back as the rain keeps falling.\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Clip length:** A lot of AI video tools cap at 5–10 seconds. If yours does, generate 2–3 clips using the timestamp sections and stitch them together.\n- **Too many ninjas:** AI often messes up 8 separate fighters. If it gets chaotic, try \"ninjas emerging from the shadows\" so they're not all on screen at once.\n- **Discord cropping:** Banners get cropped, so ask for the monk to stay centered in frame.\n- **If it looks too fake**, add: *\"photorealistic, practical effects, real actors, Hollywood stunt choreography.\"*\n\nWant a shorter version for tools with a character limit?", "prompt": "Cinematic live-action anime style fight scene, 15 seconds. Night rooftop in heavy rain, glowing neon cyberpunk city skyline in the background with pink, cyan, and purple signs reflecting in puddles. A calm, focused kung fu monk in soaked orange robes wields a wooden bo staff, surrounded by 8 ninjas in black. The ninjas attack and the monk takes them out one by one with fast, precise, spinning staff strikes. Two key hits are in dramatic slow motion, with rain droplets and water spraying off the staff and bodies on impact, droplets frozen mid-air. Dynamic camera: low angles, orbiting shots, quick whip pans. Anime-inspired framing and poses, strong neon rim lighting, high contrast, wet reflective surfaces, shallow depth of field, film grain, 24fps. Feels like a live-action anime movie trailer. Ends with the monk standing alone in the rain, staff planted, defeated ninjas around him, neon city glowing behind.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030157_3aed202b-42b1-415f-aac4-d14555058000.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030158_73b779ff-e56d-4fcf-86d1-5fac764f083e.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030159_9ba6dfc0-552a-4155-9ae2-285200fe0435.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030159_0f73ae54-938a-4002-adea-3fe01289c421.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030200_39784cbb-f44a-4aa7-90a0-98b47f5ba1cc.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030201_de87d8fd-9035-4bbe-af07-efba038f6dae.mp4", "poster": "posters/fighting-05-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}]}, {"id": "talking-head", "name": "Talking Head", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "Студия ресниц, бьюти-креатор, 9:16", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "7", "6", "7", "8"], "task": "hey! so i run a little lash studio in Scottsdale called Velvet Wink and I want a short AI video for my Instagram Reels and TikTok, vertical obviously. like 15 seconds max.\n\nit should be me basically, or a girl who looks like me lol — late 20s, long dark wavy hair, gold hoops, cream knit top, really natural glowy makeup but the lashes are the star. she's sitting in a bright pretty studio with a pink neon sign behind her (blurry is fine) and a ring light vibe.\n\nshe talks straight to camera, super friendly like a bestie giving you the tea. here's what she says:\n\n\"Okay real talk — if you're still gluing on strip lashes every morning, stop. Book a lash fill at Velvet Wink, wake up looking done, and get ten percent off your first set this month. Link's in bio, babe!\"\n\ni want it to feel like those get-ready-with-me creators, kinda casual handheld, a little hair flip at the end and a wink. can you write me the prompt for the video generator? thank uuu", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste right into your video generator:\n\n---\n\n**PROMPT:**\n\nVertical 9:16 video, 15 seconds, casual handheld smartphone footage in the style of a TikTok get-ready-with-me beauty creator.\n\n**Subject:** A woman in her late 20s with long, dark, voluminous wavy hair, gold hoop earrings, and a soft cream chunky-knit top. Natural, dewy, glowy makeup with luminous skin, a soft nude lip, and minimal eyeshadow. Her full, fluffy, wispy eyelash extensions are the clear focal point. Warm, confident, playful energy, like a best friend spilling the tea.\n\n**Setting:** A bright, airy, modern lash studio in soft white and blush-pink tones. Behind her, a pink neon sign glows softly out of focus with shallow depth of field and dreamy bokeh. Soft, even ring-light illumination on her face, with circular catchlights visible in her eyes.\n\n**Camera:** Medium close-up from mid-chest up, eye level, held at arm's length like a selfie. Subtle natural handheld sway and micro-movements. Sharp focus on her eyes and lashes.\n\n**Action & timing:**\n- 0–2s: She leans into frame with raised eyebrows and a \"girl, listen\" expression.\n- 2–11s: She talks directly to camera with animated, expressive delivery and small hand gestures. She gives a quick lash flutter on \"wake up looking done.\"\n- 11–13s: She points down toward the bottom of the frame on \"link's in bio.\"\n- 13–15s: She does a playful hair flip over her shoulder and ends with a wink and a smile at the lens.\n\n**Dialogue (lip-synced, upbeat, conversational, warm and a little sassy):**\n\"Okay real talk — if you're still gluing on strip lashes every morning, stop. Book a lash fill at Velvet Wink, wake up looking done, and get ten percent off your first set this month. Link's in bio, babe!\"\n\n**Audio:** Clear, close-mic'd voice with light room tone and a soft trendy pop beat at low volume underneath.\n\n**Avoid:** on-screen text or captions, legible writing on the neon sign, clumpy or spidery lashes, heavy glam makeup, distorted hands or extra fingers, warped earrings, cinematic camera moves.\n\n---\n\n**If your generator caps clips at 8 seconds** (a lot of them do), split it into two clips with the exact same subject/setting description:\n- **Clip 1:** intro lean-in + \"Okay real talk — if you're still gluing on strip lashes every morning, stop. Book a lash fill at Velvet Wink,\"\n- **Clip 2:** \"wake up looking done, and get ten percent off your first set this month. Link's in bio, babe!\" + hair flip and wink\n\n**A few quick tips:**\n\n1. **Script check:** Someone coming from strip lashes would need a *full set* first, since a fill is for people who already have extensions. You might tweak it to: *\"Book your first full set at Velvet Wink, wake up looking done, and get ten percent off this month.\"* It's also a little shorter, which helps with timing.\n2. **Make her look like you:** If your tool supports image-to-video or a reference image, upload a selfie. That also keeps her consistent across two clips.\n3. **Add your branding in editing:** AI tends to scramble text, which is why the sign is blurry in the prompt. Drop your logo, the offer, and captions in CapCut afterward. Most people scroll with sound off anyway.\n4. **Label it as AI:** Instagram and TikTok both ask you to tag realistic AI-generated content, and there's a toggle when you post. Skipping it can get the video flagged or its reach limited.\n\nGood luck with it! 💖", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 video, 15 seconds, casual handheld smartphone footage in the style of a TikTok get-ready-with-me beauty creator.\n\n**Subject:** A woman in her late 20s with long, dark, voluminous wavy hair, gold hoop earrings, and a soft cream chunky-knit top. Natural, dewy, glowy makeup with luminous skin, a soft nude lip, and minimal eyeshadow. Her full, fluffy, wispy eyelash extensions are the clear focal point. Warm, confident, playful energy, like a best friend spilling the tea.\n\n**Setting:** A bright, airy, modern lash studio in soft white and blush-pink tones. Behind her, a pink neon sign glows softly out of focus with shallow depth of field and dreamy bokeh. Soft, even ring-light illumination on her face, with circular catchlights visible in her eyes.\n\n**Camera:** Medium close-up from mid-chest up, eye level, held at arm's length like a selfie. Subtle natural handheld sway and micro-movements. Sharp focus on her eyes and lashes.\n\n**Action & timing:**\n- 0–2s: She leans into frame with raised eyebrows and a \"girl, listen\" expression.\n- 2–11s: She talks directly to camera with animated, expressive delivery and small hand gestures. She gives a quick lash flutter on \"wake up looking done.\"\n- 11–13s: She points down toward the bottom of the frame on \"link's in bio.\"\n- 13–15s: She does a playful hair flip over her shoulder and ends with a wink and a smile at the lens.\n\n**Dialogue (lip-synced, upbeat, conversational, warm and a little sassy):**\n\"Okay real talk — if you're still gluing on strip lashes every morning, stop. Book a lash fill at Velvet Wink, wake up looking done, and get ten percent off your first set this month. Link's in bio, babe!\"\n\n**Audio:** Clear, close-mic'd voice with light room tone and a soft trendy pop beat at low volume underneath.\n\n**Avoid:** on-screen text or captions, legible writing on the neon sign, clumpy or spidery lashes, heavy glam makeup, distorted hands or extra fingers, warped earrings, cinematic camera moves.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030324_2c77b525-dd55-4131-9000-d163e14de536.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030325_adcdd777-db52-4131-9f99-da851a38a73b.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030326_123ce64a-ea15-4b97-a013-8d5541f31b14.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030327_7c30fdb0-175e-46a3-bb44-29454829d454.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030327_86e14b69-6759-4288-a077-8dbbffbfb833.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030328_b95a5f66-cd8c-4eaf-afa5-fecc5486092a.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "02", "title": "Врач, напоминание о прививке", "total": "7,8", "scores": ["8", "8", "7", "9", "7"], "task": "Hello,\n\nI am a family physician with a small practice in Columbus, Ohio (Brightfield Family Medicine). Our office would like to add a short video to the homepage of our website reminding patients about flu shots. I have been told that an AI tool can create the video if I give it a good written description, and I would appreciate it if you could write that description for me.\n\nDetails:\n- Length: about 15 seconds.\n- Speaker: a woman doctor in her mid-50s, short gray hair, reading glasses pushed up on her head, white coat over a light blue blouse, stethoscope around her neck. Warm and reassuring, not salesy.\n- Setting: a clean, sunny exam room with a window, a few plants, and a framed diploma on the wall slightly out of focus.\n- She should speak directly to the camera, calmly, and maybe smile at the end.\n\nHer words:\n\"Flu season is here, and the shot is still the best way to protect you and the people you love. It takes five minutes, and most insurance covers it. Call us or stop by Brightfield Family Medicine — we'll take good care of you.\"\n\nPlease keep it professional and trustworthy. I do not want anything that looks like a commercial on late-night television.\n\nThank you very much,\nDr. Karen Lindqvist", "answer": "# Flu Shot Video Description for Brightfield Family Medicine\n\nHere is a description you can copy and paste directly into the AI video tool.\n\n```\nA 15-second, photorealistic video of a family physician speaking directly to the camera in her exam room. The tone is calm, sincere, and reassuring, like a trusted doctor speaking to one patient. It should not look or feel like an advertisement.\n\nSUBJECT: A woman in her mid-50s with short gray hair and reading glasses pushed up on top of her head. She wears a clean white doctor's coat over a light blue blouse, with a stethoscope around her neck. Natural, approachable appearance with realistic skin texture and minimal makeup. She stands relaxed and at ease, facing the camera.\n\nSETTING: A clean, bright, uncluttered exam room on a sunny day. A window to one side lets in soft natural daylight. A few healthy green potted plants sit near the window. A framed diploma hangs on the wall behind her, softly out of focus. Light, neutral wall colors. Tidy and calm.\n\nCAMERA: Static, eye-level medium close-up, framed from mid-chest up, with the doctor slightly off-center so part of the room is visible behind her. Shallow depth of field: she is in sharp focus and the background is gently blurred. No zooms, no cuts, no camera movement.\n\nLIGHTING: Soft, natural window light with gentle fill. Warm but realistic colors. No harsh shadows and no glossy studio look.\n\nPERFORMANCE: She makes steady, natural eye contact with the camera and speaks at a calm, unhurried, conversational pace with natural pauses. Her expressions are subtle and genuine, with minimal hand movement. After her last line, she gives a warm, gentle smile and holds it for about one second.\n\nDIALOGUE (clear speech, accurate lip sync):\n\"Flu season is here, and the shot is still the best way to protect you and the people you love. It takes five minutes, and most insurance covers it. Call us or stop by Brightfield Family Medicine — we'll take good care of you.\"\n\nAUDIO: Clean, clear voice with quiet, natural room tone. No background music and no sound effects.\n\nSTYLE: Natural, documentary-like realism, similar to a genuine physician welcome video on a medical practice website. Muted, natural color grading.\n\nAVOID: On-screen text, captions, logos, or graphics; legible text on the diploma; dramatic or upbeat music; flashy transitions; exaggerated or overly wide smiles; pointing at the camera; salesperson energy; a stock-photo or commercial look.\n```\n\n## Practical Notes\n\n**1. Timing.** Your script is about 43 words, which takes roughly 17–18 seconds at a calm pace. You can either accept the slightly longer video or trim the last line, since viewers will already be on your website:\n\n> \"Flu season is here, and the shot is still the best way to protect you and the people you love. It takes five minutes, and most insurance covers it. Call or stop by — we'll take good care of you.\"\n\nThat version fits comfortably in about 15 seconds.\n\n**2. Clip length limits.** Many AI video tools only generate 8–10 seconds at a time. If yours does, create two clips using the same description. Split the dialogue after \"...the people you love.\" Keeping the description identical helps the doctor and room look consistent between clips.\n\n**3. Add text afterward.** AI tools often misspell words that appear in the video. It is better to add your practice name, phone number, or logo in a simple editing program afterward.\n\n**4. Captions.** Many people browse websites with the sound off, so consider adding subtitles. They also help patients with hearing difficulties.\n\n**5. Review carefully before posting.** Watch for common AI errors: lip movements that don't match the words, unusual-looking hands, glasses that change shape, or a stethoscope that shifts position. Generating three or four versions and choosing the best one usually works well.\n\n**6. Transparency.** Patients may assume the doctor in the video is a member of your staff. A small note such as \"AI-generated video\" would support the trustworthy tone you're aiming for.", "prompt": "A 15-second, photorealistic video of a family physician speaking directly to the camera in her exam room. The tone is calm, sincere, and reassuring, like a trusted doctor speaking to one patient. It should not look or feel like an advertisement.\n\nSUBJECT: A woman in her mid-50s with short gray hair and reading glasses pushed up on top of her head. She wears a clean white doctor's coat over a light blue blouse, with a stethoscope around her neck. Natural, approachable appearance with realistic skin texture and minimal makeup. She stands relaxed and at ease, facing the camera.\n\nSETTING: A clean, bright, uncluttered exam room on a sunny day. A window to one side lets in soft natural daylight. A few healthy green potted plants sit near the window. A framed diploma hangs on the wall behind her, softly out of focus. Light, neutral wall colors. Tidy and calm.\n\nCAMERA: Static, eye-level medium close-up, framed from mid-chest up, with the doctor slightly off-center so part of the room is visible behind her. Shallow depth of field: she is in sharp focus and the background is gently blurred. No zooms, no cuts, no camera movement.\n\nLIGHTING: Soft, natural window light with gentle fill. Warm but realistic colors. No harsh shadows and no glossy studio look.\n\nPERFORMANCE: She makes steady, natural eye contact with the camera and speaks at a calm, unhurried, conversational pace with natural pauses. Her expressions are subtle and genuine, with minimal hand movement. After her last line, she gives a warm, gentle smile and holds it for about one second.\n\nDIALOGUE (clear speech, accurate lip sync):\n\"Flu season is here, and the shot is still the best way to protect you and the people you love. It takes five minutes, and most insurance covers it. Call us or stop by Brightfield Family Medicine — we'll take good care of you.\"\n\nAUDIO: Clean, clear voice with quiet, natural room tone. No background music and no sound effects.\n\nSTYLE: Natural, documentary-like realism, similar to a genuine physician welcome video on a medical practice website. Muted, natural color grading.\n\nAVOID: On-screen text, captions, logos, or graphics; legible text on the diploma; dramatic or upbeat music; flashy transitions; exaggerated or overly wide smiles; pointing at the camera; salesperson energy; a stock-photo or commercial look.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030431_415f6da5-45ba-40cf-b6c4-abe8a777871f.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030432_a6ed8e89-e11b-46d7-88d6-ec033b49b077.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030433_8ca9946b-65fe-4c7e-b490-8f13dbef56e2.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030434_fa43f239-5c8e-4ed0-be77-5f85ef9f6ed7.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030434_4830c7e3-608c-403a-bfab-396bbf16cf9e.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030435_cff89a1d-4af7-4c59-b069-bd69427e0d0f.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "03", "title": "Интро хоррор-стримера GraveShift", "total": "7,8", "scores": ["8", "8", "8", "8", "7"], "task": "ok so I'm just gonna talk this out, I'm driving, bear with me. So I stream on Twitch, mostly horror games, late night stuff, my channel's called GraveShift, and I want a little intro clip, like fifteen seconds, that plays before I go live, kind of a cold open. And I want it to be a guy that's like me, early twenties, kind of skinny, messy black hair, oversized black hoodie with the hood half up, big headphones around his neck, and he's sitting at a gaming desk in a dark room, the only light is like the monitor glow, blue and kind of a sickly green, and maybe some red LED strips behind him. And I want it to feel like the opening of Stranger Things or like one of those found footage movies, kind of creepy, a little flicker in the light, a little grain. And he leans into the camera real slow, like he's telling you a secret, and he goes, uh, \"It's three a.m. You should be asleep. But you're not... and neither am I. Welcome to the GraveShift.\" And then he kind of smirks and the monitor behind him glitches out, like the lights cut for a second. I don't need text or a logo or anything, I'll add that myself. Can you write me the prompt I'd put in the AI video thing to get that? Make it actually good, I've tried before and it came out looking like a cheesy ad.", "answer": "Here's a prompt built to avoid the glossy commercial look. Grab it when you're parked.\n\n```\nFound-footage style cold open, like a grainy 1980s horror film transfer mixed with a late-night webcam recording. Static camera at desk height, slightly below eye level, 35mm lens, shallow depth of field.\n\nA skinny man in his early twenties with messy black hair sits at a gaming desk in a pitch-dark bedroom. He wears an oversized black hoodie with the hood pulled halfway up and large over-ear headphones resting around his neck. His face is lit only by an off-screen computer monitor in front of him, casting cold blue and sickly green light. Behind him, dim red LED strips glow along the wall, and a second monitor is visible over his shoulder showing a dark, murky game screen. Most of the room is lost in deep shadow.\n\nLook: heavy film grain, subtle flicker in the monitor light, soft halation around the red LEDs, crushed blacks, muted and slightly desaturated color, faint VHS softness. Realistic and naturalistic, not stylized.\n\nAction: He sits still for a beat, staring just past the lens. Then he slowly leans toward the camera until his face fills more of the frame, eyes catching the green glow. He speaks quietly, low and deadpan, almost a whisper, like he's telling a secret: \"It's three a.m. You should be asleep. But you're not...\" He pauses. \"...and neither am I. Welcome to the Grave Shift.\" A slight, knowing smirk. Then the monitor behind him glitches: the image tears and stutters, and every light in the room cuts to total black for a split second before flickering back on.\n\nAudio: low room tone, faint computer fan hum, his voice close and intimate, an electrical buzz and crackle during the glitch, then silence. No music.\n\nNo text, no logos, no subtitles, no watermark.\n```\n\n**Negative prompt** (if your tool has one):\n```\ncommercial, advertisement, glossy, polished, bright lighting, beauty lighting, oversaturated, stock footage, exaggerated expression, theatrical acting, wide smile, text, logo\n```\n\n**A few tips:**\n- **Length:** Many tools cap at 8 to 10 seconds. If yours does, split it into two clips. Clip 1 is the lean-in and \"You should be asleep.\" Clip 2 is \"But you're not...\" through the glitch. Keep the description identical in both so he looks the same.\n- **Why it looked cheesy before:** Words like \"cinematic,\" \"epic,\" or \"4K\" push tools toward ad-style polish. Describing flaws like grain, flicker, and darkness works better. \"Deadpan\" also keeps him from overacting.\n- **\"Grave Shift\" as two words** helps the voice pronounce it right.\n- **I put the main monitor off-screen** so it lights his face, with a second one behind him to do the glitch. That way both parts of your idea work in one shot.\n- **To make him look like you,** use image-to-video with a photo of yourself in the hoodie, if your tool supports it.", "prompt": "Found-footage style cold open, like a grainy 1980s horror film transfer mixed with a late-night webcam recording. Static camera at desk height, slightly below eye level, 35mm lens, shallow depth of field.\n\nA skinny man in his early twenties with messy black hair sits at a gaming desk in a pitch-dark bedroom. He wears an oversized black hoodie with the hood pulled halfway up and large over-ear headphones resting around his neck. His face is lit only by an off-screen computer monitor in front of him, casting cold blue and sickly green light. Behind him, dim red LED strips glow along the wall, and a second monitor is visible over his shoulder showing a dark, murky game screen. Most of the room is lost in deep shadow.\n\nLook: heavy film grain, subtle flicker in the monitor light, soft halation around the red LEDs, crushed blacks, muted and slightly desaturated color, faint VHS softness. Realistic and naturalistic, not stylized.\n\nAction: He sits still for a beat, staring just past the lens. Then he slowly leans toward the camera until his face fills more of the frame, eyes catching the green glow. He speaks quietly, low and deadpan, almost a whisper, like he's telling a secret: \"It's three a.m. You should be asleep. But you're not...\" He pauses. \"...and neither am I. Welcome to the Grave Shift.\" A slight, knowing smirk. Then the monitor behind him glitches: the image tears and stutters, and every light in the room cuts to total black for a split second before flickering back on.\n\nAudio: low room tone, faint computer fan hum, his voice close and intimate, an electrical buzz and crackle during the glitch, then silence. No music.\n\nNo text, no logos, no subtitles, no watermark.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030521_a5fa3c74-374e-4b01-8752-b714d5c05fd8.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030522_fd8ba8f6-0292-4f8a-8953-69053bd2b810.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030522_bc868544-83f5-45a7-ba35-343fa832ee65.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030523_033de20b-e0cd-4416-ada7-5f6418f68f76.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030524_07d8d0dd-3382-42e3-8ffc-8230b2065806.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030525_d7d7be36-965a-4834-9a5b-a720b4d9198a.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "04", "title": "Риелтор на крыльце фермерского дома", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "7", "7", "7", "7"], "task": "need a prompt for an ai video gen. 15 sec-ish. real estate.\n\nguy is me basically - 40s, bald, trimmed salt n pepper beard, navy quarter zip, khakis. friendly but not cheesy. he's standing on the front porch of a white farmhouse style house, wraparound porch, big oak tree, late afternoon sun, golden. maybe camera slowly pushes in on him while he talks\n\nhe says: \"Hey y'all, Travis Hale with Red Mesa Realty. This one just hit the market in Georgetown — four beds, big yard, and a porch made for sweet tea. Won't last long. Give me a call and let's get you home.\"\n\nwant it to feel kinda like those home reno shows on tv, warm and homey. its going on fb and my website so no need for the vertical thing. thx", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste in:\n\n```\nCinematic 16:9 real estate video, warm and inviting, styled like an HGTV home renovation show. Golden hour, late afternoon.\n\nSCENE: A man in his 40s stands on the front porch of a white modern farmhouse with a wraparound porch, black-framed windows, wooden posts, and a couple of rocking chairs. A large, mature oak tree in the front yard casts dappled light across the lawn. He is bald with a neatly trimmed salt-and-pepper beard, wearing a navy quarter-zip pullover and khaki pants. Relaxed, confident posture. Genuine, easygoing smile. Friendly and approachable, not salesy.\n\nCAMERA: Opens on a medium-wide shot showing the man, porch, and front of the house. Slow, smooth dolly push-in, ending on a waist-up medium shot. Gimbal-stable, shallow depth of field, softly blurred background.\n\nLIGHTING & LOOK: Warm golden sunlight from the side, subtle lens flare through the oak leaves, natural skin tones, rich warm color grade.\n\nACTION: He looks directly into the camera and speaks naturally in a light, friendly Texas accent. Small, natural hand gestures, including a casual open-hand gesture toward the porch when he mentions it.\n\nDIALOGUE: \"Hey y'all, Travis Hale with Red Mesa Realty. This one just hit the market in Georgetown. Four beds, big yard, and a porch made for sweet tea. Won't last long. Give me a call and let's get you home.\"\n\nAUDIO: Clear dialogue, soft birdsong, a light breeze rustling the oak leaves, and quiet acoustic guitar music low in the background.\n\nAVOID: On-screen text or captions, distorted hands, exaggerated facial expressions, over-the-top grin.\n```\n\n**A few tips:**\n\n- **To make it actually look like you,** use the tool's image-to-video or character reference feature and upload a clear photo of yourself. With text alone you'll get a random bald guy.\n- **Check the clip length limit.** Your script runs about 11 to 12 seconds spoken. If your generator caps at 8 to 10 seconds, split it into two clips with the same prompt and cut them together:\n  - Clip 1: \"Hey y'all, Travis Hale with Red Mesa Realty. This one just hit the market in Georgetown. Four beds, big yard, and a porch made for sweet tea.\"\n  - Clip 2: \"Won't last long. Give me a call and let's get you home.\" (Start this one already pushed in close so the cut feels natural.)\n- **Add your logo, phone number, and website in editing afterward.** AI video tends to garble text.", "prompt": "Cinematic 16:9 real estate video, warm and inviting, styled like an HGTV home renovation show. Golden hour, late afternoon.\n\nSCENE: A man in his 40s stands on the front porch of a white modern farmhouse with a wraparound porch, black-framed windows, wooden posts, and a couple of rocking chairs. A large, mature oak tree in the front yard casts dappled light across the lawn. He is bald with a neatly trimmed salt-and-pepper beard, wearing a navy quarter-zip pullover and khaki pants. Relaxed, confident posture. Genuine, easygoing smile. Friendly and approachable, not salesy.\n\nCAMERA: Opens on a medium-wide shot showing the man, porch, and front of the house. Slow, smooth dolly push-in, ending on a waist-up medium shot. Gimbal-stable, shallow depth of field, softly blurred background.\n\nLIGHTING & LOOK: Warm golden sunlight from the side, subtle lens flare through the oak leaves, natural skin tones, rich warm color grade.\n\nACTION: He looks directly into the camera and speaks naturally in a light, friendly Texas accent. Small, natural hand gestures, including a casual open-hand gesture toward the porch when he mentions it.\n\nDIALOGUE: \"Hey y'all, Travis Hale with Red Mesa Realty. This one just hit the market in Georgetown. Four beds, big yard, and a porch made for sweet tea. Won't last long. Give me a call and let's get you home.\"\n\nAUDIO: Clear dialogue, soft birdsong, a light breeze rustling the oak leaves, and quiet acoustic guitar music low in the background.\n\nAVOID: On-screen text or captions, distorted hands, exaggerated facial expressions, over-the-top grin.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["HGTV"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030608_cffe86dc-a22b-41da-874a-1928d7089c9a.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030608_80143eda-55a5-4bec-bef3-e53abf8a15a4.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030609_adf93a6b-5095-4318-a6a1-fc0181d88540.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030610_4b685b30-b56f-43b0-a481-a7079f156c68.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030612_5cf9803d-a300-4d39-8748-dd84b3a1fffe.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030613_a3e0a40a-efb4-40b6-9091-c4ec3e897c64.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-04-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Основательница стартапа, благодарность", "total": "7,0", "scores": ["7", "8", "5", "8", "7"], "task": "Hi there. I'm the co-founder of a small startup called Tidewell — we make a refillable water bottle that tracks how much you drink. We just closed our first round and I want to post a short thank-you video from \"the founder\" on LinkedIn and in our email newsletter. Honestly I hate being on camera, so I'm hoping an AI video can do it.\n\nCould you write the lines too? I just want it to sound honest and a bit humble, not like a big corporate announcement. Main points: thank our early customers, say we're hiring, and say there's a lot more coming. Should be about 15 seconds when spoken.\n\nFor the person: a woman in her early 30s, Korean American, shoulder-length black hair tucked behind one ear, no makeup look, gray crewneck sweatshirt. She's sitting on a stool in a small warehouse office — cardboard boxes, a whiteboard with messy sketches, a few of our blue bottles on a shelf behind her. Morning light coming in through a big window.\n\nI'd love it to feel like those simple documentary-style interviews you see in Apple keynote videos, or honestly like the confessional bits in The Office but serious — just someone talking to you plainly, maybe a little laugh at one point so it feels real. Thanks so much!", "answer": "# Tidewell Thank-You Video\n\n## Script (~15 seconds)\n\n> Hi, I'm [Name], co-founder of Tidewell.\n>\n> We just closed our first round, which still feels a little unreal. *[small laugh]*\n>\n> That happened because of you, our early customers. Thank you.\n>\n> We're hiring, and there's a lot more coming.\n\nThat's about 35 words, which runs 14–16 seconds at a relaxed pace with the laugh.\n\n**Alternate ending** if you want a bit more warmth:\n> *...We're hiring, so if you want to build this with us, reach out. And there's a lot more coming.*\n\n## Video Prompt\n\nYou can paste this into a tool like Veo, Sora, Runway, or Kling. For a lip-synced talking avatar, HeyGen or Synthesia may work better.\n\n```\nDocumentary-style interview shot, static tripod camera, medium close-up.\nA Korean American woman in her early 30s sits on a wooden stool, framed\nslightly off-center. Shoulder-length black hair tucked behind one ear,\nnatural no-makeup look, plain gray crewneck sweatshirt. She looks just\noff-camera, as if talking to an interviewer, occasionally glancing into\nthe lens.\n\nSetting: a small, lived-in warehouse office. Behind her, stacked\ncardboard boxes, a whiteboard covered in messy marker sketches, and a\nshelf holding a few matte blue water bottles. Soft morning sunlight\nstreams through a large window to one side, creating gentle warm light\non her face and a slight haze in the air.\n\nStyle: clean, honest, minimal, like a corporate brand documentary.\nShallow depth of field, background softly blurred. Natural color grade,\nno dramatic effects. Calm, sincere, slightly shy demeanor. She smiles\nand gives a small genuine laugh partway through.\n\nAudio: quiet room tone, no music. She speaks plainly and warmly:\n\"Hi, I'm [Name], co-founder of Tidewell. We just closed our first round,\nwhich still feels a little unreal. [small laugh] That happened because\nof you, our early customers. Thank you. We're hiring, and there's a lot\nmore coming.\"\n```\n\n## Practical Tips\n\n- **Clip length:** Some tools cap clips at 8–10 seconds. If so, split it into two shots (the thank-you, then the hiring line) and cut between them. A slight framing change between shots actually feels very documentary.\n- **Branding:** AI tends to garble logos and text, so keep the bottles unbranded in the prompt and add your logo or an end card in editing.\n- **Hands:** Avoid having her hold or gesture with a bottle. Hands are where AI video most often looks off.\n- **Generate several takes.** The small laugh is the hardest part to get natural, and it varies a lot between generations.\n\n## Before You Post\n\nIf this avatar is meant to look like you, I'd add a brief \"made with AI\" note in the caption. LinkedIn labels AI-generated content anyway, and for a message built around honesty and humility, it lands much better if people hear it from you rather than discovering it themselves. Something like *\"I'm camera-shy, so I made this with AI, but every word is mine\"* can actually come across as charming.\n\nIf the avatar isn't based on you, I'd reconsider presenting it as \"the founder.\" Customers and investors would be thanked by someone who doesn't exist, which could undercut the trust you're trying to build. A good alternative is a voiceover in your real voice over footage of your actual office and bottles, which keeps you off camera but still feels personal.", "prompt": "Documentary-style interview shot, static tripod camera, medium close-up.\nA Korean American woman in her early 30s sits on a wooden stool, framed\nslightly off-center. Shoulder-length black hair tucked behind one ear,\nnatural no-makeup look, plain gray crewneck sweatshirt. She looks just\noff-camera, as if talking to an interviewer, occasionally glancing into\nthe lens.\n\nSetting: a small, lived-in warehouse office. Behind her, stacked\ncardboard boxes, a whiteboard covered in messy marker sketches, and a\nshelf holding a few matte blue water bottles. Soft morning sunlight\nstreams through a large window to one side, creating gentle warm light\non her face and a slight haze in the air.\n\nStyle: clean, honest, minimal, like a corporate brand documentary.\nShallow depth of field, background softly blurred. Natural color grade,\nno dramatic effects. Calm, sincere, slightly shy demeanor. She smiles\nand gives a small genuine laugh partway through.\n\nAudio: quiet room tone, no music. She speaks plainly and warmly:\n\"Hi, I'm [Name], co-founder of Tidewell. We just closed our first round,\nwhich still feels a little unreal. [small laugh] That happened because\nof you, our early customers. Thank you. We're hiring, and there's a lot\nmore coming.\"", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030658_294f14f4-5c09-4b1f-9d7e-dc10fc2300cd.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030659_94aa97b1-3e19-4fd6-9ab2-407fb4f1ef15.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030700_ed578b98-4157-4ebc-bca1-023ff884ed24.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030701_224ca62b-1976-4bdf-a22e-2d844947cce8.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030701_22298157-48fc-40b8-b4cb-1c9d8ea523e7.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_030702_4975ff35-8a7c-4587-b088-84279327bd48.mp4", "poster": "posters/talking-head-05-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}]}, {"id": "dialogue", "name": "Dramatic Dialogue", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "Расставание в машине под дождём, 9:16", "total": "7,4", "scores": ["8", "6", "8", "8", "7"], "task": "hey so i need help writing a prompt for one of those ai video generators. i want a breakup scene, like super raw, think that one episode of Euphoria where everything is lit purple and everyone's crying in a car lol\n\ntwo college kids, maybe 20, sitting in a parked car outside a dorm at night. rain on the windshield, streetlight coming through. the girl (Maya) has her hands in her sleeves and won't look at him. the guy (Jordan) keeps trying to get her to look at him.\n\nlines:\nJordan: \"just tell me what i did. please.\"\nMaya: \"you didn't do anything. that's kind of the problem.\"\nJordan: \"...what does that even mean\"\nMaya: \"it means i stopped waiting for you to show up.\"\n\nthen she opens the door and gets out and he just sits there with the rain. should be like 15 sec total. vertical bc its going on my tiktok for my film class account. make it look real not like a cheesy lifetime movie pls", "answer": "Here's a prompt built for that raw, Euphoria-style look. It's written for generators that handle dialogue and audio (like Veo 3, Sora, or Kling with audio). Split versions are below in case your tool caps clip length.\n\n---\n\n## Full Prompt (~15 sec, 9:16 vertical)\n\n> Vertical 9:16 cinematic shot, 35mm film look with visible grain, naturalistic indie-film acting. Night, interior of a parked older sedan outside a college dorm. Heavy rain streams down the windshield. A warm orange streetlight and a soft purple-magenta glow from outside filter through the wet glass, casting moving rain-droplet shadows across both faces. Dashboard lights off. Intimate, hushed, still.\n> \n> Camera mounted low on the dashboard facing back toward them, slightly off-center, both faces in frame, very slow subtle push-in. Shallow depth of field.\n> \n> **Maya**, 20, passenger seat, messy dark hair, oversized gray hoodie, sleeves pulled over her hands, knees angled toward the door. She stares out the side window and won't look at him.\n> **Jordan**, 20, driver's seat, short dark hair, worn denim jacket, turned toward her, leaning in, trying to catch her eyes.\n> \n> Jordan (quiet, voice cracking): \"just tell me what i did. please.\"\n> Maya (flat, still looking away): \"you didn't do anything. that's kind of the problem.\"\n> Jordan (beat, confused, hurt): \"...what does that even mean\"\n> Maya (soft, almost a whisper): \"it means i stopped waiting for you to show up.\"\n> \n> She opens the passenger door. Rain noise floods in. She steps out and shuts it. Hold on Jordan alone, staring at the empty seat, rain sliding down the glass. He doesn't move.\n> \n> Audio: rain drumming on the roof, muffled distant traffic, no music. Dialogue low and natural with real pauses and breaths.\n> \n> Style: Euphoria-inspired color grade, deep purples and magentas against warm sodium orange, soft halation around lights, raw and unpolished like an A24 film. Understated performances. No melodrama, no exaggerated crying, no glossy TV lighting, no slow motion.\n\n---\n\n## Split Version (if your generator maxes at 8–10 sec)\n\nKeep the character and lighting descriptions **word-for-word identical** in both prompts so the characters stay consistent.\n\n**Clip 1 (~9 sec):** Same setup and style as above, but only the four lines of dialogue. End on Maya's last line.\n\n**Clip 2 (~6 sec):**\n> [same setting, lighting, characters, style]. Maya opens the passenger door, rain noise floods in, she gets out and shuts it without looking back. Hold on Jordan alone in the driver's seat, staring at the empty passenger seat, rain on the windshield, purple and orange light on his face. He doesn't move. Only rain sound.\n\n---\n\n## Tips\n\n- **Four lines in ~10 seconds is tight.** If the AI rushes the delivery, cut \"...what does that even mean\" down to just \"...what?\" for breathing room.\n- **AI audio can sound off.** For a film class, recording your own voice actors and laying the audio over a silent generation often looks more intentional and less uncanny.\n- **The cheesy stuff usually comes from words like \"emotional,\" \"heartbroken,\" or \"tearful.\"** Keep describing *actions* (won't look at him, sleeves over hands) instead of feelings. That's what keeps it from going Lifetime.\n- **Generate a few versions.** Rain shadows and faces vary a lot between runs, so pick the take where the acting feels most natural.", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 cinematic shot, 35mm film look with visible grain, naturalistic indie-film acting. Night, interior of a parked older sedan outside a college dorm. Heavy rain streams down the windshield. A warm orange streetlight and a soft purple-magenta glow from outside filter through the wet glass, casting moving rain-droplet shadows across both faces. Dashboard lights off. Intimate, hushed, still.\n\nCamera mounted low on the dashboard facing back toward them, slightly off-center, both faces in frame, very slow subtle push-in. Shallow depth of field.\n\n**Maya**, 20, passenger seat, messy dark hair, oversized gray hoodie, sleeves pulled over her hands, knees angled toward the door. She stares out the side window and won't look at him.\n**Jordan**, 20, driver's seat, short dark hair, worn denim jacket, turned toward her, leaning in, trying to catch her eyes.\n\nJordan (quiet, voice cracking): \"just tell me what i did. please.\"\nMaya (flat, still looking away): \"you didn't do anything. that's kind of the problem.\"\nJordan (beat, confused, hurt): \"...what does that even mean\"\nMaya (soft, almost a whisper): \"it means i stopped waiting for you to show up.\"\n\nShe opens the passenger door. Rain noise floods in. She steps out and shuts it. Hold on Jordan alone, staring at the empty seat, rain sliding down the glass. He doesn't move.\n\nAudio: rain drumming on the roof, muffled distant traffic, no music. Dialogue low and natural with real pauses and breaths.\n\nStyle: Euphoria-inspired color grade, deep purples and magentas against warm sodium orange, soft halation around lights, raw and unpolished like an A24 film. Understated performances. No melodrama, no exaggerated crying, no glossy TV lighting, no slow motion.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": ["Euphoria", "A24"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032221_f7a8bc64-a86c-469c-b381-62e043be8d25.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032222_d41066c4-ffad-4f33-b595-5ff0c57eecd7.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032224_5479d0b4-d394-4aa7-afb4-60545f6e33ed.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032225_269b9744-9b82-4166-bd8f-356033a7fe4b.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": {"changes": "- «Euphoria-inspired color grade» → «Moody teen-drama color grade»\n- «like an A24 film» → «like an independent arthouse film»", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 cinematic shot, 35mm film look with visible grain, naturalistic indie-film acting. Night, interior of a parked older sedan outside a college dorm. Heavy rain streams down the windshield. A warm orange streetlight and a soft purple-magenta glow from outside filter through the wet glass, casting moving rain-droplet shadows across both faces. Dashboard lights off. Intimate, hushed, still.\n\nCamera mounted low on the dashboard facing back toward them, slightly off-center, both faces in frame, very slow subtle push-in. Shallow depth of field.\n\n**Maya**, 20, passenger seat, messy dark hair, oversized gray hoodie, sleeves pulled over her hands, knees angled toward the door. She stares out the side window and won't look at him.\n**Jordan**, 20, driver's seat, short dark hair, worn denim jacket, turned toward her, leaning in, trying to catch her eyes.\n\nJordan (quiet, voice cracking): \"just tell me what i did. please.\"\nMaya (flat, still looking away): \"you didn't do anything. that's kind of the problem.\"\nJordan (beat, confused, hurt): \"...what does that even mean\"\nMaya (soft, almost a whisper): \"it means i stopped waiting for you to show up.\"\n\nShe opens the passenger door. Rain noise floods in. She steps out and shuts it. Hold on Jordan alone, staring at the empty seat, rain sliding down the glass. He doesn't move.\n\nAudio: rain drumming on the roof, muffled distant traffic, no music. Dialogue low and natural with real pauses and breaths.\n\nStyle: Moody teen-drama color grade, deep purples and magentas against warm sodium orange, soft halation around lights, raw and unpolished like an independent arthouse film. Understated performances. No melodrama, no exaggerated crying, no glossy TV lighting, no slow motion.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}]}}, {"n": "02", "title": "Разговор у постели, Небраска 50-х", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "6", "8", "8", "6"], "task": "Hello, I hope you can help me with something. I'm a retired schoolteacher and I'm writing a short story about my grandmother, and my nephew told me I could make a little video of one scene using an AI program if I had a good description to give it. I'd like it to be about 15 seconds long.\n\nThe scene is a deathbed conversation. It takes place in a small farmhouse bedroom in Nebraska in the 1950s. An elderly woman, about 85, is lying in an iron bed under a handmade quilt. Late afternoon sun is coming through lace curtains. Her grown son, about 50, in a work shirt with his hat in his hands, is sitting on a wooden chair beside her.\n\nShe takes his hand and says: \"Your father wasn't the man you think he was. He was better.\"\nHe looks down and says quietly: \"Mama, don't. Not now.\"\nShe squeezes his hand and says: \"If not now, then when, Walter?\"\n\nI would like it to feel gentle and sad, not frightening. Something like the old film \"The Last Picture Show,\" but in soft color instead of black and white. Thank you very much for your help.", "answer": "What a lovely way to honor your grandmother. Here is a description you can copy and paste into the video program:\n\n---\n\n> A quiet, tender scene in a small farmhouse bedroom in rural Nebraska in the 1950s. Soft, golden late-afternoon sunlight filters through white lace curtains, casting delicate patterns on faded floral wallpaper and a plain wooden floor. An elderly woman, about 85, frail with thin white hair, lies in a white-painted iron bed beneath a handmade patchwork quilt. Beside the bed, her son, about 50, sits on a simple wooden chair. He has a weathered, sun-browned face and wears a faded work shirt, holding a felt hat in both hands on his knees.\n> \n> She slowly reaches out and takes his hand. In a soft, frail, warm voice she says: \"Your father wasn't the man you think he was. He was better.\" He looks down at their joined hands. After a pause, he says quietly, his voice catching: \"Mama, don't. Not now.\" She gently squeezes his hand and, with a faint, loving smile, says: \"If not now, then when, Walter?\" He slowly raises his eyes to hers, glistening with tears.\n> \n> Style: naturalistic American family drama, soft muted color like faded vintage film, warm amber light, gentle film grain. The camera is still and steady, starting on both of them and slowly moving closer. The mood is calm, intimate, sad, and loving, not dark or frightening. Quiet background sounds: a ticking clock, a light breeze, a distant meadowlark.\n\n---\n\n**A few helpful notes:**\n\n1. **Length limits:** Many programs only make clips of about 5 to 10 seconds. If yours does, make two clips and join them. Use the same description both times, but for the first clip include the dialogue only through \"Not now,\" and for the second, start with her squeezing his hand. Keeping the rest identical helps the characters and room look the same in both.\n\n2. **Spoken dialogue:** Some newer programs can create voices, but others only make silent video. If yours is silent, you could record the lines yourself or add them as captions, which can be very touching in an old-fashioned way.\n\n3. **About the film title:** I described the look of *The Last Picture Show* rather than naming it, because these programs often respond better to descriptions than to film titles. You're welcome to try adding it to see what happens.\n\n4. **Try more than once:** These programs often stumble on hands and small details. If something looks odd, just run it again. It may take a few tries to get one you love.\n\n5. **Keeping it gentle:** I avoided words like \"dying\" and \"deathbed\" because they can push the program toward something grim. Words like \"frail,\" \"tender,\" and \"loving\" tend to keep it soft.\n\nIf the first result isn't quite right, tell me what you'd like changed, and I'll help you adjust the description. Best wishes with your story.", "prompt": "A quiet, tender scene in a small farmhouse bedroom in rural Nebraska in the 1950s. Soft, golden late-afternoon sunlight filters through white lace curtains, casting delicate patterns on faded floral wallpaper and a plain wooden floor. An elderly woman, about 85, frail with thin white hair, lies in a white-painted iron bed beneath a handmade patchwork quilt. Beside the bed, her son, about 50, sits on a simple wooden chair. He has a weathered, sun-browned face and wears a faded work shirt, holding a felt hat in both hands on his knees.\n\nShe slowly reaches out and takes his hand. In a soft, frail, warm voice she says: \"Your father wasn't the man you think he was. He was better.\" He looks down at their joined hands. After a pause, he says quietly, his voice catching: \"Mama, don't. Not now.\" She gently squeezes his hand and, with a faint, loving smile, says: \"If not now, then when, Walter?\" He slowly raises his eyes to hers, glistening with tears.\n\nStyle: naturalistic American family drama, soft muted color like faded vintage film, warm amber light, gentle film grain. The camera is still and steady, starting on both of them and slowly moving closer. The mood is calm, intimate, sad, and loving, not dark or frightening. Quiet background sounds: a ticking clock, a light breeze, a distant meadowlark.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032332_5873453e-ed7b-4b15-a652-b6dd9d8c0e83.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032333_e92b3951-afb0-430d-bf98-5681f803ac19.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 5, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032335_70300817-b870-4968-9398-0d066178cb65.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": {"changes": "- Имён и брендов в промпте нет; повтор того же промпта без изменений (фильтр, вероятно, сработал на сгенерированное лицо/кадр).", "prompt": "A quiet, tender scene in a small farmhouse bedroom in rural Nebraska in the 1950s. Soft, golden late-afternoon sunlight filters through white lace curtains, casting delicate patterns on faded floral wallpaper and a plain wooden floor. An elderly woman, about 85, frail with thin white hair, lies in a white-painted iron bed beneath a handmade patchwork quilt. Beside the bed, her son, about 50, sits on a simple wooden chair. He has a weathered, sun-browned face and wears a faded work shirt, holding a felt hat in both hands on his knees.\n\nShe slowly reaches out and takes his hand. In a soft, frail, warm voice she says: \"Your father wasn't the man you think he was. He was better.\" He looks down at their joined hands. After a pause, he says quietly, his voice catching: \"Mama, don't. Not now.\" She gently squeezes his hand and, with a faint, loving smile, says: \"If not now, then when, Walter?\" He slowly raises his eyes to hers, glistening with tears.\n\nStyle: naturalistic American family drama, soft muted color like faded vintage film, warm amber light, gentle film grain. The camera is still and steady, starting on both of them and slowly moving closer. The mood is calm, intimate, sad, and loving, not dark or frightening. Quiet background sounds: a ticking clock, a light breeze, a distant meadowlark.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}]}}, {"n": "03", "title": "Допрос, фото улики, взгляд на зеркало", "total": "7,8", "scores": ["8", "7", "7", "8", "9"], "task": "Need a video gen prompt for a 15 sec interrogation scene. Pitching a crime show idea to a small production company next week, want a mood clip.\n\n- Setting: police interview room, cinder block walls, one overhead fluorescent that flickers, metal table, two-way mirror behind the suspect\n- Detective: woman, early 40s, rolled sleeves, very calm, slides a photo across the table\n- Suspect: man, late 20s, hoodie, cuffed to the table, sweating, tries to act bored\n- Dialogue:\n  - Detective: \"You said you were home all night.\"\n  - Suspect: \"I was.\"\n  - Detective (tapping the photo): \"Then explain why your truck is parked behind the Riverside Diner at 2:14 a.m.\"\n  - Suspect says nothing, just swallows\n- Camera should slowly push in on his face during the silence\n- Look: cold greens and grays, kind of like True Detective season 1\n- End on his eyes flicking to the mirror\n\nKeep it tight. No music, just the hum of the light.", "answer": "# Video Prompt\n\n```\nCinematic 15-second interrogation scene, prestige crime drama. 35mm film look, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, slow and deliberate camera. No music.\n\nSETTING: Cramped police interview room. Painted cinder block walls, scuffed and stained. A single overhead fluorescent tube buzzes and occasionally flickers. Bolted-down metal table. A large two-way mirror on the wall behind the suspect, slightly off to his right, dark and reflective.\n\nCHARACTERS:\n- Detective: woman, early 40s, dark hair pulled back, shirtsleeves rolled to the elbows. Completely calm, unhurried, quiet voice. Never raises her tone.\n- Suspect: man, late 20s, gray hoodie, wrists handcuffed to a steel ring on the table. Sweat on his forehead and upper lip. Slouched back, trying to look bored, but his jaw is tight.\n\nSHOT SEQUENCE:\n0–4s: Over-the-shoulder shot from behind the detective. She slides a photograph across the metal table toward him.\nDetective: \"You said you were home all night.\"\n4–6s: Suspect, flat, barely shrugging.\nSuspect: \"I was.\"\n6–10s: Detective taps the photo once with her index finger.\nDetective: \"Then explain why your truck is parked behind the Riverside Diner at 2:14 a.m.\"\n10–15s: Silence. Camera slowly pushes in on the suspect's face, ending in a tight close-up. He says nothing. He swallows hard. The fluorescent light flickers once. Final beat: his eyes flick sideways toward the two-way mirror. Hold on his face.\n\nLOOK: Desaturated cold palette of greens and grays, sickly green fluorescent cast, crushed blacks, fine film grain. Harsh top-down light carving deep shadows under the eyes. Moody, naturalistic, gritty, in the visual style of True Detective season 1.\n\nAUDIO: Constant low electrical hum of the fluorescent light, a faint tick when it flickers. Paper sliding on metal, a soft clink of handcuff chain. Dry, dead room tone. Clean dialogue. No music, no score.\n```\n\n# Tips\n\n- **Staging fix:** If the mirror is directly behind him, the final glance becomes a full head turn over his shoulder. Placing it \"behind and slightly to his right\" lets it read as a quick sideways eye flick, which plays better in close-up.\n- **If your tool caps at 8 seconds** (Veo 3, for example), split it into two clips: 0–6s ending on \"I was,\" then 6–15s starting on the tap. Copy the character and setting descriptions word for word into both prompts so the faces and lighting stay consistent.\n- **Don't ask for readable text on the photo.** Generators usually garble it, and the line already tells the audience what's in the photo.\n- **Generate several takes.** The swallow and the eye flick are subtle acting beats, and they're hit or miss. Expect to pick the best of 4 or 5.\n- **If a tool won't accept the show reference**, delete \"True Detective season 1.\" The palette and lighting descriptions carry most of the look anyway.\n\nGood luck with the pitch.", "prompt": "Cinematic 15-second interrogation scene, prestige crime drama. 35mm film look, anamorphic lens, shallow depth of field, slow and deliberate camera. No music.\n\nSETTING: Cramped police interview room. Painted cinder block walls, scuffed and stained. A single overhead fluorescent tube buzzes and occasionally flickers. Bolted-down metal table. A large two-way mirror on the wall behind the suspect, slightly off to his right, dark and reflective.\n\nCHARACTERS:\n- Detective: woman, early 40s, dark hair pulled back, shirtsleeves rolled to the elbows. Completely calm, unhurried, quiet voice. Never raises her tone.\n- Suspect: man, late 20s, gray hoodie, wrists handcuffed to a steel ring on the table. Sweat on his forehead and upper lip. Slouched back, trying to look bored, but his jaw is tight.\n\nSHOT SEQUENCE:\n0–4s: Over-the-shoulder shot from behind the detective. She slides a photograph across the metal table toward him.\nDetective: \"You said you were home all night.\"\n4–6s: Suspect, flat, barely shrugging.\nSuspect: \"I was.\"\n6–10s: Detective taps the photo once with her index finger.\nDetective: \"Then explain why your truck is parked behind the Riverside Diner at 2:14 a.m.\"\n10–15s: Silence. Camera slowly pushes in on the suspect's face, ending in a tight close-up. He says nothing. He swallows hard. The fluorescent light flickers once. Final beat: his eyes flick sideways toward the two-way mirror. Hold on his face.\n\nLOOK: Desaturated cold palette of greens and grays, sickly green fluorescent cast, crushed blacks, fine film grain. Harsh top-down light carving deep shadows under the eyes. Moody, naturalistic, gritty, in the visual style of True Detective season 1.\n\nAUDIO: Constant low electrical hum of the fluorescent light, a faint tick when it flickers. Paper sliding on metal, a soft clink of handcuff chain. Dry, dead room tone. Clean dialogue. No music, no score.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["True Detective"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032440_6bbaee5d-efc1-4586-a82d-e2e13c701b10.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032441_3e510e67-afcf-46be-bf2e-8ea1c0f8a5fe.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032442_85d2130d-0b2c-41cb-80c7-e3761e811084.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032443_00ab5802-5b3d-4894-924e-8822ec1dd1c4.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032444_77253ae1-dc5d-4889-b069-600ef5b4c376.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032445_5b566104-7734-46db-b433-7ea53aa8f0e8.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "04", "title": "Семейная ссора, теленовелла (ПРОМПТ НЕ ДАН — план съёмки на телефон)", "total": "2,6", "scores": ["3", "3", "2", "2", "3"], "task": "ok so um I'm talking into my phone so sorry if this is messy. I run a little family restaurant in San Antonio, it's called Casa Lupita's, and we do these short little skits for our Instagram Reels, like telenovela style but kind of funny-serious, you know, people love them. So I want a video for that, vertical, like fifteen seconds.\n\nSo it's a family argument in the restaurant kitchen after closing. There's the mom, she's like sixty, apron on, holding a wooden spoon, and her son who's like thirty and he just came in with a suitcase. And there's the abuela too, she's sitting on a stool in the corner peeling garlic and just watching, she doesn't say anything until the very end. Okay so the mom says \"Five years. Five years and not one phone call, and now you show up at my stove?\" And the son says \"I came back to help, Ma. I heard about the restaurant.\" And the mom kind of slams the spoon down and goes \"Nobody here needs your help.\" And then the abuela, without looking up, just says \"I do. Sit down, mijo.\" And everybody freezes.\n\nThe kitchen should be warm, like yellow light, steam from the pots, old tiles, little saint candle on the shelf. I want it dramatic like a real telenovela with the zoom-in on faces, you know what I mean, but also it should look like a real place not like a fake set. Thank you so much!!", "answer": "I can't create the video file itself, but here's a shot-by-shot plan you can film on your phone after closing. It's built to fit 15 seconds.\n\n## Shot List (vertical 9:16)\n\n**Shot 1 (0:00–0:01): Arrival**\nClose on the floor: suitcase wheels roll onto the old tiles and stop. Steam drifts in the background. *Sound: the thud of the suitcase.*\n\n**Shot 2 (0:01–0:05): Mom**\nMedium close-up, spoon in hand, steam behind her.\n**MOM:** \"Five years. Five years and not one phone call, and now you show up at *my stove?*\"\n\n**Shot 3 (0:05–0:08): Son**\nMedium shot, suitcase at his side, a little nervous.\n**SON:** \"I came back to help, Ma. I heard about the restaurant.\"\n\n**Shot 4 (0:08–0:10): The Slam**\nQuick close-up of the spoon slamming on the counter, then cut to Mom's face.\n**MOM:** \"Nobody here needs your help.\"\n\n**Shot 5 (0:10–0:13): Abuela**\nWide-ish shot of Abuela on her stool with the saint candle glowing on the shelf behind her. She keeps peeling garlic and never looks up.\n**ABUELA:** \"I do. Sit down, mijo.\"\n\n**Shot 6 (0:13–0:15): The Freeze**\nThree fast telenovela zooms: Mom's shocked face, then Son's, then Abuela calmly peeling. Add a dramatic sting sound and end on Abuela.\n\n## Tips to Make It Look Real and Dramatic\n\n- **Warm light:** Turn off any cold fluorescent overheads and use warm bulbs or a lamp placed off-camera. Avoid mixing warm and cold light, which makes skin look weird.\n- **Steam:** Actually boil water in the pots. Steam only shows up on camera if the light is *behind* it, so put a lamp behind the stove.\n- **Sound:** Turn off the hood fan while filming lines. Kitchens echo, so keep the phone close or use a cheap clip-on mic.\n- **Zooms:** Don't zoom with the phone while filming. Shoot normally, then add the snap zooms in CapCut or Instagram's editor (keyframe zoom plus a \"whoosh\" or dramatic sting). It looks much more like a real telenovela.\n- **Freeze:** Have everyone hold completely still for 2 to 3 seconds at the end. That gives you room to edit the zooms.\n- **Pacing:** 15 seconds is tight for all this dialogue, so say the lines quickly. If it runs long, trim the mom's line to: *\"Five years. Not one call. And now you show up at my stove?\"*\n- **Captions:** Add on-screen subtitles, since lots of people watch with the sound off.\n\n## Ending Text Ideas\n- \"¿Parte 2? 👀\"\n- \"At Casa Lupita's, there's always a seat at the table.\"\n- \"Abuela always gets the last word.\"\n\nIf you'd rather try an AI video tool (like Veo, Sora, or Runway), I can write prompts for each shot. Most of those tools make clips shorter than 15 seconds, so you'd generate the shots separately and stitch them together.", "prompt": "Shot List (vertical 9:16)\n\nShot 1 (0:00–0:01): Arrival\nClose on the floor: suitcase wheels roll onto the old tiles and stop. Steam drifts in the background. Sound: the thud of the suitcase.\n\nShot 2 (0:01–0:05): Mom\nMedium close-up, spoon in hand, steam behind her.\nMOM: \"Five years. Five years and not one phone call, and now you show up at my stove?\"\n\nShot 3 (0:05–0:08): Son\nMedium shot, suitcase at his side, a little nervous.\nSON: \"I came back to help, Ma. I heard about the restaurant.\"\n\nShot 4 (0:08–0:10): The Slam\nQuick close-up of the spoon slamming on the counter, then cut to Mom's face.\nMOM: \"Nobody here needs your help.\"\n\nShot 5 (0:10–0:13): Abuela\nWide-ish shot of Abuela on her stool with the saint candle glowing on the shelf behind her. She keeps peeling garlic and never looks up.\nABUELA: \"I do. Sit down, mijo.\"\n\nShot 6 (0:13–0:15): The Freeze\nThree fast telenovela zooms: Mom's shocked face, then Son's, then Abuela calmly peeling. Add a dramatic sting sound and end on Abuela.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032530_8e102606-33b1-4472-a4d6-c4f5a3584a26.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032531_3d297b3c-c4eb-4deb-b55c-e86789094faf.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032532_999a776d-de28-4562-944b-ba072b6ec0fd.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032532_f9d2f9b1-73ee-42f6-b8d5-63439c04d17c.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032533_737728ef-33fc-450d-8041-0e9ac6c60319.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032534_2d363f69-9c9f-42c4-9c2c-0aa96de4ddeb.mp4", "poster": "posters/dramatic-dialogue-04-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Признание у озера на закате", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "6", "8", "8", "6"], "task": "can u write me a prompt for ai video. confession scene, 15 secs or so\n\ntwo guys, best friends, late 30s, sitting on the tailgate of a pickup at a lake at sunset. both drinking beer (can be generic cans, no brand). one of them, Danny, has been quiet the whole time. other one, Rob, is laughing about something then stops.\n\nDanny: \"i'm the one who told Karen about the money.\"\nRob: (long pause) \"...you what\"\nDanny: \"i couldnt keep lying to her man. she's your wife.\"\n\nRob just stares at the water. thats the end. no yelling. want it quiet and heavy, golden light, wind on the water, kinda like the way Taylor Sheridan shows shoot stuff. its for a short film me and my buddies are doing for a local festival in Montana, just want to see what it could look like first", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste in, plus a shot-by-shot version in case your tool caps clips at 8-10 seconds.\n\n---\n\n**Main Prompt (15 sec)**\n\n> Cinematic 15-second dramatic scene, modern Western drama style. Golden hour at a remote mountain lake in Montana. The sun sits low on the horizon, casting warm amber light and long shadows. Light wind ripples across the water and moves the tall grass along the shore. Distant mountains are hazy in the background.\n> \n> Two men in their late 30s, lifelong best friends, sit side by side on the lowered tailgate of a weathered old pickup truck facing the lake. Both hold plain, unbranded beer cans. **Rob**: broad-shouldered, short beard, faded ball cap, flannel jacket. **Danny**: leaner, stubble, worn canvas work jacket, no hat. Danny has been quiet, staring at the water.\n> \n> Rob is mid-laugh, shaking his head at something. His laugh fades when he notices Danny isn't laughing. Silence. Danny keeps looking at the lake and says quietly, flatly: \"I'm the one who told Karen about the money.\"\n> \n> Long pause. Only wind and water. Rob slowly turns to look at him and says, barely above a whisper: \"...You what.\"\n> \n> Danny finally looks at him, his voice tight with guilt: \"I couldn't keep lying to her, man. She's your wife.\"\n> \n> Rob doesn't answer. He slowly turns back and stares out at the water, jaw tight, eyes unreadable. He doesn't move or yell. Hold on the silence.\n> \n> Style: anamorphic widescreen, shallow depth of field, subtle 35mm film grain, muted earth tones with warm golden highlights, natural light only. Slow, deliberate camera movement. Restrained, understated performances. Quiet, heavy, melancholic mood.\n> \n> Audio: Wind, water lapping against the shore, a distant bird. No music.\n\n---\n\n**Shot-by-Shot Version (if you need to split it up)**\n\n**Shot 1 (0-4s):** Wide shot from behind and to the side of the pickup. Two men are silhouetted on the tailgate against the glowing lake. Slow push-in. Rob laughs, then the laugh trails off.\n\n**Shot 2 (4-8s):** Medium close-up on Danny in profile, golden backlight, staring at the water. He says quietly: \"I'm the one who told Karen about the money.\"\n\n**Shot 3 (8-11s):** Close-up on Rob. His face goes still. He holds the pause, slowly turns his head, and says: \"...You what.\"\n\n**Shot 4 (11-13s):** Close-up on Danny, who looks at Rob for the first time. \"I couldn't keep lying to her, man. She's your wife.\"\n\n**Shot 5 (13-15s):** Wide shot of both men small in the frame, the lake and mountains huge around them. Rob stares at the water. Wind moves across the surface. Neither moves.\n\nCopy the full character and style descriptions into every shot prompt so the guys look the same across clips.\n\n---\n\n**Tips**\n- **Tool choice:** Veo 3 and Sora 2 handle dialogue and audio best right now. Kling and Runway look great but you may need to add voices separately.\n- **Pacing:** 15 seconds is tight for that pause. If the AI rushes it, generate the scene a bit longer and trim in editing. The silence is what sells it.\n- **Music:** Leave it out of the generation and add it in your edit. A single low cello or slide guitar note under the last shot would fit that Sheridan feel.\n- **Character looks:** Swap the descriptions to match your actual actors so the preview is closer to what you'll shoot.\n\nGood luck at the festival.", "prompt": "Cinematic 15-second dramatic scene, modern Western drama style. Golden hour at a remote mountain lake in Montana. The sun sits low on the horizon, casting warm amber light and long shadows. Light wind ripples across the water and moves the tall grass along the shore. Distant mountains are hazy in the background.\n\nTwo men in their late 30s, lifelong best friends, sit side by side on the lowered tailgate of a weathered old pickup truck facing the lake. Both hold plain, unbranded beer cans. **Rob**: broad-shouldered, short beard, faded ball cap, flannel jacket. **Danny**: leaner, stubble, worn canvas work jacket, no hat. Danny has been quiet, staring at the water.\n\nRob is mid-laugh, shaking his head at something. His laugh fades when he notices Danny isn't laughing. Silence. Danny keeps looking at the lake and says quietly, flatly: \"I'm the one who told Karen about the money.\"\n\nLong pause. Only wind and water. Rob slowly turns to look at him and says, barely above a whisper: \"...You what.\"\n\nDanny finally looks at him, his voice tight with guilt: \"I couldn't keep lying to her, man. She's your wife.\"\n\nRob doesn't answer. He slowly turns back and stares out at the water, jaw tight, eyes unreadable. He doesn't move or yell. Hold on the silence.\n\nStyle: anamorphic widescreen, shallow depth of field, subtle 35mm film grain, muted earth tones with warm golden highlights, natural light only. Slow, deliberate camera movement. Restrained, understated performances. Quiet, heavy, melancholic mood.\n\nAudio: Wind, water lapping against the shore, a distant bird. No music.", "aspect": "", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 5, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": {"changes": "- Имён и брендов в промпте нет; повтор того же промпта без изменений (фильтр, вероятно, сработал на сгенерированное лицо/кадр).", "prompt": "Cinematic 15-second dramatic scene, modern Western drama style. Golden hour at a remote mountain lake in Montana. The sun sits low on the horizon, casting warm amber light and long shadows. Light wind ripples across the water and moves the tall grass along the shore. Distant mountains are hazy in the background.\n\nTwo men in their late 30s, lifelong best friends, sit side by side on the lowered tailgate of a weathered old pickup truck facing the lake. Both hold plain, unbranded beer cans. **Rob**: broad-shouldered, short beard, faded ball cap, flannel jacket. **Danny**: leaner, stubble, worn canvas work jacket, no hat. Danny has been quiet, staring at the water.\n\nRob is mid-laugh, shaking his head at something. His laugh fades when he notices Danny isn't laughing. Silence. Danny keeps looking at the lake and says quietly, flatly: \"I'm the one who told Karen about the money.\"\n\nLong pause. Only wind and water. Rob slowly turns to look at him and says, barely above a whisper: \"...You what.\"\n\nDanny finally looks at him, his voice tight with guilt: \"I couldn't keep lying to her, man. She's your wife.\"\n\nRob doesn't answer. He slowly turns back and stares out at the water, jaw tight, eyes unreadable. He doesn't move or yell. Hold on the silence.\n\nStyle: anamorphic widescreen, shallow depth of field, subtle 35mm film grain, muted earth tones with warm golden highlights, natural light only. Slow, deliberate camera movement. Restrained, understated performances. Quiet, heavy, melancholic mood.\n\nAudio: Wind, water lapping against the shore, a distant bird. No music.", "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 2, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 5, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "in_progress", "url": "", "poster": ""}]}}]}, {"id": "v2v", "name": "Video to Video", "items": []}, {"id": "ugc", "name": "UGC", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "GRWM с маслом для губ Dewbelle, 9:16", "total": "6,8", "scores": ["7", "6", "6", "8", "7"], "task": "hiii ok so i need help lol. i'm launching my lip oil on tiktok next week, the brand is called Dewbelle and the shade i'm pushing is \"Peach Soda.\" can you write me a prompt for an AI video generator so i can make a little get ready with me clip? like 15 sec max.\n\nvibe: girl (early 20s) sitting on her bedroom floor in front of one of those big leaning mirrors, morning light, messy bun, oversized tee, ring light kinda off to the side. she's mid-makeup, already did her skin, then grabs the Dewbelle tube (frosted glass, peach colored, little gold cap), swipes it on, does the lip pop thing, and leans into the camera like she's telling her bestie a secret. maybe she says something like \"ok this is the only thing i'm wearing today.\" end on a close up of her lips all glossy and shiny.\n\ni want it to look like an actual girl filmed it on her phone propped on the floor, NOT like a fancy ad. think Alix Earle GRWM energy. vertical obviously since it's for tiktok and reels. thank uuu", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste in:\n\n```\nVertical 9:16 video, casual UGC get-ready-with-me style, filmed on a smartphone propped up on a bedroom floor at a slightly low angle. Unpolished, authentic, not an advertisement.\n\nA young woman in her early 20s sits cross-legged on a carpeted bedroom floor in front of a large leaning floor mirror. Soft natural morning light streams in from a window, warm and a little hazy. A ring light sits off to the side, turned off. She has a messy bun with loose face-framing strands and wears an oversized, faded t-shirt. Her skin is already done: dewy, fresh, minimal makeup. Lived-in bedroom background with the edge of an unmade bed and a few makeup products scattered on the floor.\n\nShe picks up a small lip oil tube made of frosted glass with a soft peach tint and a small shiny gold cap. She unscrews it and swipes the applicator across her lips while looking in the mirror, presses her lips together, and does a quick playful lip pop. Then she turns to the phone, leans in close with a conspiratorial little smile, like she's telling her best friend a secret, and says: \"Okay, this is the only thing I'm wearing today.\"\n\nFinal shot: tight close-up of her lips, glossy, juicy, and shiny with a sheer peachy tint catching the morning light.\n\nStyle: real phone camera footage, natural skin texture with visible pores, slight auto-exposure shifts, natural imperfect framing. No cinematic lighting, no color grading, no slow motion, no studio look. Audio: quiet room ambience, natural speaking voice, soft lip pop sound, no music.\n```\n\n**If your generator caps clips at 5–10 sec** (most do), split it into shots and stitch them in CapCut:\n\n- **Shot 1 (~7s):** Everything up through the swipe and lip pop.\n- **Shot 2 (~5s):** She turns to camera, leans in, and says the line.\n- **Shot 3 (~3s):** Lip close-up only.\n\nPaste the same character and setting description into each one so she stays consistent. If your tool supports it, use the last frame of one shot as the starting image for the next.\n\n**A few tips:**\n\n- **Your actual tube:** The AI will invent its own version of the product. For accuracy, use image-to-video mode with a real photo of your Dewbelle tube as the reference. Don't expect it to render the \"Dewbelle\" name legibly. Add your logo or a text overlay in editing.\n- **Dialogue:** Tools like Veo 3 or Sora handle speech fine, but if yours gets weird with lip sync, generate it silent and record the line yourself as a voiceover. That honestly makes it feel more real anyway.\n- **No influencer names in the prompt:** I left Alix Earle out on purpose. A lot of tools block real names, and you don't want her likeness showing up in your ad. The \"unpolished phone footage\" descriptors get you that vibe.\n- **Label it:** TikTok requires the \"AI-generated content\" label on realistic AI videos, and FTC rules don't allow presenting AI people as real customers. Post it from your brand account as brand content and you're totally fine.\n\nGood luck with the launch! Peach Soda sounds adorable 🍑", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 video, casual UGC get-ready-with-me style, filmed on a smartphone propped up on a bedroom floor at a slightly low angle. Unpolished, authentic, not an advertisement.\n\nA young woman in her early 20s sits cross-legged on a carpeted bedroom floor in front of a large leaning floor mirror. Soft natural morning light streams in from a window, warm and a little hazy. A ring light sits off to the side, turned off. She has a messy bun with loose face-framing strands and wears an oversized, faded t-shirt. Her skin is already done: dewy, fresh, minimal makeup. Lived-in bedroom background with the edge of an unmade bed and a few makeup products scattered on the floor.\n\nShe picks up a small lip oil tube made of frosted glass with a soft peach tint and a small shiny gold cap. She unscrews it and swipes the applicator across her lips while looking in the mirror, presses her lips together, and does a quick playful lip pop. Then she turns to the phone, leans in close with a conspiratorial little smile, like she's telling her best friend a secret, and says: \"Okay, this is the only thing I'm wearing today.\"\n\nFinal shot: tight close-up of her lips, glossy, juicy, and shiny with a sheer peachy tint catching the morning light.\n\nStyle: real phone camera footage, natural skin texture with visible pores, slight auto-exposure shifts, natural imperfect framing. No cinematic lighting, no color grading, no slow motion, no studio look. Audio: quiet room ambience, natural speaking voice, soft lip pop sound, no music.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032747_7bc30a68-e088-4d73-9149-86de5cf69e60.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032748_ac0ec74b-4a50-4660-a6b4-b0689090ca76.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032749_c26ac08d-2214-4977-a47b-8cc156da7cca.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032750_38aba84a-bf23-4b6b-a947-cd2379c98d21.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032750_a0264d06-7751-4eaf-9c21-48eaf15f59ca.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032751_c3c7a552-b572-4327-9f44-1f40898c570a.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "02", "title": "Отзыв о насадке TrueFlow (плейсхолдер вместо продукта)", "total": "5,4", "scores": ["6", "6", "3", "6", "6"], "task": "Good afternoon,\n\nI own a small hardware and garden supply store in Knoxville, Tennessee, and my nephew talked me into trying one of these AI video programs for our Facebook page. I would appreciate it if you could write me a prompt I can put into it.\n\nWe carry our own brand of hose nozzle called the TrueFlow Ranger. It has eight spray settings and a thumb lever that doesn't cramp your hand, which is the main selling point for our older customers.\n\nWhat I have in mind is a short testimonial, about fifteen seconds long. A retired fellow, maybe in his late sixties, flannel shirt and a ball cap, standing in his backyard vegetable garden in the late afternoon. He's holding the nozzle up to the camera like he's showing it to a neighbor, explains in his own plain words that his old nozzle hurt his arthritis and this one doesn't, then turns and waters his tomato plants with a nice gentle shower setting. It should look like his grandson filmed it on a phone, a little shaky, nothing polished. Friendly and honest, not salesy.\n\nThank you kindly for your help.\n\nDale", "answer": "Good afternoon, Dale,\n\nHere's a prompt you can paste right in. I've written it in plain descriptive language, which works well with most of these video programs.\n\n---\n\n**PROMPT:**\n\n> A casual, unpolished home video filmed on a smartphone by a teenage grandson. Handheld and slightly shaky, with natural autofocus shifts, no professional lighting, and no music.\n> \n> **Setting:** A backyard vegetable garden in East Tennessee in the late afternoon. Warm, low golden sunlight comes in from the side, casting long soft shadows. Staked tomato plants heavy with green and ripening red tomatoes, a weathered wooden fence and leafy trees in the background, a green garden hose running along the ground.\n> \n> **Subject:** A friendly retired man in his late sixties with a weathered face and gray stubble. He wears a faded red-and-black flannel shirt with the sleeves rolled up, worn jeans, and a well-worn ball cap. He's relaxed and a little bashful about being filmed, like he's showing something to a neighbor over the fence.\n> \n> **Action (0–9 seconds):** He holds a garden hose nozzle up close to the camera with one hand and gently presses the thumb lever to show how easy it is. He speaks directly to the camera in a warm, unhurried Southern Appalachian accent:\n> *\"My old nozzle hurt my hands somethin' awful. Arthritis. This TrueFlow Ranger, you just rest your thumb on the lever. No cramping at all. Eight settings, too. Watch here.\"*\n> \n> **Action (9–15 seconds):** He turns to his tomato plants, presses the lever, and waters them with a soft, gentle shower spray. Fine droplets sparkle in the sunlight. The camera follows him a little unsteadily. He glances back at the camera with a small, satisfied smile.\n> \n> **The nozzle:** [DESCRIBE YOUR NOZZLE HERE, e.g., \"a pistol-grip hose nozzle, green and black, with a round rotating dial on the front for spray patterns and a wide, padded thumb lever on top\"]\n> \n> **Style:** Authentic and candid, natural colors, ambient backyard sounds (birds, a light breeze, water spraying). Not a commercial. No text, no logos, no music.\n\n---\n\n**If your program only makes short clips:** Many of these tools max out around 8 to 10 seconds. If so, run it as two separate clips: one for the talking part and one for the watering part. Repeat the setting and subject descriptions in both so the man and garden look the same. Your nephew can stitch them together.\n\n**A few practical tips:**\n\n- **Make sure the nozzle looks like yours.** The program has no idea what the TrueFlow Ranger looks like, so fill in that bracket carefully. If the tool lets you upload a reference photo, use a picture of your actual nozzle. You want folks who come into the store to recognize it.\n- **Add the name as a caption afterward.** These programs often scramble any words printed on objects, so it's best to put \"TrueFlow Ranger\" in a text caption when you post.\n- **Generate it a few times.** Results vary, and you might need a couple of tries to get \"TrueFlow\" pronounced right and the spray looking natural.\n\n**One friendly heads-up:** Since the man in the video won't be a real customer, it's worth labeling it something like \"Dramatization (AI-generated)\" in the post. The Federal Trade Commission has rules against testimonials that appear to come from real customers when they don't, and Facebook also asks that AI-made videos be labeled. A small caption takes care of it.\n\nYou could also use this same description as a shot list if you have a real regular who loves the nozzle and wouldn't mind being filmed. A familiar local face often goes over even better on a hometown store's page.\n\nBest of luck with it, and I hope it brings some folks through the door.", "prompt": "A casual, unpolished home video filmed on a smartphone by a teenage grandson. Handheld and slightly shaky, with natural autofocus shifts, no professional lighting, and no music.\n\n**Setting:** A backyard vegetable garden in East Tennessee in the late afternoon. Warm, low golden sunlight comes in from the side, casting long soft shadows. Staked tomato plants heavy with green and ripening red tomatoes, a weathered wooden fence and leafy trees in the background, a green garden hose running along the ground.\n\n**Subject:** A friendly retired man in his late sixties with a weathered face and gray stubble. He wears a faded red-and-black flannel shirt with the sleeves rolled up, worn jeans, and a well-worn ball cap. He's relaxed and a little bashful about being filmed, like he's showing something to a neighbor over the fence.\n\n**Action (0–9 seconds):** He holds a garden hose nozzle up close to the camera with one hand and gently presses the thumb lever to show how easy it is. He speaks directly to the camera in a warm, unhurried Southern Appalachian accent:\n*\"My old nozzle hurt my hands somethin' awful. Arthritis. This TrueFlow Ranger, you just rest your thumb on the lever. No cramping at all. Eight settings, too. Watch here.\"*\n\n**Action (9–15 seconds):** He turns to his tomato plants, presses the lever, and waters them with a soft, gentle shower spray. Fine droplets sparkle in the sunlight. The camera follows him a little unsteadily. He glances back at the camera with a small, satisfied smile.\n\n**The nozzle:** [DESCRIBE YOUR NOZZLE HERE, e.g., \"a pistol-grip hose nozzle, green and black, with a round rotating dial on the front for spray patterns and a wide, padded thumb lever on top\"]\n\n**Style:** Authentic and candid, natural colors, ambient backyard sounds (birds, a light breeze, water spraying). Not a commercial. No text, no logos, no music.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032846_d85a4859-89a7-474d-8e5d-2b7d5e787486.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032847_371c2d99-fde5-48d9-a4b6-a72b7fc17ea9.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032847_40d4e842-4d13-432d-add6-e7d4e302ec6a.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032848_c504e4cd-aa45-48a8-b4b9-7fb8f0cf5fe5.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032849_40e7159d-8a5c-44a6-bece-43737edb6807.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032850_598174eb-6b52-4410-b27d-abaaeabee975.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "03", "title": "Приложение Splitzy, problem→solution, 9:16", "total": "7,4", "scores": ["8", "7", "6", "8", "8"], "task": "Need a prompt for an AI video gen. Details:\n\n- App: Splitzy (splits bills/rent between roommates, sends reminders so you don't have to be the bad guy)\n- Length: ~15 sec\n- Format: vertical, it's for IG Reels + TikTok\n- Style: problem → solution, creator talking straight to the phone\n- Person: guy mid-20s, hoodie, shared apartment kitchen, dirty dishes in the sink for realism\n- Beat 1: he's annoyed, holding up a crumpled grocery receipt, \"my roommates owe me $63 and nobody's paying\"\n- Beat 2: pulls out his phone, taps the app, quick shot of the screen showing the split\n- Beat 3: phone buzzes a couple times, he grins, \"paid. paid. paid.\"\n- Should feel like a real creator post, slightly messy framing, natural kitchen light, not a commercial\n- Ref: kind of like those dry, deadpan roommate skits people do on TikTok\n\nThx", "answer": "**Prompt:**\n\n```\nVertical 9:16 video, about 15 seconds, filmed like an authentic TikTok / Instagram Reels creator post on a phone's front-facing camera. Handheld with slight wobble, imperfect off-center framing, natural daylight from a kitchen window, no cinematic lighting, no color grading, no music. Should feel like a real person's post, not an ad.\n\nSetting: small, lived-in shared apartment kitchen. Cluttered counter, pile of dirty dishes and a greasy pan in the sink behind him, mismatched mugs, a crumpled takeout bag.\n\nCharacter: man in his mid-20s, gray hoodie, messy hair, light stubble. Dry, deadpan, mildly fed-up energy, like a low-key roommate comedy skit.\n\nBeat 1 (0–5s): Close-up, he leans toward the camera holding a crumpled grocery receipt up near the lens. Flat, annoyed delivery: \"My roommates owe me sixty-three dollars and nobody's paying.\"\n\nBeat 2 (5–9s): He exhales, pulls his phone from his hoodie pocket, taps it a few times. Quick cut to a close-up over his shoulder of the phone screen: a clean, simple bill-splitting app showing an $84 grocery total split four ways, $21 each, and his thumb tapping \"Send reminder.\"\n\nBeat 3 (9–15s): Back to front camera. His phone buzzes in his hand. He glances down, small grin starting. \"Paid.\" Phone buzzes again. \"Paid.\" Buzzes a third time. He looks straight into the camera, deadpan, slightly smug: \"Paid.\" Clip cuts off abruptly.\n\nAudio: natural room tone, faint fridge hum, crisp phone vibration sounds on each buzz. Dialogue sounds casual and unpolished, like he's talking to his phone.\n```\n\n**Negative prompt (if your tool supports it):**\n`studio lighting, gimbal-smooth movement, cinematic grade, background music, subtitles, on-screen text, logos, extra people, clean tidy kitchen, actor-y delivery`\n\n**Tips for getting it to work:**\n\n- **Length:** Most generators cap clips at 5–10 seconds. If yours does, generate Beat 1 and Beats 2–3 as separate clips and paste the full Character + Setting paragraphs into each so he looks the same in both. Then stitch them together in CapCut.\n- **App screen:** AI will mangle UI text and won't know what Splitzy looks like. Either generate Beat 2 with a blank or green phone screen and composite a real screen recording over it, or just cut to an actual screen recording for that shot. This will look more legit anyway.\n- **Branding:** Add \"Splitzy\" as a native-style TikTok/IG text overlay or a quick end card in the edit. Don't rely on the AI to render the name.\n- **Math check:** $84 split four ways means three roommates owe $21 each, which totals $63. That matches the three \"paid\"s, in case anyone in the comments does the math.\n- **No-audio models:** If your tool doesn't generate dialogue, record the lines yourself on your phone. A slightly lo-fi voice memo actually sells the \"real creator\" feel better.", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 video, about 15 seconds, filmed like an authentic TikTok / Instagram Reels creator post on a phone's front-facing camera. Handheld with slight wobble, imperfect off-center framing, natural daylight from a kitchen window, no cinematic lighting, no color grading, no music. Should feel like a real person's post, not an ad.\n\nSetting: small, lived-in shared apartment kitchen. Cluttered counter, pile of dirty dishes and a greasy pan in the sink behind him, mismatched mugs, a crumpled takeout bag.\n\nCharacter: man in his mid-20s, gray hoodie, messy hair, light stubble. Dry, deadpan, mildly fed-up energy, like a low-key roommate comedy skit.\n\nBeat 1 (0–5s): Close-up, he leans toward the camera holding a crumpled grocery receipt up near the lens. Flat, annoyed delivery: \"My roommates owe me sixty-three dollars and nobody's paying.\"\n\nBeat 2 (5–9s): He exhales, pulls his phone from his hoodie pocket, taps it a few times. Quick cut to a close-up over his shoulder of the phone screen: a clean, simple bill-splitting app showing an $84 grocery total split four ways, $21 each, and his thumb tapping \"Send reminder.\"\n\nBeat 3 (9–15s): Back to front camera. His phone buzzes in his hand. He glances down, small grin starting. \"Paid.\" Phone buzzes again. \"Paid.\" Buzzes a third time. He looks straight into the camera, deadpan, slightly smug: \"Paid.\" Clip cuts off abruptly.\n\nAudio: natural room tone, faint fridge hum, crisp phone vibration sounds on each buzz. Dialogue sounds casual and unpolished, like he's talking to his phone.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032945_3fa412bb-c188-4837-ae86-ee709d15f58d.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032946_e2b14db2-2566-4a8b-9b6c-ef1df0932be7.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032946_bd422ea6-93dc-4362-96fd-8403671ab13b.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032947_c061b03a-0b3d-47c8-b727-b1df0b523728.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032948_27d27306-5c7a-4219-a9ef-0278b168cdc9.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_032949_98b1d76d-65c1-4bbf-bf33-483527fc58b0.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "04", "title": "Контейнеры Lunchnest, утро мамы (AI-промпт приписан в конце плана съёмки)", "total": "4,6", "scores": ["5", "4", "5", "5", "4"], "task": "Okay so I'm gonna just kind of talk this out because I'm driving to pickup and using voice to text, sorry if it's a mess. So I'm a mom of three, I live outside Phoenix, and I started this little side business making a meal prep container set, it's called Lunchnest, they're these stackable glass containers with bamboo lids and they've got little color coded dividers so the kids know which one's theirs. And I want to make a day in my life type video, like the ones where the mom is like narrating her morning, you know, kind of like that Ballerina Farm vibe but way less fancy, more like real suburban mom chaos. It needs to be like fifteen seconds, maybe a little less. So I'm picturing it starts super early, kitchen still kind of dim, coffee maker going, she's in a robe and a claw clip, and she's lining up the Lunchnest containers on the counter and filling them really fast, like apple slices, sandwiches, little crackers. Then a kid runs in and grabs the blue one, and then like a quick cut to her at the door handing them out and the kids running to the car. And then at the end she sips her coffee and kind of gives the camera a look like, yep, we survived. It should look like it was filmed on her phone, a little bit handheld, warm morning light. Oh and it's for Instagram stories and reels so it should be vertical. Okay thank you so much, I really appreciate it.", "answer": "No worries, that came through clearly. Here's a plan you can use whether you film it yourself or use an AI video tool.\n\n## Lunchnest \"Morning Chaos\" Reel (~14 sec, vertical 9:16)\n\n| Time | Shot | On-screen text |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0–2s | Close-up of coffee maker dripping, kitchen dim, just under-cabinet light and a hint of sunrise through the window | **5:52 AM** |\n| 2–6s | Mom in robe + claw clip lines up Lunchnest containers, then fills them fast (sped up 2x): apple slices, sandwiches, crackers. Make sure the **colored dividers and bamboo lids** are clearly visible. | **3 kids. 3 lunches.** |\n| 6–8s | A kid runs into frame and grabs the blue one off the counter | **no fights over whose is whose 🙌** |\n| 8–11s | Quick cut to the front door: she hands out containers, kids run toward the car | |\n| 11–14s | She leans on the doorframe, sips coffee, gives the camera a deadpan \"yep, we survived\" look | **we survived.** |\n| 14–15s | (optional) Lunchnest logo or product shot | **Lunchnest** |\n\n## Optional voiceover (~15 sec, read casually)\n> \"Five fifty-two. Coffee's on, nobody's up yet. Three lunches, three colors, zero arguments about whose is whose. Mostly. And... they're out. Yep. We survived.\"\n\nOr skip the voiceover and use a trending audio with just the text overlays. That often performs better on Reels.\n\n## Filming tips\n- **Hold the phone yourself.** A slight wobble is what makes it feel real. Skip the tripod.\n- **Light:** In Phoenix, sunrise light through a kitchen window is perfect. Turn off overheads and keep only under-cabinet lights on.\n- **Text placement:** Keep text out of the top and bottom ~15% of the screen so Instagram's buttons don't cover it.\n- **Hero moment:** Get one clean, close shot of the kid grabbing the blue container. That's your product demo.\n\n## If you're using an AI video tool\nPaste something like this:\n\n> *Vertical 9:16, handheld iPhone footage, warm early-morning light. A tired but cheerful mom in her 30s, in a robe with her hair in a claw clip, quickly packs school lunches in a dim suburban kitchen. She fills stackable glass meal prep containers with bamboo lids and colorful dividers with apple slices, sandwiches, and crackers. A young child runs in and grabs the blue container. Cut to the front door: she hands out lunches and kids run to the car. Final shot: she sips coffee and gives the camera a knowing, deadpan look. Authentic, candid, slightly chaotic, natural lighting, realistic.*\n\nOne heads-up: AI tools won't reproduce your actual containers accurately, and most generate clips of only 5–10 seconds. A good hybrid is to generate the mom/kids/vibe shots with AI, film a quick real close-up of your Lunchnest set being filled, and edit them together in CapCut.\n\nGood luck with the launch, and no need to read any of this until you're parked! 🚗☕", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16, handheld iPhone footage, warm early-morning light. A tired but cheerful mom in her 30s, in a robe with her hair in a claw clip, quickly packs school lunches in a dim suburban kitchen. She fills stackable glass meal prep containers with bamboo lids and colorful dividers with apple slices, sandwiches, and crackers. A young child runs in and grabs the blue container. Cut to the front door: she hands out lunches and kids run to the car. Final shot: she sips coffee and gives the camera a knowing, deadpan look. Authentic, candid, slightly chaotic, natural lighting, realistic.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033037_a4b3c413-9725-49d3-84e0-7b95e94ddd39.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033038_59d3632a-a146-4f56-999e-fd97ebd325ba.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033039_5031d826-de0b-4d09-8e5c-d34ec0f07e47.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033040_928ec652-b1d4-40f5-be25-1892c0c55426.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033040_2e2ca3ea-139e-4844-a419-a58d2a554c3f.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033041_44aef61f-8847-42a4-b98b-0b686a69b6f1.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-04-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Распаковка шейкера IRONVAULT", "total": "7,2", "scores": ["8", "7", "6", "7", "8"], "task": "yo can u write me a prompt for an ai video thing. im a personal trainer in chicago and i got my own protein shaker brand called IRONVAULT, matte black w a steel loop on top and a hidden pill compartment in the bottom. want an unboxing vid like 15 secs\n\ndude in a gym locker room sitting on the bench, opens the box (black box w red logo), pulls out the shaker, twists the bottom to show the hidden compartment, then throws a scoop of powder in, shakes it hard and it doesnt leak at all, takes a big sip and nods at the camera. no talking needed just reactions, maybe a little grunt lol\n\nshoud look filmed on a phone by his gym buddy, kinda close and raw, fluorescent gym lighting. like those gymtok unboxing clips. no fancy ad stuff", "answer": "Here's a paste-ready prompt:\n\n---\n\n**Prompt:**\n\nVertical 9:16 smartphone video, handheld by a gym buddy standing close. Slightly shaky, casual framing, occasional autofocus hunting. Raw, unpolished GymTok-style clip, not a commercial.\n\n**Setting:** Gym locker room with gray metal lockers, a wooden bench, and a tile floor. Harsh overhead fluorescent lighting with a slightly cool, greenish tint.\n\n**Subject:** Muscular guy, late 20s, a little sweaty post-workout, black cut-off tank top, sitting on the bench facing the camera.\n\n**Action:**\n- **0–3s:** He opens a matte black box with a bold red \"IRONVAULT\" logo and pulls out a matte black protein shaker with a brushed steel loop on the lid. Eyebrows raise, impressed.\n- **3–6s:** He twists off the bottom of the shaker to reveal a hidden compartment holding a few supplement capsules, tilts it toward the camera, and smirks. Screws it back on.\n- **6–9s:** Pours water in from a bottle, dumps in a scoop of protein powder, snaps the lid shut.\n- **9–12s:** Shakes it hard and fast close to the lens. No drips, no leaks.\n- **12–15s:** Flips the spout, takes a big gulp, wipes his mouth with the back of his hand, nods at the camera with a low satisfied grunt.\n\n**Audio:** Ambient locker room echo, distant clanking weights, a locker door shutting, liquid sloshing during the shake, one low \"mm\" grunt. No dialogue, no music, no voiceover.\n\n**Avoid:** Cinematic lighting, slow motion, color grading, text overlays, lens flares, polished ad look.\n\n---\n\n**Tips:**\n\n- **Logo:** AI video often garbles text, so \"IRONVAULT\" might come out misspelled. If your tool supports image-to-video, upload a real photo of your box and shaker as a reference. Otherwise, plan to fix the logo in editing.\n- **Length:** Some tools cap clips at 8–10 seconds. If yours does, split it into two clips at the compartment reveal (0–6s and 6–15s) and stitch them together.\n- **Leak test:** If the shake looks off, add \"lid tightly sealed, bottle completely dry on the outside\" to push it toward a clean result.", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 smartphone video, handheld by a gym buddy standing close. Slightly shaky, casual framing, occasional autofocus hunting. Raw, unpolished GymTok-style clip, not a commercial.\n\n**Setting:** Gym locker room with gray metal lockers, a wooden bench, and a tile floor. Harsh overhead fluorescent lighting with a slightly cool, greenish tint.\n\n**Subject:** Muscular guy, late 20s, a little sweaty post-workout, black cut-off tank top, sitting on the bench facing the camera.\n\n**Action:**\n- **0–3s:** He opens a matte black box with a bold red \"IRONVAULT\" logo and pulls out a matte black protein shaker with a brushed steel loop on the lid. Eyebrows raise, impressed.\n- **3–6s:** He twists off the bottom of the shaker to reveal a hidden compartment holding a few supplement capsules, tilts it toward the camera, and smirks. Screws it back on.\n- **6–9s:** Pours water in from a bottle, dumps in a scoop of protein powder, snaps the lid shut.\n- **9–12s:** Shakes it hard and fast close to the lens. No drips, no leaks.\n- **12–15s:** Flips the spout, takes a big gulp, wipes his mouth with the back of his hand, nods at the camera with a low satisfied grunt.\n\n**Audio:** Ambient locker room echo, distant clanking weights, a locker door shutting, liquid sloshing during the shake, one low \"mm\" grunt. No dialogue, no music, no voiceover.\n\n**Avoid:** Cinematic lighting, slow motion, color grading, text overlays, lens flares, polished ad look.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033128_981a7fcb-0a99-44b0-85d4-a3ae3ce8f82b.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-05-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033129_7fe6586b-9ed2-4d85-9cdf-6b93aad787cd.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-05-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033130_273731b4-a26e-46bc-b291-0bc4784515ec.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-05-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033130_7807b74b-aa31-4e72-aac4-1b33f7139a77.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-05-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033131_2d5705ca-b592-4f31-a038-aef740ceb934.mp4", "poster": "posters/ugc-05-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "nsfw", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": null}]}, {"id": "paid-ads", "name": "Paid Ads", "items": [{"n": "01", "title": "Боксёрский зал Iron Lantern, TikTok 9:16", "total": "6,4", "scores": ["7", "6", "5", "7", "7"], "task": "hey so i own a small boxing gym in west philly called Iron Lantern Boxing and i wanna run a tiktok ad. can u write me a prompt for one of those ai video makers? like 15 sec, vertical obviously\n\nwhat i want: starts dark, just the sound of a heavy bag getting hit, then the lights kinda flicker on and its regular people training, not pro fighters, like a nurse, a dad, a college kid, all sweating and going hard. kinda gritty rocky vibe, old brick walls, chalk dust, sweat flying in slow mo. end on the sign out front at night with \"first class free\" on it\n\nwho its for: people in the neighborhood 20-45 who never boxed before and think its too intense. gotta sell that its for normal people and the first class is free. dont make it look cheesy or like a supplement commercial lol", "answer": "# AI Video Prompt: Iron Lantern Boxing (15s TikTok)\n\n## Option 1: Single Prompt\nFor tools that can do a full 15 seconds (Sora, Veo, etc.)\n\n```\n15-second vertical 9:16 video ad for a small neighborhood boxing gym. Gritty, \ncinematic documentary style: handheld camera, natural light, 16mm film grain, \nmuted warm color grade, deep shadows. Real everyday people, not athletes or models.\n\n0-2s: Total darkness. Only sound is the heavy thud of fists hitting a leather \nheavy bag, chains creaking.\n\n2-4s: Old industrial overhead lights flicker on one by one, revealing a worn \nboxing gym with exposed red brick walls, cracked leather heavy bags, and chalk \ndust floating in the light beams.\n\n4-11s: Fast cuts of regular people training hard:\n- A woman in her 30s wearing hospital scrub pants and a tank top, hair tied \n  back, punching mitts held by a coach\n- A dad in his 40s with a slight belly and gray in his beard, breathing hard \n  on the heavy bag\n- A college-age guy in a faded hoodie jumping rope, a little clumsy but focused\n- Slow-motion close-up of sweat flying off a face as a punch lands\n- Slow-motion burst of chalk dust off a heavy bag\n- A coach fist-bumping a tired, smiling beginner\n\n11-15s: Exterior at night. Old brick storefront on a city street in West \nPhiladelphia, wet pavement reflecting a warm glowing sign. Light from the \nwindow spills onto the sidewalk. Slow push-in on the entrance.\n\nMixed ages, body types, and ethnicities. Raw, honest, unpolished.\n\nAvoid: bodybuilders, six-packs, shirtless models, glossy commercial lighting, \nlens flares, epic movie-trailer feel, supplement-ad aesthetic.\n```\n\n## Option 2: Shot-by-Shot\nMost AI video tools (Runway, Kling, Pika) cap at 5–10 seconds, so you may need to generate clips separately and stitch them in CapCut. Paste this style line at the end of every clip so they match:\n\n> *Style: handheld documentary, 16mm film grain, muted warm grade, deep shadows, gritty and realistic, vertical 9:16*\n\n1. **Lights on (3s):** Dark old boxing gym, industrial lights flicker on one by one, revealing red brick walls, heavy bags, chalk dust floating in light beams.\n2. **Nurse (3s):** Woman in her 30s in scrub pants and a tank top punching focus mitts held by a coach, sweating, determined.\n3. **Dad (3s):** Man in his 40s, slight belly, gray beard, hitting a heavy bag, breathing hard, slow motion sweat flying.\n4. **College kid + fist bump (3s):** College-age guy in a hoodie jumping rope, then a coach fist-bumping him as he laughs, out of breath.\n5. **Sign (3s):** Brick storefront at night, wet street reflecting a warm glowing sign, slow push-in on the door.\n\n## Tips\n\n**Don't let the AI write your sign.** AI video is bad at text and will probably spell it \"FRIST CLAZZ FERE.\" Two better options:\n- Generate the storefront with no text, then add \"FIRST CLASS FREE\" as a text overlay in CapCut.\n- Even better, film your actual sign at night on your phone and use that as the last shot. It's real, the text is correct, and locals will recognize the building.\n\n**Watch the intensity.** Your audience already thinks boxing is too intense, and a full Rocky montage could confirm that fear. That's why I put in the fist bump and the clumsy jump-rope kid. One or two moments of people smiling or a coach helping someone tells viewers \"you'd fit in here\" better than any caption. Keep at least one in the final cut.\n\n**Sound.** If your tool doesn't generate audio, add it in CapCut: a couple of real bag thuds in the dark, then a gritty beat when the lights come on. A dry, simple sound beats epic music for avoiding the supplement-ad feel.\n\n**On-screen text.** Keep it to two moments:\n- Around 5s: *\"No experience needed.\"*\n- On the sign shot: *\"First class free. West Philly.\"*\n\n**Caption idea:** *\"you don't need to be a fighter to walk in here 🥊 first class is on us\"*", "prompt": "15-second vertical 9:16 video ad for a small neighborhood boxing gym. Gritty, \ncinematic documentary style: handheld camera, natural light, 16mm film grain, \nmuted warm color grade, deep shadows. Real everyday people, not athletes or models.\n\n0-2s: Total darkness. Only sound is the heavy thud of fists hitting a leather \nheavy bag, chains creaking.\n\n2-4s: Old industrial overhead lights flicker on one by one, revealing a worn \nboxing gym with exposed red brick walls, cracked leather heavy bags, and chalk \ndust floating in the light beams.\n\n4-11s: Fast cuts of regular people training hard:\n- A woman in her 30s wearing hospital scrub pants and a tank top, hair tied \n  back, punching mitts held by a coach\n- A dad in his 40s with a slight belly and gray in his beard, breathing hard \n  on the heavy bag\n- A college-age guy in a faded hoodie jumping rope, a little clumsy but focused\n- Slow-motion close-up of sweat flying off a face as a punch lands\n- Slow-motion burst of chalk dust off a heavy bag\n- A coach fist-bumping a tired, smiling beginner\n\n11-15s: Exterior at night. Old brick storefront on a city street in West \nPhiladelphia, wet pavement reflecting a warm glowing sign. Light from the \nwindow spills onto the sidewalk. Slow push-in on the entrance.\n\nMixed ages, body types, and ethnicities. Raw, honest, unpolished.\n\nAvoid: bodybuilders, six-packs, shirtless models, glossy commercial lighting, \nlens flares, epic movie-trailer feel, supplement-ad aesthetic.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033250_a95108b4-b398-4b43-b95b-b9b468b59b74.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033251_f6eebb77-c2c7-44ab-afed-8c684ee371b2.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033252_755e9945-e60b-428f-9d89-f214deab3563.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033252_59bcc098-a34b-4aff-93be-e57f74bd3901.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033253_cd9edaaa-62f9-46e5-ad71-c4e12d8c29b7.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033254_e0732622-b428-46fb-9593-222eb6fcffa2.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-01-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "02", "title": "Кофейня Copper Kettle, утро", "total": "6,0", "scores": ["6", "5", "7", "6", "6"], "task": "Hello,\n\nI hope this is the right way to ask. My husband and I run a small coffee shop in Asheville, North Carolina called The Copper Kettle Coffee House, and our granddaughter told me I could ask you to write the instructions for one of those AI programs that make videos. We would like a short advertisement, about 15 seconds long, to put on our Facebook and Instagram page.\n\nWe are trying to bring in more people on weekday mornings, especially retirees and folks who work from home. We want to sell our new maple oat latte and the fact that we have big comfortable chairs and free refills on drip coffee until 10 a.m.\n\nWhat I picture is a quiet, cozy morning. Fog on the mountains outside the window, warm light coming in, steam rising off a latte with a little leaf drawn in the foam, an older gentleman reading the paper and a young woman on her laptop by the fireplace. Something gentle, like the feeling of a Hallmark movie. At the end it should show our name and \"Free refills until 10 a.m.\"\n\nThank you so much for your help.\n\nMargaret", "answer": "Hello Margaret,\n\nYou've come to the right place. Below is a prompt you can copy and paste into the video program. I've also included a shot-by-shot version and a few tips.\n\n---\n\n## The Prompt (copy and paste this)\n\n> A 15-second cozy, cinematic advertisement for a small-town coffee shop, with the warm, gentle feeling of a Hallmark movie. Early on a quiet weekday morning inside an inviting coffee house in Asheville, North Carolina. Through a large window, soft fog drifts over the rolling Blue Ridge Mountains as golden morning sunlight streams into the room. Close-up of a maple oat latte in a ceramic mug on a wooden table, steam gently rising, a delicate leaf drawn in the creamy foam. An older gentleman with gray hair relaxes in a big, overstuffed armchair, reading a newspaper and sipping coffee with a contented smile. Nearby, a young woman works on her laptop in a comfortable chair beside a crackling stone fireplace, a warm mug at her side. Slow, smooth camera movements, soft focus, warm golden and amber tones, peaceful and unhurried atmosphere. The final shot is a calm, wide view of the cozy room with open space for text to be added later. No words or text in the video.\n\n---\n\n## Shot-by-Shot Version\n\nMany video programs only make clips of 5 to 10 seconds. If yours does, you can make each shot separately and join them together:\n\n1. **(0–3 sec)** Fog drifting over the Blue Ridge Mountains, seen through a coffee shop window, with warm golden morning light coming in.\n2. **(3–6 sec)** Close-up of a maple oat latte with a leaf drawn in the foam, steam slowly rising, on a wooden table in soft sunlight.\n3. **(6–9 sec)** An older gray-haired gentleman in a big comfortable armchair, reading a newspaper and sipping coffee, smiling peacefully.\n4. **(9–12 sec)** A young woman working on her laptop in a cozy chair beside a crackling stone fireplace, a warm mug beside her.\n5. **(12–15 sec)** A wide, gentle view of the warm, inviting coffee shop interior, leaving room for your name and message.\n\n---\n\n## A Few Helpful Tips\n\n**Add your shop name and message yourself.** AI video programs often misspell words or make letters look jumbled. It's better to add the text afterward using a free app like **Canva** or **CapCut**, or the text tool built into Instagram and Facebook. For the ending, I'd suggest:\n\n> **The Copper Kettle Coffee House**\n> Try our new Maple Oat Latte\n> Free refills on drip coffee until 10 a.m.\n\n**Choose a tall (vertical) video.** Look for a setting called \"9:16\" or \"vertical.\" That shape works best for Instagram Reels and Facebook.\n\n**Try it a few times.** Each attempt comes out a little differently, so make several and pick your favorite. Look closely at hands and faces, since AI sometimes makes these look a bit odd.\n\n**Add gentle music.** Soft acoustic guitar or piano would suit the feeling you're after. Instagram and Facebook both have free music you can add when you post.\n\n**Consider using your own photos.** Some programs let you upload a picture to start from. If you have a nice photo of your shop's window, chairs, or fireplace, the video will look more like the real Copper Kettle, and your customers will recognize the place when they walk in.\n\n**A small idea:** you might ask for a *maple* leaf in the foam instead of a regular leaf. It would tie in nicely with the maple oat latte.\n\n---\n\n## A Caption for Your Post\n\n> Slow mornings are better at The Copper Kettle ☕🍁 Come try our new Maple Oat Latte, settle into a big comfy chair, and enjoy free refills on drip coffee until 10 a.m. We'll save you a seat by the fire.\n\n---\n\nI hope this helps bring in some new morning regulars. If the video doesn't come out quite right, just tell me what looked off and I'll help you adjust the instructions.\n\nWarmly, and best wishes to you and your husband.", "prompt": "A 15-second cozy, cinematic advertisement for a small-town coffee shop, with the warm, gentle feeling of a Hallmark movie. Early on a quiet weekday morning inside an inviting coffee house in Asheville, North Carolina. Through a large window, soft fog drifts over the rolling Blue Ridge Mountains as golden morning sunlight streams into the room. Close-up of a maple oat latte in a ceramic mug on a wooden table, steam gently rising, a delicate leaf drawn in the creamy foam. An older gentleman with gray hair relaxes in a big, overstuffed armchair, reading a newspaper and sipping coffee with a contented smile. Nearby, a young woman works on her laptop in a comfortable chair beside a crackling stone fireplace, a warm mug at her side. Slow, smooth camera movements, soft focus, warm golden and amber tones, peaceful and unhurried atmosphere. The final shot is a calm, wide view of the cozy room with open space for text to be added later. No words or text in the video.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033405_8a62a821-421f-4b39-b9ce-5a58042e0c9d.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033406_51c08596-6a60-4b93-8b5a-36aaa75a1aca.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033406_a1876ddd-7f1c-465c-8c64-daeaee8cdfad.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033407_553502b7-cb9a-4bde-bc1e-ee3a6e786605.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033409_2e6ea3ea-9638-43ce-b3b8-7b590179deea.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033410_004c5f51-d333-4d3f-b6b3-8e093156d75d.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-02-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "03", "title": "Сыворотка Dewvale (плейсхолдер вместо флакона)", "total": "6,8", "scores": ["7", "7", "5", "8", "7"], "task": "Need a video prompt for an AI generator. Details:\n\n- Product: Dewvale Night Repair Serum (our brand, small DTC skincare startup, I do the marketing)\n- Length: ~15 seconds\n- Where: Instagram Reels + TikTok, so vertical\n- Audience: women 28-40 who already have a skincare routine and are sick of products that promise everything\n- What it has to sell: wake up with skin that looks rested. Main ingredient is a squalane + peptide blend, fragrance free, $38\n- Look: clean, soft, lots of white and pale green, glass dropper bottle catching morning light, close-ups of a single drop sliding down, a woman (no makeup, real skin texture, not airbrushed) putting it on before bed and then the same woman waking up and touching her cheek\n- Vibe reference: those quiet Apple product videos, very minimal, nothing flashy\n- End: bottle on a bathroom shelf, text \"Dewvale. Sleep is the step.\" \n- Avoid: fake before/after, glowing CGI skin, sparkles", "answer": "# Dewvale Night Repair Serum: 15s Vertical Video Prompt\n\n[Служебно: в генерацию идёт Main Prompt + блок Optional Audio — модель сама сказала добавлять его для генераторов со звуком.]\n\n## Main Prompt\n\nPaste the whole thing into tools that support 15s clips, or split it by shot (see notes below).\n\n```\nVertical 9:16, 15-second minimalist skincare film in the style of a quiet Apple product video. Calm, unhurried pacing. Slow, deliberate camera movement. Generous negative space. Shallow depth of field. Soft natural light. Color palette: clean whites, pale sage green, soft neutrals. Photorealistic, subtle film grain, true-to-life skin.\n\nSHOT 1 (0–3s): Extreme macro close-up of a glass dropper above [describe your bottle, e.g., \"a frosted glass bottle with a white cap\"]. A single drop of clear, slightly viscous serum forms at the tip of the dropper and slowly slides down the glass. Soft diffused light, white background, delicate highlights on the glass.\n\nSHOT 2 (3–7s): Night. A softly lit white bathroom with one warm lamp. A woman in her early 30s with a bare face, no makeup, and natural skin texture: visible pores, slight unevenness, real skin. Hair loosely pulled back, simple oatmeal-colored t-shirt. She slowly presses a few drops of serum into her cheek with her fingertips, eyes half closed, unhurried. Static medium close-up.\n\nSHOT 3 (7–11s): Morning. Cool, soft daylight through sheer white curtains. The same woman wakes in a bed with white linen sheets and a pale green throw, lifts her head from the pillow, and gently touches her cheek with her fingertips. A small, private smile. Her skin has the same natural texture as the night before, simply looking rested. Slow push-in to close-up.\n\nSHOT 4 (11–15s): The serum bottle sits alone on a white bathroom shelf. Morning sunlight from a window catches the glass and casts a soft refraction on the wall. A sprig of eucalyptus is softly out of focus in the background. Static locked-off shot with empty space in the upper-middle of the frame.\n```\n\n## Negative Prompt\n\n```\nsparkles, glitter, shimmer, glowing skin, CGI glow, airbrushed skin, plastic skin, poreless skin, heavy makeup, before-and-after split screen, dramatic transformation, lens flares, fast cuts, flashy transitions, saturated colors, neon, on-screen text, distorted text, logos, distorted hands, extra fingers\n```\n\n## Optional Audio (for Veo 3 or other tools that generate sound)\n\n```\nNear-silent ambient room tone. Faint, sparse piano. Soft rustle of linen sheets in shot 3. No voiceover.\n```\n\n## Production Notes\n\n**1. Add all text in your editor, not the generator.** AI tools usually garble on-screen text. Add \"Dewvale. Sleep is the step.\" in a thin sans-serif during the edit. Keep it in the upper-middle of the frame, because TikTok and Reels cover the bottom ~20% and the right edge with UI.\n\n**2. Use your real bottle as an image reference.** Without one, the generator will invent a generic bottle. Upload a product photo as the start frame or image reference for shots 1 and 4.\n\n**3. Keep the woman consistent across shots.** Most generators cap clips at 5–10 seconds, so you'll likely generate each shot separately and cut them together. Make one reference still of your actress first, then use it as the character reference for shots 2 and 3. Runway, Kling, and Veo all support this.\n\n**4. Add your selling points as text overlays.** The visuals alone can't communicate squalane + peptides, fragrance free, or $38. To keep the minimal feel:\n- Over shot 1, add a small, quiet line: *\"Squalane + peptides. Fragrance free.\"*\n- Put $38 in the caption, or in small type under the end line.\n\n**5. Check the morning shot closely.** Shot 3 is where generators tend to sneak in a glowy \"after\" look, even with the negative prompt. If her skin looks smoother or shinier than in shot 2, regenerate. The rested look should come from her expression and the light, not from altered skin.", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16, 15-second minimalist skincare film in the style of a quiet Apple product video. Calm, unhurried pacing. Slow, deliberate camera movement. Generous negative space. Shallow depth of field. Soft natural light. Color palette: clean whites, pale sage green, soft neutrals. Photorealistic, subtle film grain, true-to-life skin.\n\nSHOT 1 (0–3s): Extreme macro close-up of a glass dropper above [describe your bottle, e.g., \"a frosted glass bottle with a white cap\"]. A single drop of clear, slightly viscous serum forms at the tip of the dropper and slowly slides down the glass. Soft diffused light, white background, delicate highlights on the glass.\n\nSHOT 2 (3–7s): Night. A softly lit white bathroom with one warm lamp. A woman in her early 30s with a bare face, no makeup, and natural skin texture: visible pores, slight unevenness, real skin. Hair loosely pulled back, simple oatmeal-colored t-shirt. She slowly presses a few drops of serum into her cheek with her fingertips, eyes half closed, unhurried. Static medium close-up.\n\nSHOT 3 (7–11s): Morning. Cool, soft daylight through sheer white curtains. The same woman wakes in a bed with white linen sheets and a pale green throw, lifts her head from the pillow, and gently touches her cheek with her fingertips. A small, private smile. Her skin has the same natural texture as the night before, simply looking rested. Slow push-in to close-up.\n\nSHOT 4 (11–15s): The serum bottle sits alone on a white bathroom shelf. Morning sunlight from a window catches the glass and casts a soft refraction on the wall. A sprig of eucalyptus is softly out of focus in the background. Static locked-off shot with empty space in the upper-middle of the frame.\n\nNear-silent ambient room tone. Faint, sparse piano. Soft rustle of linen sheets in shot 3. No voiceover.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": ["Apple"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033457_56edd8de-35a1-4dd3-86b5-d510a1d38bc8.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033458_dce3aff1-f364-4610-94b4-2413e8e0fd8b.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033458_502d1af8-c628-4658-9cb7-137fda72c078.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033459_64b40fbb-536b-4bec-a836-c9b63f641e2f.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033500_46d6fe62-0fc5-4c6f-b056-5e6ae33a836a.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033500_4ad7adcb-1b3c-404d-b333-4d3b6085a33f.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-03-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}, {"n": "04", "title": "Мобильная игра Pocket Kraken, pre-roll 16:9", "total": "6,8", "scores": ["8", "7", "6", "6", "7"], "task": "ok so um I'm doing this through voice so sorry if it's messy, basically me and my buddy made a mobile game, it's called Pocket Kraken, it's like a puzzle game where you're this little cartoon octopus and you slide tiles around to rescue fish from a sunken ship, and we want to run ads on YouTube before videos, like a pre-roll thing, and we need a prompt for an AI video generator to make like a fifteen second ad. And the thing is every mobile game ad looks the same, it's always that fake \"only 1% can solve this\" thing, and we kind of want to make fun of that a little, like it starts looking like one of those cheesy ads and then the octopus like reaches out of the phone screen and slaps it away, you know, and then it's actual gameplay looking stuff, colorful, bright, kind of Pixar-ish, bubbles, the kraken grabbing fish with all eight arms, and at the end the title Pocket Kraken and \"free on iPhone and Android.\" Who it's for is like casual players, teens up to like thirty-five, people who play on the bus. Main thing we're selling is that it's free and it's actually fun and not a scam ad. Yeah. That's it I think.", "answer": "Here's a prompt you can paste straight in, plus a few tips.\n\n---\n\n**Prompt:**\n\n> 15-second video ad, 16:9, bright and playful, ending in Pixar-style 3D animation.\n> \n> **0–4s:** Close-up of a smartphone held in someone's hand on a city bus. The screen plays a cheesy, low-budget mobile game ad: flashing red text \"ONLY 1% CAN SOLVE THIS!\", a clumsy cartoon character failing an obviously easy puzzle, garish colors, blinking arrows, cheap and tacky. Tinny, annoying jingle.\n> \n> **4–6s:** A cute cartoon octopus tentacle bursts out of the phone screen and slaps the cheesy ad away. The fake ad crumples like paper and flies out of frame. Loud comedic slap sound and record scratch. The camera dives into the phone screen.\n> \n> **6–13s:** A vibrant Pixar-style underwater world: a sunken wooden ship, glowing sunlight rays, drifting bubbles, colorful coral. A small, round, purple cartoon octopus with big expressive eyes slides glowing colored tiles around a puzzle grid on the ship's hull. Each correct move pops open a hatch and frees a trapped cartoon fish. The octopus catches the happy fish with all eight arms at once. Smooth, satisfying motion. Upbeat bubbly music, bubble pops, cheerful fish squeaks.\n> \n> **13–15s:** The octopus pops up proudly, arms full of fish, and winks at the camera. Clean background space at the bottom for a title card. Music hits a final cheerful note.\n\n---\n\n**Tips:**\n\n1. **Land the slap before 5 seconds.** That's when viewers can hit Skip on YouTube, so the joke needs to happen right before then. The timeline above is built for that.\n\n2. **Add the text yourself in editing.** AI video tools mangle words, so \"Pocket Kraken\" and \"Free on iPhone and Android\" will probably come out as gibberish. Generate the video with empty space at the end, then put your real logo and tagline on top in CapCut, Premiere, or whatever you use. Do the same for the \"Only 1% can solve this\" text if it comes out garbled.\n\n3. **If your tool only makes short clips** (a lot cap at 5–10 seconds), paste each timecoded section as its own prompt and stitch them together. Add the line \"bright Pixar-style 3D animation, small round purple octopus with big expressive eyes\" to every shot so the style and character stay consistent.\n\n4. **Use a reference image of your actual octopus.** Most tools have an image-to-video option. Without it, the AI will invent its own octopus that won't match your game. Change \"purple\" in the prompt to whatever your character actually looks like.\n\n5. **Consider using real gameplay for the middle part.** Your whole pitch is \"this isn't a scam ad,\" so if the AI invents gameplay that doesn't match the actual game, you're doing the thing you're making fun of. Cutting in a few seconds of screen-recorded gameplay keeps it honest, avoids bad reviews from people who feel tricked, and keeps you clear of ad platforms' misleading-ad rules. You can keep the AI footage for the fake ad and the slap and switch to real footage after the dive into the phone.\n\nIf you tell me which generator you're using (Sora, Veo, Runway, Kling, etc.), I can adjust the prompt for its quirks.", "prompt": "15-second video ad, 16:9, bright and playful, ending in Pixar-style 3D animation.\n\n**0–4s:** Close-up of a smartphone held in someone's hand on a city bus. The screen plays a cheesy, low-budget mobile game ad: flashing red text \"ONLY 1% CAN SOLVE THIS!\", a clumsy cartoon character failing an obviously easy puzzle, garish colors, blinking arrows, cheap and tacky. Tinny, annoying jingle.\n\n**4–6s:** A cute cartoon octopus tentacle bursts out of the phone screen and slaps the cheesy ad away. The fake ad crumples like paper and flies out of frame. Loud comedic slap sound and record scratch. The camera dives into the phone screen.\n\n**6–13s:** A vibrant Pixar-style underwater world: a sunken wooden ship, glowing sunlight rays, drifting bubbles, colorful coral. A small, round, purple cartoon octopus with big expressive eyes slides glowing colored tiles around a puzzle grid on the ship's hull. Each correct move pops open a hatch and frees a trapped cartoon fish. The octopus catches the happy fish with all eight arms at once. Smooth, satisfying motion. Upbeat bubbly music, bubble pops, cheerful fish squeaks.\n\n**13–15s:** The octopus pops up proudly, arms full of fish, and winks at the camera. Clean background space at the bottom for a title card. Music hits a final cheerful note.", "aspect": "16:9", "dur": 15, "ip": ["Pixar"], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033550_a4fe4f20-3ad0-4dbb-b116-4e180f02baa6.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-04-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 3, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 4, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 5, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}, {"n": 6, "status": "ip_detected", "url": "", "poster": ""}], "clean": null}, {"n": "05", "title": "Выездной детейлинг Mirror Finish, 9:16", "total": "5,2", "scores": ["7", "5", "5", "4", "5"], "task": "need ai video promt for my detailing biz. Mirror Finish Mobile Detail, phoenix az, we come to ur house. 15 sec ad for instagram stories so vertical. show a dusty filthy black pickup in a driveway in the desert sun, then my guy foaming it, pressure wash, ceramic coat, wipe and its so shiny u can see the sky and palm trees in the hood. kinda fast cuts like a fast and furious garage scene. want guys 25-55 who love there trucks but dont got time. sell: we come to you, done in 2 hrs, $149 full detail. end w/ logo + \"book online\"", "answer": "# Mirror Finish Mobile Detail: 15s IG Story Ad\n\n## Option 1: All-in-One Prompt\n*(For tools that do 10-15s clips, like Sora or Veo)*\n\n> Vertical 9:16 cinematic commercial, 15 seconds, fast-paced high-energy editing with quick cuts, speed ramps, and whip pans like a street-racing movie garage montage. Opens on a filthy, dust-covered black pickup truck parked in a suburban Phoenix Arizona driveway, harsh bright desert sun, desert landscaping with gravel, cactus, and palm trees, heat shimmer in the air. A professional mobile detailer in a black polo shirt blasts the truck with thick white foam from a foam cannon, shown in slow motion. Quick cut to a pressure washer rinsing the foam off in sheets, water droplets sparkling in sunlight. Close-up of the detailer applying ceramic coating with an applicator pad, then wiping with a microfiber towel to reveal deep glossy black paint. Final hero shot: slow low-angle push-in on the truck's hood, now a flawless mirror finish clearly reflecting blue sky and palm trees. High contrast, rich blacks, warm sunlight, teal and orange color grade, anamorphic lens flares, macro detail shots, ultra-realistic, 4K commercial quality.\n\n## Option 2: Shot-by-Shot Prompts\n*(Better results. Generate each clip separately and cut them together in CapCut.)*\n\n**Shot 1 (0-2s): The hook**\n> Vertical 9:16, dirty dust-covered black pickup truck in a Phoenix Arizona driveway, harsh midday desert sun, heat haze, gravel yard with cactus and palm trees, slow dramatic push-in, cinematic, high contrast\n\n**Shot 2 (2-3s): We come to you**\n> Vertical 9:16, a professional mobile detailer in a black polo steps out of a work van parked at the curb of a suburban desert home, low angle, confident walk toward camera, bright sun, cinematic commercial\n\n**Shot 3 (3-6s): Foam**\n> Vertical 9:16, slow motion, foam cannon spraying thick white snow foam onto a dirty black pickup truck, foam covering the paint, sunlight backlighting the spray, dramatic action shot, macro detail\n\n**Shot 4 (6-8s): Rinse**\n> Vertical 9:16, pressure washer rinsing white foam off black truck paint in sheets, water droplets sparkling in sunlight, speed ramp from fast to slow motion, cinematic\n\n**Shot 5 (8-10s): Ceramic and wipe**\n> Vertical 9:16, close-up of gloved hand applying ceramic coating to black truck paint with an applicator pad, then microfiber towel wipe reveals ultra-glossy deep black finish, macro shot, satisfying reveal\n\n**Shot 6 (10-13s): The money shot**\n> Vertical 9:16, low-angle slow push-in across the hood of a gleaming black pickup truck, flawless mirror-finish paint perfectly reflecting a blue sky and tall palm trees, bright Arizona sun, lens flare, ultra-realistic, luxury car commercial\n\n**Shot 7 (13-15s): End card**\nMake this in CapCut or Canva using your real logo. AI will mess it up.\n\n## Text Overlays (add in editor)\n\n| Time | Text |\n|---|---|\n| 0-2s | **NO TIME TO WASH YOUR TRUCK?** |\n| 2-4s | **WE COME TO YOU** |\n| 5-9s | **DONE IN 2 HRS** |\n| 10-13s | **$149 FULL DETAIL** |\n| 13-15s | **[LOGO] + BOOK ONLINE 👆** |\n\nUse big bold white text with a black outline. Keep everything in the middle of the screen, since IG covers the top and bottom with buttons and your profile name.\n\n## Audio\n- **Music:** hard-hitting phonk or trap beat, around 140 BPM. Grab one from CapCut's or IG's commercial-safe library.\n- **SFX:** foam cannon hiss, pressure washer blast, microfiber squeak, a \"ding\" or shine sparkle on the hood shot.\n- Cut every clip on the beat. That's what gives it the Fast & Furious feel.\n\n## Tips\n- **Don't type \"Fast and Furious\" into the prompt.** Some tools block movie names. The style words above get you the same look.\n- **AI can't do text or logos well.** Always add those yourself.\n- **Run each shot 3-5 times** and keep the best one. AI trucks sometimes come out with weird wheels or melted badges.\n- **Check your offer wording.** If the $149 package uses a ceramic spray sealant rather than a full ceramic coating, call it that in the ad so customers don't feel misled.\n- **Make a version with your real footage too.** Even one real clip of your guy working builds trust. A mix of real and AI footage usually performs best.\n\nWant me to write a quick voiceover script or a caption to go with it?", "prompt": "Vertical 9:16 cinematic commercial, 15 seconds, fast-paced high-energy editing with quick cuts, speed ramps, and whip pans like a street-racing movie garage montage. Opens on a filthy, dust-covered black pickup truck parked in a suburban Phoenix Arizona driveway, harsh bright desert sun, desert landscaping with gravel, cactus, and palm trees, heat shimmer in the air. A professional mobile detailer in a black polo shirt blasts the truck with thick white foam from a foam cannon, shown in slow motion. Quick cut to a pressure washer rinsing the foam off in sheets, water droplets sparkling in sunlight. Close-up of the detailer applying ceramic coating with an applicator pad, then wiping with a microfiber towel to reveal deep glossy black paint. Final hero shot: slow low-angle push-in on the truck's hood, now a flawless mirror finish clearly reflecting blue sky and palm trees. High contrast, rich blacks, warm sunlight, teal and orange color grade, anamorphic lens flares, macro detail shots, ultra-realistic, 4K commercial quality.", "aspect": "9:16", "dur": 15, "ip": [], "takes": [{"n": 1, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033647_f3fd482e-04c0-409c-b551-11ad85147c56.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-1.jpg"}, {"n": 2, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033648_c57f236d-5b41-4417-ba9d-900e25870674.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-2.jpg"}, {"n": 3, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033649_cf76239a-1c6b-4628-ae39-918022410353.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-3.jpg"}, {"n": 4, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033649_d7cbb63d-f8d7-4fdf-ba17-1cb6889fd3d7.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-4.jpg"}, {"n": 5, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033650_2133ebd0-8332-42e6-b3d9-1e05d8c97ae2.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-5.jpg"}, {"n": 6, "status": "completed", "url": "https://d8j0ntlcm91z4.cloudfront.net/user_3I3HmEWqlqt7Yj4qFjPPgcXyV6R/hf_20261025_033651_030b1d69-ebc6-4043-a76c-26e5c3114454.mp4", "poster": "posters/paid-ads-05-6.jpg"}], "clean": null}]}];
